1
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:16,683
The Chuseok holidays
are around the corner.

2
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:18,351
As we welcome Chuseok,

3
00:00:18,418 --> 00:00:22,255
the biggest holiday in our country,

4
00:00:22,322 --> 00:00:26,259
we've invited very special A-list guests
perfect for the occasion.

5
00:00:26,326 --> 00:00:27,560
Are they really A-listers?

6
00:00:29,195 --> 00:00:31,064
-Let's just get them here.
-I agree.

7
00:00:31,398 --> 00:00:32,632
THE GUESTS ARE ODDLY UNWELCOME

8
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:33,967
I want to meet them already.

9
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:36,336
-What's with all these complaints?
-I get it.

10
00:00:36,403 --> 00:00:38,204
-Well, I'd do the same.
-Exactly.

11
00:00:38,271 --> 00:00:40,473
<i>Chef & My Fridge,</i> the Chuseok special.

12
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:43,543
Please welcome today's fridge owners.

13
00:00:43,610 --> 00:00:45,412
WE PRESENT THE FRIDGE OWNERS

14
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:46,813
EXCITED

15
00:00:48,281 --> 00:00:50,316
TA-DA

16
00:00:50,517 --> 00:00:52,385
LOOKING SO COOL

17
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:53,820
SHOOTING POISON DARTS

18
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:56,756
Today's fridge owners
are Chef Kwon Sung-jun and Yoon Nam-no!

19
00:00:56,823 --> 00:00:58,358
Welcome to the show.

20
00:00:58,858 --> 00:00:59,726
Hello.

21
00:00:59,793 --> 00:01:00,693
SWAGGER

22
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:02,629
-They're already smug.
-Take a seat.

23
00:01:02,695 --> 00:01:05,031
-Welcome.
-He wore that to my wedding.

24
00:01:05,098 --> 00:01:06,833
You're dressed like Bbo-sik today.

25
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,435
-Bbo-sik?
-Bbo-sik?

26
00:01:08,501 --> 00:01:09,903
-All right.
-Bbo-sik.

27
00:01:09,969 --> 00:01:11,237
Nice set.

28
00:01:11,304 --> 00:01:12,305
You're looking sharp.

29
00:01:12,372 --> 00:01:15,375
Excuse me. You're drinking that
as soon as you got here?

30
00:01:15,442 --> 00:01:16,509
-Promptly.
-A welcome drink.

31
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:18,578
Now, let me introduce this guest.

32
00:01:18,645 --> 00:01:21,347
<i>He got smug after coming up</i>
<i>with his own characters</i>

33
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:22,849
<i>-and buzzwords,</i>
-Miss.

34
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:25,919
…and then even rose up
to seize the guest's seat.

35
00:01:25,985 --> 00:01:27,387
Please welcome Chef Kwon Sung-jun.

36
00:01:29,622 --> 00:01:31,057
Hello.

37
00:01:31,124 --> 00:01:32,725
I'm Chef Kwon Sung-jun.

38
00:01:33,159 --> 00:01:34,461
A DIGNIFIED PRESENCE

39
00:01:34,527 --> 00:01:36,062
That's his character today.

40
00:01:36,129 --> 00:01:38,031
Something's shining on your wrist.

41
00:01:38,098 --> 00:01:39,632
Did you get that sponsored?

42
00:01:39,699 --> 00:01:40,900
No, my money, my purchase, sir.

43
00:01:40,967 --> 00:01:44,838
-"My money, my purchase, sir"?
-What's with the sir?

44
00:01:44,904 --> 00:01:47,073
-He should be polite.
-I mean, we've never met.

45
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:49,109
-Your watch is sparkly.
-What's your persona today?

46
00:01:49,175 --> 00:01:50,310
Today's persona

47
00:01:50,376 --> 00:01:52,745
is a male actor
who broke his hiatus after two years.

48
00:01:53,046 --> 00:01:54,447
DID HIS PART AND PREPARED A PERSONA

49
00:01:54,514 --> 00:01:56,382
You're good. You have my approval.

50
00:01:56,449 --> 00:01:58,885
-I came to promote my drama.
-Your drama?

51
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:00,787
As for our next guest,

52
00:02:00,854 --> 00:02:04,257
<i>he could never eat enough on the show,</i>
<i>so he decided to show up as a guest.</i>

53
00:02:04,324 --> 00:02:05,625
FINISHING FOOD IS HIS HOBBY

54
00:02:05,692 --> 00:02:07,560
The professional foodie of the show,

55
00:02:07,627 --> 00:02:09,329
Chef Yoon Nam-no!

56
00:02:10,597 --> 00:02:12,065
WELCOME

57
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:14,501
Hello, I'm…

58
00:02:15,568 --> 00:02:16,569
Let me do that again.

59
00:02:17,103 --> 00:02:18,605
Wait, are you nervous?

60
00:02:18,671 --> 00:02:20,039
-Are you?
-He's nervous.

61
00:02:20,106 --> 00:02:21,941
He can't piece together
more than three words.

62
00:02:22,008 --> 00:02:23,776
It's so awkward to sit here.

63
00:02:23,843 --> 00:02:26,079
I'm Yoon Nam-no,
the diner-base of the show.

64
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:27,380
-Hey.
-Database?

65
00:02:27,447 --> 00:02:29,015
-"Diner-base."
-"Diner."

66
00:02:29,082 --> 00:02:30,450
Why is no one cheering?

67
00:02:30,817 --> 00:02:32,318
OH, RIGHT

68
00:02:32,619 --> 00:02:35,088
GREATLY WELCOME

69
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:37,957
-We had the President here last Chuseok.
-We did.

70
00:02:38,024 --> 00:02:40,493
So was it that hard
to find a special guest?

71
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:42,295
-I mean…
-Tell me about it.

72
00:02:42,362 --> 00:02:44,764
-I'd like to clear this with the viewers.
-What?

73
00:02:44,831 --> 00:02:46,199
It's not that our original guests bailed.

74
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:47,967
WE REALLY MEANT TO INVITE THESE TWO

75
00:02:48,034 --> 00:02:50,236
I'm now 55 years old, right?

76
00:02:50,303 --> 00:02:52,138
I've lived far too long.

77
00:02:52,205 --> 00:02:53,239
What is this nonsense?

78
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:55,341
AN ODD SIGHT EVEN FOR THE GRANDPA

79
00:02:55,408 --> 00:02:57,610
But honestly, in our previous episode,

80
00:02:57,677 --> 00:02:59,479
we had invited a great actor.

81
00:02:59,546 --> 00:03:02,815
Naturally, I thought we'd have
someone really huge for Chuseok,

82
00:03:02,882 --> 00:03:04,350
so I thought we couldn't get anyone.

83
00:03:04,417 --> 00:03:06,719
He must've thought,
"We've become a cottage industry."

84
00:03:06,786 --> 00:03:07,921
I was quite worried.

85
00:03:07,987 --> 00:03:09,789
Can you just tell us
instead of beating around the bush?

86
00:03:10,356 --> 00:03:11,291
It's a massive step down.

87
00:03:11,624 --> 00:03:13,493
A CANDID TAKE

88
00:03:13,726 --> 00:03:15,061
TOTALLY PLEASED

89
00:03:15,361 --> 00:03:16,796
THE GREAT GUESTS IN A CRISIS

90
00:03:16,863 --> 00:03:18,498
It's much nicer to throw it out there.

91
00:03:18,565 --> 00:03:20,233
But it's true.

92
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,869
We should've gone through
Sam and Ho-young's fridge first.

93
00:03:22,936 --> 00:03:25,605
-They're older too.
-And they're the OG members.

94
00:03:25,672 --> 00:03:26,973
Even if it were us,

95
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,107
it would've still been a big step down.

96
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:31,444
He's so self-aware too.

97
00:03:31,511 --> 00:03:34,280
Even Chef Eun-yeong
was also utterly appalled.

98
00:03:34,347 --> 00:03:35,415
-That much?
-Yes.

99
00:03:35,481 --> 00:03:37,650
-Those Grubby Twins.
-"Grubby Twins"?

100
00:03:37,717 --> 00:03:40,620
-It's Tubby Twins.
-Grubby Twins?

101
00:03:40,687 --> 00:03:43,056
I was a bit distressed on my way here.

102
00:03:43,957 --> 00:03:46,259
I knew Sung-jun
would be smug the whole time,

103
00:03:46,326 --> 00:03:48,795
and Nam-no would
let himself go and start devouring.

104
00:03:49,095 --> 00:03:50,697
OF COURSE

105
00:03:50,763 --> 00:03:53,166
What do you two think about this topic?

106
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:56,035
I'm someone who's considered an analyst.

107
00:03:56,102 --> 00:03:57,804
I predict about 3.8%.

108
00:03:57,870 --> 00:03:59,372
-What? The ratings?
-The ratings.

109
00:03:59,572 --> 00:04:01,074
OOZING WITH CONFIDENCE

110
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:02,475
Make a pledge.

111
00:04:02,542 --> 00:04:03,409
-A pledge?
-Yes.

112
00:04:03,476 --> 00:04:04,744
What would you do?

113
00:04:04,811 --> 00:04:05,778
Shaving your head?

114
00:04:05,845 --> 00:04:07,480
-Then it'll go up.
-That's a good one.

115
00:04:07,547 --> 00:04:09,148
Shave your head, and it'll reach 3.8%.

116
00:04:09,215 --> 00:04:10,550
That's not a bad idea.

117
00:04:10,617 --> 00:04:11,918
Shaving my head isn't a bad idea?

118
00:04:11,985 --> 00:04:13,686
You two can be Tubby High Beams.

119
00:04:13,753 --> 00:04:16,222
TUBBY HIGH BEAMS

120
00:04:16,789 --> 00:04:17,790
-Shave it off?
-Shave it off.

121
00:04:17,857 --> 00:04:18,791
Are you in?

122
00:04:18,858 --> 00:04:20,193
-So you're in, right?
-Do it.

123
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:21,561
I'm not doing it.

124
00:04:21,628 --> 00:04:23,896
Don't back out.
I'll shave my head if we do.

125
00:04:25,031 --> 00:04:26,332
-Hey!
-That's the spirit!

126
00:04:26,599 --> 00:04:27,934
THE ACTOR GETS ANXIOUS…

127
00:04:28,001 --> 00:04:29,836
That's so cool, Nam-no.

128
00:04:29,902 --> 00:04:31,237
Should we do it together?

129
00:04:31,304 --> 00:04:33,606
We're one. We're the Tubby Twins.

130
00:04:33,906 --> 00:04:35,375
WHAT WILL HAPPEN TO THEIR HAIR?

131
00:04:35,441 --> 00:04:38,845
-Sung-jun asked us to ask him this one.
-He did?

132
00:04:38,911 --> 00:04:41,080
-He prepared the questions?
-He had a list.

133
00:04:41,147 --> 00:04:42,548
He came up with his own questions?

134
00:04:42,615 --> 00:04:44,617
I have no idea
why you want me to ask you this.

135
00:04:44,684 --> 00:04:46,252
"Chef Kwon Sung-jun,

136
00:04:46,319 --> 00:04:49,355
-you recently had a health checkup."
-A health checkup?

137
00:04:49,422 --> 00:04:50,923
Do we have to know this?

138
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:54,193
I recently got my first
gastroscopy and colonoscopy,

139
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:56,562
and the doctor was quite surprised.

140
00:04:56,629 --> 00:04:58,031
-Why?
-At my stomach and colon.

141
00:04:58,097 --> 00:04:59,098
Are they rotting?

142
00:04:59,932 --> 00:05:00,767
Rotting?

143
00:05:00,833 --> 00:05:02,635
-Has it gone bad?
-Here it is word-for-word.

144
00:05:02,702 --> 00:05:05,538
"Your stomach and colon
are like those of a teenager."

145
00:05:05,605 --> 00:05:08,608
-I see.
-"I've never seen them so light pink."

146
00:05:08,675 --> 00:05:10,209
I see. You must be healthy.

147
00:05:10,276 --> 00:05:12,011
-I have handsome organs.
-Handsome organs?

148
00:05:12,078 --> 00:05:14,614
-Word-for-word.
-Light pink.

149
00:05:14,681 --> 00:05:17,850
-Organs in good vibes?
-In good vibes.

150
00:05:17,917 --> 00:05:19,686
He still can't lose his <i>sujebi, </i>the dough.

151
00:05:19,752 --> 00:05:21,721
It's like a lump on his face.

152
00:05:21,788 --> 00:05:24,057
The young man with the <i>sujebi</i> lump.

153
00:05:24,123 --> 00:05:26,559
-Don't be hard on the guest.
-Wait.

154
00:05:26,626 --> 00:05:28,995
-They'll give out stars today.
-Yes.

155
00:05:29,062 --> 00:05:31,331
-You'd better get on their good side.
-Right.

156
00:05:31,397 --> 00:05:33,333
We never cook for stars.

157
00:05:34,734 --> 00:05:36,135
Aren't guests the stars?

158
00:05:36,202 --> 00:05:37,704
They are the stars.

159
00:05:37,770 --> 00:05:40,940
-Star or guest?
-Will you go for the star or the guest?

160
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,275
Today, I will

161
00:05:42,342 --> 00:05:43,376
boycott cooking.

162
00:05:45,445 --> 00:05:47,714
-There are two fridges.
-Yes.

163
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:50,883
But we'll have to wrap it all up
in just one episode.

164
00:05:50,950 --> 00:05:53,219
I'm the type who's really self-aware,

165
00:05:53,286 --> 00:05:55,421
and the two of us
only deserve one episode.

166
00:05:57,223 --> 00:05:58,991
-Excessive, even.
-I knew it, Sung-jun.

167
00:05:59,058 --> 00:06:01,394
-I'm glad.
-One episode is perfect.

168
00:06:01,961 --> 00:06:03,296
Anyway, so…

169
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:04,997
-Should we look at their fridges?
-Yes, we…

170
00:06:05,064 --> 00:06:06,999
-Already?
-Let's move on.

171
00:06:07,066 --> 00:06:08,267
-Don't be mean.
-Let's hurry.

172
00:06:08,334 --> 00:06:09,836
-Let's move on.
-Let's open their fridges.

173
00:06:09,902 --> 00:06:11,371
-Yes.
-We already know them.

174
00:06:11,437 --> 00:06:13,306
It's a bit too early for that.

175
00:06:13,373 --> 00:06:15,942
We've already chatted enough.
We have enough airtime already.

176
00:06:16,008 --> 00:06:18,311
It was so funny.
I've never heard of such a clean stomach.

177
00:06:18,378 --> 00:06:20,813
Is there anything more
you really want to mention?

178
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,815
-Any updates in your life?
-Let's just move on.

179
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:24,584
The crew will add a caption for you.

180
00:06:24,817 --> 00:06:26,819
THE TUBBY TWINS ARE DOING WELL

181
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:29,555
-Do it for the 3.8%.
-Do it for the show.

182
00:06:29,622 --> 00:06:30,957
-Right.
-I'm sure you have one.

183
00:06:31,023 --> 00:06:32,525
-I think so. He must have one.
-Yes.

184
00:06:32,592 --> 00:06:34,293
Why don't we chat
as we look at the fridge?

185
00:06:35,328 --> 00:06:36,529
SELF-AWARENESS IN ACTION

186
00:06:36,596 --> 00:06:39,399
Now, the two chefs, the Tubby Twins.

187
00:06:39,465 --> 00:06:41,267
-Wait, that's really it?
-Yes.

188
00:06:41,334 --> 00:06:42,635
THEIR FRIDGES ARE THE HIGHLIGHT

189
00:06:42,702 --> 00:06:45,104
Chef Nam-no, who's always hungry for food,

190
00:06:45,171 --> 00:06:47,106
and Chef Sung-jun,
who's always hungry for attention,

191
00:06:47,173 --> 00:06:49,409
-are about to share their fridges.
-Clout chaser.

192
00:06:49,475 --> 00:06:52,879
We'll first look through
Sung-jun's fridge.

193
00:06:52,945 --> 00:06:55,281
The key point of this Chuseok special

194
00:06:55,348 --> 00:06:58,718
-is to find out what chefs actually eat.
-Of course.

195
00:06:58,785 --> 00:07:00,987
That's probably
what the viewers want to know.

196
00:07:01,053 --> 00:07:02,922
Is this actually your fridge?

197
00:07:02,989 --> 00:07:04,090
It's not from my home.

198
00:07:04,157 --> 00:07:06,292
I had more ingredients
in my test kitchen, so it's from there.

199
00:07:06,359 --> 00:07:08,995
-Don't you have one at home?
-I do have a fridge.

200
00:07:09,061 --> 00:07:10,363
But I only keep beverages there.

201
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:12,732
You should've brought that
instead of the one from your restaurant.

202
00:07:12,799 --> 00:07:14,634
It's not from my restaurant.
It's from my test kitchen.

203
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:17,203
-Test kitchen?
-I'm mostly at my test kitchen.

204
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,638
All I do at home is sleep.

205
00:07:18,704 --> 00:07:20,673
Do other chefs
also have a studio or a test kitchen?

206
00:07:22,241 --> 00:07:23,443
I do.

207
00:07:23,509 --> 00:07:24,577
You?

208
00:07:24,644 --> 00:07:25,912
-I do.
-He does?

209
00:07:26,412 --> 00:07:28,881
AN UNLIKELY OWNER OF A STUDIO

210
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:31,684
-Wait, for cooking or webtoon?
-To do what?

211
00:07:31,751 --> 00:07:33,886
I do both.

212
00:07:33,953 --> 00:07:35,221
I also test recipes.

213
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:36,689
Am I not allowed to have one?

214
00:07:36,756 --> 00:07:38,291
I have to try even harder than most!

215
00:07:38,357 --> 00:07:40,560
All right, then.

216
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:43,629
The winner of <i>Culinary Class Wars 1,</i>

217
00:07:43,696 --> 00:07:46,132
Chef Kwon Sung-jun,
brought his test kitchen fridge.

218
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:47,233
-Let's open it!
-Let's open it!

219
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:48,367
-Let's open it!
-Let's open it!

220
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:51,337
CURIOUS

221
00:07:51,404 --> 00:07:52,672
-Let's open it!
-Let's open it!

222
00:07:52,738 --> 00:07:55,074
-He has lots of stuff.
-I see.

223
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:56,976
-You have more than I expected.
-It's not so bad.

224
00:07:57,043 --> 00:07:59,178
Yes, a lot more than what I thought.

225
00:07:59,245 --> 00:08:00,746
Let's start from the top.

226
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:02,748
What's this? Oh.

227
00:08:02,815 --> 00:08:04,450
-Chicken breast.
-Huh?

228
00:08:04,517 --> 00:08:06,152
That's my staple diet.

229
00:08:06,219 --> 00:08:07,987
-What?
-Your staple diet?

230
00:08:08,054 --> 00:08:08,888
For your cats?

231
00:08:08,955 --> 00:08:10,556
No, it really is mine.

232
00:08:10,623 --> 00:08:12,391
Sure.

233
00:08:12,458 --> 00:08:14,193
These are all lies.

234
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:16,162
He's already losing credibility.

235
00:08:16,229 --> 00:08:17,897
He and I have the same routine.

236
00:08:17,964 --> 00:08:19,465
<i>We start with a loaded toast</i>

237
00:08:19,532 --> 00:08:21,467
<i>and even eat our meal boxes</i>
<i>with a side of </i>ramyeon.

238
00:08:21,534 --> 00:08:24,003
We always ate the same way,
so what's he saying now?

239
00:08:24,070 --> 00:08:25,905
-Is this an act?
-The thing is,

240
00:08:25,972 --> 00:08:29,775
I do eat a little more when I shoot
like it's my cheat day.

241
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:32,845
But I usually only eat chicken breast
and rice for breakfast and dinner.

242
00:08:32,912 --> 00:08:34,714
COLD STARE

243
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:35,982
I'm serious.

244
00:08:36,048 --> 00:08:38,017
-Sure.
-That's too much.

245
00:08:38,084 --> 00:08:40,152
-Must you go that far?
-We all know you.

246
00:08:40,219 --> 00:08:42,021
Kids these days would say this about him.

247
00:08:42,088 --> 00:08:43,789
A self-proclaimed dieter.

248
00:08:44,790 --> 00:08:47,426
-I'm serious. It's my staple diet.
-It is?

249
00:08:47,493 --> 00:08:49,295
-Breakfast and dinner?
-Breakfast and dinner?

250
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:50,930
You'll see farro rice over there.

251
00:08:50,997 --> 00:08:51,831
Farro?

252
00:08:51,898 --> 00:08:54,367
The same farro
that many celebrities eat these days?

253
00:08:54,433 --> 00:08:56,903
-Farro. It's here.
-Italian grains, right?

254
00:08:56,969 --> 00:08:58,738
Low-sugar farro and brown rice.

255
00:08:58,804 --> 00:09:00,673
-Grains?
-So this is what he eats.

256
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:02,575
I see the Italian flag here.

257
00:09:02,642 --> 00:09:06,579
It's one of the ancient Italian grains,
recently on the rise.

258
00:09:06,646 --> 00:09:09,248
-Because he's Napoli Matfia.
-Yes, I'm an Italian.

259
00:09:09,315 --> 00:09:10,383
It's good for weight loss.

260
00:09:10,449 --> 00:09:12,118
It is. There's also brown rice in there.

261
00:09:12,184 --> 00:09:14,554
-There's no white rice.
-I see.

262
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:17,256
-So…
-He should shed a few more pounds.

263
00:09:17,323 --> 00:09:19,759
He's talking like he's ripped.

264
00:09:20,826 --> 00:09:22,461
-It's not that.
-I get it.

265
00:09:22,528 --> 00:09:25,731
I was just listening,
and he talked as if he were Ahn Bo-hyun.

266
00:09:25,798 --> 00:09:27,833
You should've lost more
if you lived off these.

267
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,735
Yes, I can't believe
those are your staples.

268
00:09:29,802 --> 00:09:32,872
-He's talking like he's Namkoong Min.
-Wait.

269
00:09:32,939 --> 00:09:34,674
-You're…
-We've started in different places.

270
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:37,510
We always face each other,
so this is my first time

271
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:39,078
seeing him from the back.

272
00:09:39,145 --> 00:09:41,547
And from the back,
it's easier to notice his <i>sujebi.</i>

273
00:09:41,614 --> 00:09:42,748
Don't you think?

274
00:09:42,815 --> 00:09:45,718
THE DOUGH'S STICKING OUT

275
00:09:45,785 --> 00:09:47,320
When did you start this diet?

276
00:09:47,386 --> 00:09:49,989
It's been about six months now.

277
00:09:50,056 --> 00:09:52,224
-Six months?
-Is it not working?

278
00:09:52,491 --> 00:09:53,960
SEEMS IMPERCEPTIBLE

279
00:09:54,026 --> 00:09:57,463
-You still have this after six months?
-I still do have my <i>sujebi.</i>

280
00:09:57,530 --> 00:09:59,332
But I did lose about 10 kg.

281
00:09:59,398 --> 00:10:02,501
And how did I do that?
I slowly changed what I eat.

282
00:10:02,568 --> 00:10:04,937
So this is how he maintains his shape.

283
00:10:05,004 --> 00:10:07,573
-He even put a basket in here.
-Yes, that basket.

284
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:10,676
-Let's see what's inside.
-I'm dying to find out.

285
00:10:10,743 --> 00:10:12,712
CURIOUS

286
00:10:12,778 --> 00:10:14,380
That's called a <i>banneton</i>.

287
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:16,983
-A <i>banneton</i>.
-A proofing basket for bread?

288
00:10:17,049 --> 00:10:19,118
Are you fermenting this?

289
00:10:19,185 --> 00:10:21,387
-Yes, so you'll find a levain on the side.
-Levain?

290
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:24,123
-I've been growing that levain.
-Levain?

291
00:10:24,190 --> 00:10:25,658
I have to feed it now.

292
00:10:25,725 --> 00:10:27,293
You have to feed the levain?

293
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:29,028
It needs to be fed?

294
00:10:29,095 --> 00:10:31,497
You always have to feed the levain.

295
00:10:31,564 --> 00:10:34,200
It's used instead of yeast
to leaven the bread naturally.

296
00:10:34,266 --> 00:10:37,169
That's the bread I made with this.

297
00:10:37,236 --> 00:10:39,872
It's already fermented,
so I just have to bake it.

298
00:10:39,939 --> 00:10:41,941
I have to feed it, so let me do that.

299
00:10:42,008 --> 00:10:43,776
Will that grow once you feed it?

300
00:10:43,843 --> 00:10:45,911
It does, and you can make bread with it.

301
00:10:45,978 --> 00:10:49,315
-Is that flour?
-Flour and water.

302
00:10:49,382 --> 00:10:53,119
Then the enzymes in the grains
meet with the starter.

303
00:10:53,185 --> 00:10:54,253
Then it ferments.

304
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:56,088
A chef's pantry has different stuff.

305
00:10:56,155 --> 00:10:57,623
This is how I feed it every day.

306
00:10:57,690 --> 00:10:59,525
Why are you doing it here
and not in your kitchen?

307
00:11:00,459 --> 00:11:04,096
I've been making that bread
by myself for seven years now.

308
00:11:04,163 --> 00:11:06,999
He has to throw away
half of the levain before he does that.

309
00:11:07,066 --> 00:11:09,602
-I do.
-And then he can feed it.

310
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:10,636
He skipped that altogether.

311
00:11:10,703 --> 00:11:12,271
You have to throw it out, but…

312
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:13,906
-Wait.
-Is this right?

313
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:15,908
DID HE HAVE TO DO THIS HERE?

314
00:11:15,975 --> 00:11:18,310
Something's not adding up.

315
00:11:18,377 --> 00:11:21,714
I've known him for a long time,

316
00:11:21,781 --> 00:11:23,382
and I think it's staged.

317
00:11:24,517 --> 00:11:25,785
It's staged?

318
00:11:25,851 --> 00:11:28,087
STAGING EVERYTHING SO HE CAN LOOK COOL

319
00:11:28,154 --> 00:11:31,023
Was this staged?

320
00:11:31,090 --> 00:11:34,060
Anyway, we got to see this
because it's a chef's fridge.

321
00:11:34,126 --> 00:11:37,463
-We're starting off with many suspicions.
-This is why he won <i>CCW 1.</i>

322
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:39,298
Meat.

323
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:42,768
-This looks nice.
-Lamb chops.

324
00:11:42,835 --> 00:11:45,337
That's my favorite among red meat.

325
00:11:45,404 --> 00:11:47,540
-Really?
-I use it at my restaurant too.

326
00:11:47,606 --> 00:11:51,544
You bought that for your business,
then took some home.

327
00:11:51,610 --> 00:11:55,481
-Isn't that embezzlement?
-Was it for work?

328
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:58,718
I'm a private operator,
not a corporate body, so it's okay.

329
00:11:58,784 --> 00:12:01,053
-Well, then he's fine.
-I own the place 100%.

330
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:02,254
If I eat it, it's a staff meal.

331
00:12:02,321 --> 00:12:04,223
-A staff meal?
-Lamb chops.

332
00:12:04,290 --> 00:12:06,392
-What's this? venus clams.
-What's that?

333
00:12:06,459 --> 00:12:09,428
-Venus clams. Among food ingredients,
-Littleneck clams.

334
00:12:09,495 --> 00:12:13,199
…I eat clams and shellfish the most,
and I enjoy them a lot too.

335
00:12:13,265 --> 00:12:15,101
Those two are my favorites.

336
00:12:15,167 --> 00:12:16,402
I use them to make vongole pasta.

337
00:12:16,469 --> 00:12:18,003
Do you make that at home?

338
00:12:18,070 --> 00:12:20,072
-I do.
-I see.

339
00:12:20,139 --> 00:12:21,006
Even at home?

340
00:12:21,073 --> 00:12:22,475
This is too staged.

341
00:12:23,743 --> 00:12:25,878
Sam, do you make vongole pasta at home?

342
00:12:25,945 --> 00:12:27,980
Even if I did,
I wouldn't keep the clams like that.

343
00:12:28,981 --> 00:12:31,984
-You wouldn't?
-Then how would you do it?

344
00:12:32,051 --> 00:12:33,419
It looks too staged.

345
00:12:33,486 --> 00:12:34,787
Does it really?

346
00:12:34,854 --> 00:12:36,889
-What is it?
-I'm very suspicious.

347
00:12:36,956 --> 00:12:38,224
Let's move on.

348
00:12:38,290 --> 00:12:39,992
-It's what he does.
-Things are pretty rough.

349
00:12:40,059 --> 00:12:44,096
And next to the clams,
he laid out the cheese.

350
00:12:44,163 --> 00:12:45,898
-There aren't too many.
-Come on.

351
00:12:45,965 --> 00:12:48,134
It looks like
you're claiming to be an Italian.

352
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:49,668
That's what you want to show.

353
00:12:49,735 --> 00:12:50,970
A self-proclaimed Italian.

354
00:12:51,036 --> 00:12:53,639
-So he has cheese and anchovies.
-I didn't stage this.

355
00:12:53,706 --> 00:12:57,910
I mainly eat sandwiches,
pasta, and burgers.

356
00:12:57,977 --> 00:13:00,279
-Wait, what about chicken breast?
-Not chicken breast?

357
00:13:00,346 --> 00:13:02,181
What is going on?

358
00:13:02,248 --> 00:13:04,950
-You said it was chicken breast!
-I mean it. Sandwiches.

359
00:13:05,017 --> 00:13:07,953
-Other than chicken breast, I mean.
-You said you only eat chicken with rice.

360
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:11,557
Those are for breakfast and dinner,
so that must be lunch.

361
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:13,592
His facade will slowly crumble.

362
00:13:13,659 --> 00:13:16,228
I guess you do cook for yourself.
There's pasta.

363
00:13:16,295 --> 00:13:20,199
-I use those often.
-He has these noodles.

364
00:13:20,266 --> 00:13:23,102
It looks like he came with a theme, but…

365
00:13:23,169 --> 00:13:25,971
-What's this wrapped in tissue paper?
-Butter.

366
00:13:26,038 --> 00:13:30,442
Butter, but I got lazy
and rolled it up in a paper towel.

367
00:13:30,509 --> 00:13:33,045
-So chefs do this too?
-I'm not all that different from others.

368
00:13:33,112 --> 00:13:36,048
-Even that was staged.
-That was staged too?

369
00:13:36,115 --> 00:13:38,184
You staged the butter too?

370
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:40,486
He's staging his chill side too.

371
00:13:40,553 --> 00:13:43,489
-Everything else looks neat except this.
-To seem relatable.

372
00:13:43,556 --> 00:13:45,958
You really didn't set it up?
The paper towel?

373
00:13:46,025 --> 00:13:48,260
He threw in a little twist.

374
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:50,329
-This is way too staged.
-What is it?

375
00:13:50,396 --> 00:13:51,530
-What is it?
-This is…

376
00:13:51,597 --> 00:13:53,032
I can't do this.

377
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:56,936
-Why? What is it?
-What?

378
00:13:57,002 --> 00:13:59,505
-What is he?
-He's boycotting.

379
00:13:59,572 --> 00:14:01,140
I've done this show since 2014,

380
00:14:01,207 --> 00:14:03,209
and never once have I seen
anything like this.

381
00:14:03,275 --> 00:14:05,177
-What is it?
-I can't keep doing it like this.

382
00:14:05,244 --> 00:14:07,479
Hey, who keeps this in the fridge?

383
00:14:07,546 --> 00:14:10,583
-He's growing these.
-I mean, seriously?

384
00:14:10,983 --> 00:14:12,885
COME ON, WHAT IS THIS?

385
00:14:12,952 --> 00:14:14,787
WHY IS THAT IN HIS FRIDGE?

386
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:18,390
I'm not growing them.
Those are basil and lemon basil.

387
00:14:18,457 --> 00:14:21,227
You're making it look like
you're in a science lab.

388
00:14:21,293 --> 00:14:23,429
-I'm serious.
-I mean, in your fridge?

389
00:14:23,495 --> 00:14:25,497
They grow better at room temperature.

390
00:14:25,564 --> 00:14:26,565
-They do?
-Much better.

391
00:14:26,632 --> 00:14:28,834
-Yes, keep them outside.
-Of course.

392
00:14:28,901 --> 00:14:31,303
I'll keep them
at room temperature from now on.

393
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:34,473
-Put them as shelf-stable ingredients.
-Shelf-stable?

394
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:37,977
-I'll leave them outside.
-He's good.

395
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:40,880
-My gosh.
-They must've been freezing.

396
00:14:40,946 --> 00:14:43,015
-What? Wait.
-What is it?

397
00:14:43,082 --> 00:14:45,784
Sung-jun, I thought you didn't drink.

398
00:14:45,851 --> 00:14:47,853
-Is that soju?
-That's soju.

399
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,488
-I don't.
-What's that?

400
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:51,490
-Or is it us?
-No.

401
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:52,825
-What's that?
-I feel betrayed.

402
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:56,695
We've never seen him drinking
even at our team dinners.

403
00:14:56,762 --> 00:14:59,531
But he has a bottle of soju
at his test kitchen.

404
00:14:59,598 --> 00:15:01,934
Wait, he might be there
testing relationships with women.

405
00:15:02,001 --> 00:15:03,602
-I see.
-That's the test?

406
00:15:03,669 --> 00:15:06,305
When I have to go abroad
or be away for work,

407
00:15:06,372 --> 00:15:08,774
my younger sister comes to cat-sit.

408
00:15:08,841 --> 00:15:10,376
I think it's hers.

409
00:15:10,442 --> 00:15:12,544
Is she your biological sister?

410
00:15:12,611 --> 00:15:14,580
-You have a sister?
-Wasn't he an only child?

411
00:15:14,647 --> 00:15:17,383
-I have a younger sister.
-A son and a daughter.

412
00:15:17,449 --> 00:15:19,852
You have a sibling,
yet you're that unsociable?

413
00:15:20,686 --> 00:15:22,321
THE BIGGEST TWIST(?)

414
00:15:22,388 --> 00:15:23,789
I have a younger sister.

415
00:15:23,856 --> 00:15:26,759
And he truly is a cat guy.
He has cat treats here.

416
00:15:26,825 --> 00:15:29,328
-What's this?
-Omega-3 for cats.

417
00:15:29,395 --> 00:15:31,063
-It's for your cats?
-It is.

418
00:15:32,331 --> 00:15:33,499
To the freezer.

419
00:15:33,565 --> 00:15:35,367
What's this?

420
00:15:35,434 --> 00:15:37,636
Those may be
the most important ingredients today.

421
00:15:37,703 --> 00:15:40,139
-Carabineros and scampi.
-Scampi?

422
00:15:40,205 --> 00:15:41,907
-Scampi?
-And carabineros.

423
00:15:41,974 --> 00:15:43,242
This is scampi.

424
00:15:43,309 --> 00:15:44,243
What's scampi?

425
00:15:44,310 --> 00:15:47,880
They're also called red-banded lobsters.

426
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:50,582
Carabineros are red shrimps from Spain.
They're expensive.

427
00:15:50,649 --> 00:15:52,418
They're both high-end ingredients.

428
00:15:52,484 --> 00:15:54,520
-They're both expensive.
-It's the first time on the show.

429
00:15:54,586 --> 00:15:56,789
Yes, it's the first time
someone has had carabineros.

430
00:15:56,855 --> 00:16:00,459
When the ingredients lose their freshness,
I move them to the test kitchen.

431
00:16:00,526 --> 00:16:03,128
So you can test and experiment with these.

432
00:16:03,195 --> 00:16:06,231
-We get to see these, thanks to the chefs.
-Those scampi are great.

433
00:16:06,298 --> 00:16:07,967
What's this meat?

434
00:16:08,033 --> 00:16:09,301
Veal shank.

435
00:16:09,368 --> 00:16:11,370
-Everything's staged.
-Veal shank?

436
00:16:11,437 --> 00:16:14,306
I used it at the restaurant,
but I took the dish off the menu.

437
00:16:14,373 --> 00:16:15,808
SENT TO THE TEST KITCHEN

438
00:16:15,874 --> 00:16:18,277
-That's lamb thymus, sweetbread.
-Sweetbread?

439
00:16:18,344 --> 00:16:19,645
What's lamb thymus?

440
00:16:19,712 --> 00:16:23,615
It's a veal cut
that includes its lymphatic system.

441
00:16:23,682 --> 00:16:26,318
It's like cod milt, but meat.

442
00:16:26,385 --> 00:16:27,553
Like milt?

443
00:16:27,619 --> 00:16:30,055
-It's creamy, and it tastes meaty.
-Really?

444
00:16:30,122 --> 00:16:31,390
Shelf-stable ingredients.

445
00:16:31,457 --> 00:16:34,493
-What's this?
-Gelatin.

446
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:37,229
I test many dessert recipes,

447
00:16:37,296 --> 00:16:38,831
and I use that often.

448
00:16:38,897 --> 00:16:40,399
It's used to make jelly.

449
00:16:41,367 --> 00:16:44,536
That was all for Chef Sung-jun's fridge.

450
00:16:44,603 --> 00:16:45,704
It was like a set.

451
00:16:45,771 --> 00:16:48,607
I've never felt this icky
as we shut the fridge door.

452
00:16:49,108 --> 00:16:50,609
SMUG FRIDGE 101

453
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:53,278
We'll now move on to Nam-no's fridge.

454
00:16:53,345 --> 00:16:55,481
Is that from your test kitchen too?

455
00:16:55,547 --> 00:16:56,749
It's from my home.

456
00:16:56,815 --> 00:16:58,817
-This is what I call authentic.
-Exactly.

457
00:16:58,884 --> 00:17:00,152
-It's so real.
-He's sincere.

458
00:17:00,452 --> 00:17:01,687
…HMM

459
00:17:01,754 --> 00:17:03,088
They actually took my fridge.

460
00:17:03,155 --> 00:17:04,456
Yes, the entire thing.

461
00:17:04,523 --> 00:17:06,825
I got a pint of ice cream and went home,

462
00:17:06,892 --> 00:17:09,261
thinking I'd still have my fridge there.

463
00:17:09,328 --> 00:17:12,498
I usually eat half
and store the other half in the freezer,

464
00:17:12,564 --> 00:17:14,166
but it was missing.

465
00:17:14,233 --> 00:17:15,667
So I had to eat it all.

466
00:17:15,734 --> 00:17:17,503
-How smart.
-You had no choice.

467
00:17:17,569 --> 00:17:19,872
Were you happy or disappointed?

468
00:17:19,938 --> 00:17:21,540
I was really stressed out without it.

469
00:17:21,607 --> 00:17:22,775
SEPARATION ANXIETY

470
00:17:22,841 --> 00:17:25,077
There's a picture showing his misery

471
00:17:25,144 --> 00:17:27,379
as we took his fridge.

472
00:17:27,446 --> 00:17:28,313
Do you want to see it?

473
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:30,849
TA-DA

474
00:17:30,916 --> 00:17:32,851
Look at his face.

475
00:17:32,918 --> 00:17:34,086
-My gosh.
-What's with my toes?

476
00:17:34,153 --> 00:17:35,187
They're curled.

477
00:17:35,254 --> 00:17:37,289
-Why are they curled?
-Spread them out.

478
00:17:37,356 --> 00:17:39,558
He got mad and curled his toes.

479
00:17:39,625 --> 00:17:41,860
We can see how real everything is.

480
00:17:41,927 --> 00:17:43,829
It already feels sincere.

481
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:45,664
Do you cook often?

482
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:49,234
I wouldn't say I cook often,

483
00:17:49,301 --> 00:17:50,402
but I eat ready-ready food.

484
00:17:50,469 --> 00:17:52,838
-Ready-made?
-Ready-ready?

485
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:54,139
What's ready-ready?

486
00:17:54,206 --> 00:17:55,441
Ready-ready.

487
00:17:55,507 --> 00:17:56,942
-"Ready-made."
-"Ready-made."

488
00:17:57,009 --> 00:17:59,144
Yes, ready-made. What's with me?

489
00:17:59,211 --> 00:18:01,413
He wants to get ready twice.

490
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:02,548
Come on.

491
00:18:02,614 --> 00:18:05,717
-Convenience food.
-Yes, that's better.

492
00:18:05,784 --> 00:18:07,486
-Convenience food.
-Let's take a look.

493
00:18:07,553 --> 00:18:10,622
-We present Nam-no's fridge!
-Fridge!

494
00:18:12,291 --> 00:18:13,926
EVERYONE'S AMAZED

495
00:18:13,992 --> 00:18:15,027
-Fridge!
-Fridge!

496
00:18:16,361 --> 00:18:17,229
It's full.

497
00:18:18,530 --> 00:18:20,532
It's definitely a home fridge.

498
00:18:20,599 --> 00:18:22,534
Yes, it's a whole household.

499
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:24,636
-It's so real.
-It's full of stuff.

500
00:18:24,703 --> 00:18:26,605
-He has lots of food.
-He does.

501
00:18:26,672 --> 00:18:29,541
It's so crowded in here.

502
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:31,777
He's almost done with this.

503
00:18:31,844 --> 00:18:33,645
-Jam. Strawberry jam?
-Strawberry jam?

504
00:18:33,712 --> 00:18:34,713
-Wait.
-Has it expired?

505
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:36,682
-"For Chef Yoon Nam-no."
-What?

506
00:18:36,748 --> 00:18:38,383
-Who's it from?
-It's a woman's handwriting.

507
00:18:38,450 --> 00:18:40,319
-What?
-Who's it from?

508
00:18:40,385 --> 00:18:43,088
-From Ms. Jang in Nonsan.
-What?

509
00:18:43,155 --> 00:18:46,692
We did a shoot together,
and her jam was really good.

510
00:18:46,758 --> 00:18:48,660
You got it as a present? That's so nice.

511
00:18:48,727 --> 00:18:50,295
That's very cute.

512
00:18:50,362 --> 00:18:52,631
What are these on the second shelf?

513
00:18:52,698 --> 00:18:55,033
-Dried persimmon?
-Dried persimmons, right?

514
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:56,468
Whole dried persimmons and slices.

515
00:18:56,535 --> 00:18:59,371
I got them from Ms. Choi at Jirisan.

516
00:19:00,606 --> 00:19:02,808
-He knows all these ladies.
-He's loved by older ladies.

517
00:19:03,308 --> 00:19:05,410
POPULAR AMONG OLDER WOMEN

518
00:19:05,477 --> 00:19:07,412
What are these?

519
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:09,381
Prickly ash,
and that's probably perilla oil.

520
00:19:09,448 --> 00:19:11,850
-All from Ms. Choi of Jirisan.
-From Jirisan?

521
00:19:11,917 --> 00:19:13,585
How did you meet her?

522
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:16,121
She reached out to me personally,

523
00:19:16,188 --> 00:19:18,657
saying she loves the way I eat.

524
00:19:18,724 --> 00:19:20,459
She began to send me side dishes,

525
00:19:20,526 --> 00:19:23,028
such as green onion kimchi and whatnot.

526
00:19:23,095 --> 00:19:25,097
She doesn't want me to lose weight,

527
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:27,533
-so she sends me food to keep me here.
-For what reason?

528
00:19:27,599 --> 00:19:29,935
-That's real love.
-It is.

529
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,703
I'm loved by the elders.

530
00:19:31,770 --> 00:19:35,474
We can see from his fridge that he's loved
by many in his mom's generation.

531
00:19:35,541 --> 00:19:37,075
You got <i>jokbal</i>, pig's trotters, delivered.

532
00:19:37,142 --> 00:19:39,778
He did, but he didn't eat any.

533
00:19:39,845 --> 00:19:41,346
-Why not?
-That's impossible.

534
00:19:41,413 --> 00:19:43,482
-What's this? <i>Jokbal?</i>
-That?

535
00:19:43,549 --> 00:19:46,451
Someone here can use
my favorite <i>jokbal</i> and cook with it.

536
00:19:46,518 --> 00:19:48,620
-It was an ingredient.
-It was for them.

537
00:19:48,687 --> 00:19:50,589
-Or we can eat it together.
-Sounds good.

538
00:19:50,656 --> 00:19:53,125
He brought one without opening it.
Just as how it came.

539
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:54,526
Can I take that home?

540
00:19:54,593 --> 00:19:56,028
What's this?

541
00:19:56,094 --> 00:19:58,130
Green plum preserves.

542
00:19:58,197 --> 00:19:59,031
Green plum preserves?

543
00:19:59,097 --> 00:20:02,968
It's not Japanese style,
the salty and sour flavor.

544
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:06,104
I've preserved them in sugar.

545
00:20:06,171 --> 00:20:07,539
Do you eat it with your meals?

546
00:20:07,606 --> 00:20:10,008
No, that's my ice cream topping.

547
00:20:10,075 --> 00:20:12,211
-Ice cream?
-With ice cream?

548
00:20:12,277 --> 00:20:14,413
Regular vanilla ice cream?

549
00:20:14,479 --> 00:20:16,448
-Macadamia ice cream.
-Macadamia ice cream?

550
00:20:16,515 --> 00:20:17,950
He only has ice cream in here.

551
00:20:18,016 --> 00:20:19,551
Well, then.

552
00:20:19,618 --> 00:20:22,454
Why don't you try this?
He says it's a good combination.

553
00:20:22,521 --> 00:20:25,624
-He says it's a good ice cream topping.
-It's so good.

554
00:20:25,691 --> 00:20:27,859
It'd be awesome if this were good.

555
00:20:27,926 --> 00:20:29,828
-I'll get some.
-Don't eat too much.

556
00:20:30,095 --> 00:20:31,830
ANXIOUS

557
00:20:32,164 --> 00:20:34,199
CROWDED

558
00:20:34,266 --> 00:20:37,970
-He didn't use salt, but just sugar.
-Just sugar.

559
00:20:38,036 --> 00:20:39,738
The chefs try the snack too.

560
00:20:39,805 --> 00:20:41,506
What's the mix like?

561
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:42,774
This is great.

562
00:20:42,841 --> 00:20:44,009
-Is it?
-It's sour.

563
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:45,444
It's sweet and sour.

564
00:20:45,510 --> 00:20:47,179
-It's a good mix.
-It's great.

565
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:48,814
-He's a foodie.
-It is good.

566
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:51,550
Macadamia nuts have nutty and rich flavor,

567
00:20:51,617 --> 00:20:53,752
-so a hint of sourness is really nice.
-The sourness.

568
00:20:53,819 --> 00:20:55,454
It makes you salivate.

569
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:57,723
-It's good.
-It's sweet and sour.

570
00:20:57,789 --> 00:20:59,291
-Do you want some?
-No.

571
00:20:59,358 --> 00:21:00,192
You can have it.

572
00:21:00,792 --> 00:21:02,961
YUM(?)

573
00:21:03,028 --> 00:21:04,396
GOSH!

574
00:21:04,663 --> 00:21:05,931
GAVE UP HIS ICE CREAM

575
00:21:05,998 --> 00:21:08,834
Is there any other food combination
that most people don't know of?

576
00:21:08,900 --> 00:21:10,869
<i>-Yukgaejang,</i> spicy beef soup.
<i>-Yukgaejang.</i>

577
00:21:10,936 --> 00:21:15,674
Grab some soup and use another spoon
to top it with macaroni salad.

578
00:21:15,741 --> 00:21:16,975
-Macaroni salad?
-The mayo salad.

579
00:21:17,042 --> 00:21:18,343
-Macaroni salad?
-With mayo?

580
00:21:18,410 --> 00:21:21,380
Those two can't be good.
<i>Yukgaejang</i> and macaroni salad?

581
00:21:21,446 --> 00:21:23,682
You'll taste sweetness, spiciness,

582
00:21:23,749 --> 00:21:26,251
and some richness, three in one.

583
00:21:26,318 --> 00:21:27,886
So try those two together.

584
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:30,155
Fried rice is always delicious

585
00:21:30,222 --> 00:21:31,823
but try adding breadcrumbs to it.

586
00:21:31,890 --> 00:21:35,260
-What?
-You can find a bag for 700 to 900 won,

587
00:21:35,327 --> 00:21:37,496
-…and it just says "breadcrumbs."
-Breadcrumbs.

588
00:21:37,562 --> 00:21:39,364
So toast them in a pan
and add them to your rice.

589
00:21:39,431 --> 00:21:41,266
Or you can just add it on top.

590
00:21:41,333 --> 00:21:43,135
The texture. I get it.

591
00:21:43,201 --> 00:21:45,804
Can Nam-no just cook for us?

592
00:21:46,071 --> 00:21:48,540
TASTINESS GUARANTEED

593
00:21:48,607 --> 00:21:52,511
What are these? Do you have indigestion?
They're all digestive drinks.

594
00:21:52,577 --> 00:21:54,513
I got GLP-1 injections for a while,

595
00:21:54,579 --> 00:21:56,748
so I took them because of the indigestion.

596
00:21:56,815 --> 00:21:59,451
-Isn't this the shot?
-That's it.

597
00:21:59,518 --> 00:22:00,352
That's it.

598
00:22:00,419 --> 00:22:02,120
-Did you lose weight?
-You used that?

599
00:22:02,187 --> 00:22:03,488
It was effective.

600
00:22:03,555 --> 00:22:04,923
-What?
-How so?

601
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:07,492
-I lost one kilogram.
-One kilogram?

602
00:22:07,559 --> 00:22:09,061
-It's the same as skipping one meal.
-That little?

603
00:22:09,127 --> 00:22:11,496
-Skipping one meal.
-Yes, skip one meal.

604
00:22:11,563 --> 00:22:13,432
It's tough for him to skip one meal.

605
00:22:13,498 --> 00:22:14,633
You overcame the GLP-1.

606
00:22:15,967 --> 00:22:17,736
-What is this?
-What's that?

607
00:22:17,803 --> 00:22:21,206
-That's a very precious ingredient.
-What's that?

608
00:22:21,273 --> 00:22:23,742
-What's that?
<i>-Hapjajang.</i>

609
00:22:23,809 --> 00:22:26,578
-It's made by boiling down mussel broth.
-Yes.

610
00:22:26,645 --> 00:22:28,113
It's practically an umami bomb.

611
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:29,881
-Mussels?
-Mussels have a lot of umami.

612
00:22:29,948 --> 00:22:31,850
The crisper drawer.

613
00:22:31,917 --> 00:22:33,518
Why does he need that?

614
00:22:33,585 --> 00:22:36,822
-He eats veggies?
-It's full of cabbage and…

615
00:22:36,888 --> 00:22:39,624
-Napa cabbage.
-Napa cabbage.

616
00:22:39,691 --> 00:22:41,760
Those are two of my favorite veggies.

617
00:22:41,827 --> 00:22:44,529
Two or whatever, that's all you have.

618
00:22:44,596 --> 00:22:45,864
There's nothing else.

619
00:22:45,931 --> 00:22:47,866
I love napa cabbage in <i>ramyeon,</i>

620
00:22:47,933 --> 00:22:51,636
and I add cabbage
to <i>jeyuk-bokkeum,</i> spicy pork stir-fry.

621
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:53,071
I love to feed on those.

622
00:22:53,138 --> 00:22:55,307
-He does cook often at home.
-He does.

623
00:22:55,374 --> 00:22:58,210
Is this from Dubai?

624
00:22:58,276 --> 00:22:59,611
-What is it?
-Dates?

625
00:22:59,678 --> 00:23:03,081
My older brother worked
in Abu Dhabi until recently,

626
00:23:03,148 --> 00:23:04,616
-for a decade.
-Looks good.

627
00:23:04,683 --> 00:23:07,486
I always asked him
to bring me some of those.

628
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:08,920
Those are really sweet.

629
00:23:08,987 --> 00:23:12,657
Top a cracker
with cream cheese and one date.

630
00:23:12,724 --> 00:23:14,526
Next, the freezer.

631
00:23:14,593 --> 00:23:17,295
-Ice cream.
-Look at these.

632
00:23:17,362 --> 00:23:18,663
-He has lots.
-Yogurt ice cream?

633
00:23:18,730 --> 00:23:20,065
<i>-Bingsu.</i>
<i>-Bingsu.</i>

634
00:23:20,132 --> 00:23:21,366
He has a sweet tooth.

635
00:23:21,433 --> 00:23:23,135
-Next.
-He loves desserts.

636
00:23:23,201 --> 00:23:24,770
<i>-Mandu.</i> Dumplings.
-You must love them.

637
00:23:24,836 --> 00:23:26,204
They're good as is,

638
00:23:26,271 --> 00:23:27,739
but I like to eat them

639
00:23:27,806 --> 00:23:30,942
with a mix of diced squid <i>jeotgal</i>,

640
00:23:31,009 --> 00:23:33,812
minced garlic, green onion, sesame seeds,

641
00:23:33,879 --> 00:23:35,313
and a bit of red pepper powder.

642
00:23:35,380 --> 00:23:37,082
I top it on the dumplings.

643
00:23:37,149 --> 00:23:38,583
Instead of soy sauce?

644
00:23:38,650 --> 00:23:39,818
What's this?

645
00:23:39,885 --> 00:23:42,954
Those bite-size corn dogs
are my morning routine.

646
00:23:43,021 --> 00:23:44,923
-Wait.
-Your morning routine?

647
00:23:44,990 --> 00:23:46,625
-You're busy.
-Did you get your checkup?

648
00:23:46,691 --> 00:23:48,460
Corn dogs are big, right?

649
00:23:48,527 --> 00:23:50,829
-But you can fit that in your mouth.
-How many do you eat?

650
00:23:50,896 --> 00:23:54,199
-About 20 in the morning.
-What? 20?

651
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:57,035
-That's a whole bag.
-Those are tiny.

652
00:23:57,102 --> 00:23:58,637
-Wait.
-They're like pills.

653
00:23:58,703 --> 00:24:00,071
-Pills?
-They're bigger.

654
00:24:00,138 --> 00:24:00,972
YUM

655
00:24:01,039 --> 00:24:03,275
Even 20 pills would make you full.

656
00:24:03,341 --> 00:24:04,476
It's filled with a sausage.

657
00:24:04,543 --> 00:24:06,545
You have bags of these.
So this is for breakfast?

658
00:24:06,611 --> 00:24:08,346
-Those and…
-A cup of coffee?

659
00:24:08,413 --> 00:24:11,249
-…sparkling water or cola.
-Sparkling water?

660
00:24:11,316 --> 00:24:12,184
A DEEP SIGH

661
00:24:12,250 --> 00:24:13,351
Shelf-stable ingredients.

662
00:24:13,418 --> 00:24:15,287
-You have lots of <i>ramyeon.</i>
-I do.

663
00:24:15,353 --> 00:24:18,190
Is there another recommendation
for one of the <i>ramyeon?</i>

664
00:24:18,256 --> 00:24:20,859
The black bean <i>ramyeon</i>
and <i>jjamppong ramyeon.</i>

665
00:24:20,926 --> 00:24:23,762
Their mix is fantastic.

666
00:24:23,829 --> 00:24:24,896
-Do you mix these two?
-Yes.

667
00:24:24,963 --> 00:24:25,997
It's really good.

668
00:24:26,064 --> 00:24:28,767
-Also, the anchovy <i>kal-guksu ramyeon.</i>
-Anchovy <i>kal-guksu</i>.

669
00:24:28,834 --> 00:24:32,304
It tastes like <i>al-tang,</i> fish roe soup,
if you add some pollack roe.

670
00:24:32,370 --> 00:24:34,539
It's a mix of anchovy broth

671
00:24:34,606 --> 00:24:37,042
-and the pollack roe flavor.
-I can see the vision.

672
00:24:37,108 --> 00:24:38,944
What's this? They're in here.

673
00:24:39,010 --> 00:24:40,312
They look so precious.

674
00:24:40,378 --> 00:24:42,347
I kept them in the basket.

675
00:24:42,414 --> 00:24:43,682
-Protein.
-Protein?

676
00:24:43,748 --> 00:24:45,283
-Protein?
-You take protein?

677
00:24:45,350 --> 00:24:46,685
They're from Jong-won.

678
00:24:46,751 --> 00:24:49,554
-I see.
-Our green room is crowded, right?

679
00:24:49,621 --> 00:24:52,557
He said, "You want this, Nam-no?"
And my heart started racing.

680
00:24:52,624 --> 00:24:54,259
-Suddenly?
-Your heart?

681
00:24:54,326 --> 00:24:55,727
So that's like his merch?

682
00:24:55,794 --> 00:24:58,163
-It's his merch.
-I couldn't eat them.

683
00:24:58,230 --> 00:25:00,799
Maybe he thought
what Jong-won was eating looked good.

684
00:25:00,866 --> 00:25:04,035
I get indigestion
if I eat anything during the shoot,

685
00:25:04,102 --> 00:25:06,905
so I take one for lunch
and one for dinner on a shoot day.

686
00:25:06,972 --> 00:25:09,040
So while I was eating one,

687
00:25:09,608 --> 00:25:12,744
he had <i>ramyeon, </i>eggs, and a meal box,

688
00:25:12,811 --> 00:25:14,613
then looked at me. I was taking that.

689
00:25:14,679 --> 00:25:15,981
Desperately?

690
00:25:16,047 --> 00:25:18,950
And he looked at me so desperately.

691
00:25:19,017 --> 00:25:21,520
-That's uncomfortable.
-So I skipped dinner that day.

692
00:25:21,586 --> 00:25:24,589
-That was your dinner?
-So why did you keep it like this?

693
00:25:24,656 --> 00:25:26,558
-It's his merch.
-It's the merch.

694
00:25:26,625 --> 00:25:27,893
He's keeping it.

695
00:25:27,959 --> 00:25:31,263
We looked through Chef Nam-no's fridge,
a guy who has the best database

696
00:25:31,329 --> 00:25:32,898
when it comes to food!

697
00:25:32,964 --> 00:25:35,333
FINISHED CHECKING OUT NAM-NO'S FRIDGE

698
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:37,736
Let's find out what their orders are.

699
00:25:37,802 --> 00:25:40,539
First, show us Chef Sung-jun's order.

700
00:25:40,605 --> 00:25:41,473
Show us!

701
00:25:43,041 --> 00:25:45,510
-Everyone, I've Done It! I've Gone Viral!
-I've Gone Viral!

702
00:25:45,577 --> 00:25:48,146
SHOUTING IMMEDIATELY

703
00:25:48,213 --> 00:25:49,948
He sounds like a voice actor.

704
00:25:50,015 --> 00:25:53,018
-That was a meme.
-It's a meme.

705
00:25:53,084 --> 00:25:54,686
Everyone, I've done it!

706
00:25:54,753 --> 00:25:56,588
A POPULAR AI VOICE ON SOCIAL MEDIA

707
00:25:56,655 --> 00:25:58,423
-He can probably do it.
-I can.

708
00:25:58,490 --> 00:25:59,524
How do you do it?

709
00:25:59,591 --> 00:26:00,759
It usually begins with…

710
00:26:00,825 --> 00:26:01,726
Dang it!

711
00:26:01,793 --> 00:26:02,961
Everyone, I've Done It!

712
00:26:03,028 --> 00:26:04,329
I've Gone Viral!

713
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:05,263
GOOD AT RANDOM THINGS

714
00:26:05,330 --> 00:26:07,299
-He's good.
-Is that how it's done?

715
00:26:07,365 --> 00:26:09,367
-Everyone, I've Done It!
-Dang it!

716
00:26:09,434 --> 00:26:11,102
-I've Gone Viral!
-I've Gone Viral!

717
00:26:11,169 --> 00:26:13,204
-Do you practice this at home?
-Of course.

718
00:26:13,271 --> 00:26:15,907
-I always study these things.
-That's why you do that.

719
00:26:15,974 --> 00:26:17,275
Do kids love this meme?

720
00:26:17,342 --> 00:26:19,110
-They'd love it.
-Really?

721
00:26:19,177 --> 00:26:22,380
-Everyone, I've Done It! I've Gone Viral!
-I've Gone Viral!

722
00:26:22,447 --> 00:26:25,450
I really love social media,

723
00:26:25,517 --> 00:26:29,921
so I want something that'll go viral,
something that'll create a buzz.

724
00:26:30,755 --> 00:26:32,657
I want something like that,

725
00:26:32,724 --> 00:26:35,994
something that'll rake in
about 100,000 likes on the Internet.

726
00:26:36,061 --> 00:26:37,963
He wants a dish that will be remembered…

727
00:26:38,029 --> 00:26:39,798
-Yes.
-…and talked about.

728
00:26:39,864 --> 00:26:43,034
Next up, Nam-no's order. What is it?

729
00:26:44,069 --> 00:26:46,905
Pay Stub? Nonsense.
I'm Taking My Pay in Food.

730
00:26:46,972 --> 00:26:48,473
-Won-bin's line?
-Yes.

731
00:26:48,540 --> 00:26:50,241
-It's that line.
-His biggest line.

732
00:26:50,308 --> 00:26:52,010
-Can you do it like him?
-Do it.

733
00:26:52,077 --> 00:26:53,612
-Yoon-bin.
-Do it.

734
00:26:53,678 --> 00:26:55,580
Pay Stub?

735
00:26:55,647 --> 00:26:57,716
Nonsense. I'm Taking My Pay in Food.

736
00:26:57,782 --> 00:26:58,617
I'm scared.

737
00:26:58,683 --> 00:27:00,018
He's good.

738
00:27:00,085 --> 00:27:02,087
-He is.
-That was Won-bin's line.

739
00:27:02,153 --> 00:27:03,788
"Nonsense."

740
00:27:03,855 --> 00:27:05,423
-I'm Taking My Pay in Food.
-I'm Taking My Pay in Food.

741
00:27:05,490 --> 00:27:08,159
-So you want to be paid in food?
-Yes.

742
00:27:08,226 --> 00:27:10,462
What many people assume

743
00:27:10,528 --> 00:27:13,131
is that I get paid
by the food that's made here.

744
00:27:13,898 --> 00:27:15,634
-You do eat a lot.
-I hear that so often,

745
00:27:15,700 --> 00:27:17,869
almost too much. But actually,

746
00:27:17,936 --> 00:27:19,638
I want something more than my pay,

747
00:27:19,704 --> 00:27:22,340
like a 100% bonus, an incentive.

748
00:27:22,407 --> 00:27:23,308
-An incentive?
-Yes.

749
00:27:23,375 --> 00:27:24,309
Something hearty.

750
00:27:24,376 --> 00:27:26,244
-A huge quantity?
-It has to be a lot.

751
00:27:26,311 --> 00:27:28,546
The quantity is very important.

752
00:27:28,613 --> 00:27:29,581
A generous serving.

753
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:32,550
Please do not make me
something that looks like finger food.

754
00:27:32,617 --> 00:27:34,152
-Finger food?
-Like pills.

755
00:27:34,219 --> 00:27:35,453
Finger food?

756
00:27:35,520 --> 00:27:38,089
-Is he attacking someone?
-I'm suddenly triggered.

757
00:27:38,356 --> 00:27:39,357
ANXIOUS

758
00:27:39,424 --> 00:27:41,526
-No, many people do that.
-He's attacking you.

759
00:27:41,593 --> 00:27:43,662
He's like, "Jong-won, don't come to me."

760
00:27:43,995 --> 00:27:46,231
FALSELY FRAMED

761
00:27:46,297 --> 00:27:48,800
All right.
You can pick the chef you're fond of,

762
00:27:48,867 --> 00:27:50,402
or you can join as a team.

763
00:27:50,468 --> 00:27:51,736
As teams?

764
00:27:51,803 --> 00:27:55,206
Who wants to join?
You're all looking around.

765
00:27:55,273 --> 00:27:56,975
Why won't anyone look me in the eye?

766
00:27:57,042 --> 00:27:58,710
-Why won't anyone join?
-Go ahead.

767
00:27:58,777 --> 00:28:00,512
What happens if no one joins?

768
00:28:00,578 --> 00:28:02,180
Do we go home?

769
00:28:02,247 --> 00:28:03,848
Do I cook for myself?

770
00:28:03,915 --> 00:28:05,183
Cook for yourself?

771
00:28:05,250 --> 00:28:07,652
If no one steps in,

772
00:28:07,719 --> 00:28:09,688
we'll get some food delivered.

773
00:28:09,754 --> 00:28:11,990
-That's not a bad idea.
-Not bad.

774
00:28:12,057 --> 00:28:13,324
The chefs are like,

775
00:28:13,391 --> 00:28:14,959
"Do we have to cook for you two?"

776
00:28:15,226 --> 00:28:16,127
YOU GOT US(?)

777
00:28:16,194 --> 00:28:17,562
-How mean.
-I can read your faces.

778
00:28:17,629 --> 00:28:19,197
-Everyone!
-Come on. Jump in.

779
00:28:19,264 --> 00:28:20,699
-You can still win stars.
-Give it a go.

780
00:28:20,765 --> 00:28:22,801
-Poong raised his hand.
-Poong?

781
00:28:22,867 --> 00:28:24,703
WHO WILL POONG CHOOSE?

782
00:28:24,769 --> 00:28:27,972
First of all,
I'd like to make a huge portion.

783
00:28:28,039 --> 00:28:30,875
So I'll go for Nam-no's fridge.

784
00:28:30,942 --> 00:28:34,779
There's someone
I've never cooked with as a team,

785
00:28:34,846 --> 00:28:36,715
and it's Sam.

786
00:28:36,781 --> 00:28:38,016
With Sam?

787
00:28:38,083 --> 00:28:41,019
So I thought it'd be fun
to team up with him.

788
00:28:41,086 --> 00:28:42,187
Aren't they the polar opposites?

789
00:28:42,253 --> 00:28:43,855
Sam never makes a huge portion.

790
00:28:43,922 --> 00:28:45,256
I don't.

791
00:28:45,323 --> 00:28:47,258
-One loves bold flavors.
-Right.

792
00:28:47,325 --> 00:28:49,094
-And he's a naturalist.
-The other one, yes.

793
00:28:49,360 --> 00:28:50,595
A MIX OF DISSONANCE(?)

794
00:28:50,662 --> 00:28:52,464
It seemed like a great opportunity.

795
00:28:52,530 --> 00:28:54,065
You two might get into a conflict.

796
00:28:54,132 --> 00:28:58,837
-Sam and Poong join Nam-no's round.
-A new combination.

797
00:28:58,903 --> 00:29:02,273
-Who wants to join next?
-I'll go.

798
00:29:02,340 --> 00:29:04,042
-Whoa.
-Which one?

799
00:29:04,109 --> 00:29:08,246
There's a chef
whom I've always wanted to team up with.

800
00:29:08,313 --> 00:29:10,482
-It's Chef Eun-yeong.
-Me?

801
00:29:10,548 --> 00:29:12,684
-We're on different wavelengths.
-Nam-no's round?

802
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:15,019
I'll join that round.

803
00:29:15,086 --> 00:29:17,555
I don't think Nam-no wanted him.

804
00:29:17,622 --> 00:29:19,290
-You're on a strict diet.
-Right?

805
00:29:19,357 --> 00:29:21,960
-I can eat a lot on a cheat day.
-Sure.

806
00:29:22,026 --> 00:29:24,028
-Is that okay, Eun-yeong?
-Sounds good.

807
00:29:24,095 --> 00:29:27,098
I'd love to.
I've wanted to cook with him too.

808
00:29:27,165 --> 00:29:29,467
So we'll team up
and feed him until he's full.

809
00:29:29,734 --> 00:29:31,069
PLEASED

810
00:29:31,136 --> 00:29:33,071
Another new team.

811
00:29:33,138 --> 00:29:35,273
There are three of you left.

812
00:29:35,340 --> 00:29:36,341
Who'll join?

813
00:29:36,407 --> 00:29:37,909
I see the social media addict.

814
00:29:37,976 --> 00:29:39,577
-Hey.
-Ho-young!

815
00:29:39,644 --> 00:29:43,481
-It's Ho-young!
-Yes, he knows the importance of virality.

816
00:29:43,548 --> 00:29:45,083
Social media is important for him too.

817
00:29:45,150 --> 00:29:47,619
As a social media addict,

818
00:29:48,953 --> 00:29:50,755
the theme is perfect for me.

819
00:29:52,323 --> 00:29:53,858
I'll go.

820
00:29:53,925 --> 00:29:54,893
Are you sure?

821
00:29:54,959 --> 00:29:57,162
I failed miserably trying to beat

822
00:29:57,228 --> 00:29:58,830
that social media addict.

823
00:29:58,897 --> 00:30:02,967
But I want to beat Chef Ho-young,
who loves things that go viral.

824
00:30:03,034 --> 00:30:04,502
Like, "Get a grip."

825
00:30:04,569 --> 00:30:07,038
Which one will Sung-jun choose?

826
00:30:07,105 --> 00:30:11,576
Let us begin
Hyun-suk and Ho-young's cook-off!

827
00:30:13,878 --> 00:30:18,183
<i>The first cook-off</i>
<i>is played with Sung-jun's ingredients.</i>

828
00:30:18,249 --> 00:30:22,020
Chef Jung Ho-young, hoping to go viral
through his selfie photo dump,

829
00:30:22,086 --> 00:30:24,455
versus Chef Choi Hyun-suk,

830
00:30:24,522 --> 00:30:27,025
looking to go viral
through his salt dumping.

831
00:30:27,091 --> 00:30:30,528
Hyun-suk, did you really expect

832
00:30:30,595 --> 00:30:34,299
Sung-jun to show up with this order today?

833
00:30:34,365 --> 00:30:36,534
Who else is going to order that?

834
00:30:36,601 --> 00:30:38,303
There's no other guest

835
00:30:38,369 --> 00:30:40,205
who's looking to stand in the spotlight

836
00:30:40,271 --> 00:30:41,806
and receive the attention by himself.

837
00:30:41,873 --> 00:30:45,510
I knew Sung-jun would come
with an order that reflects his character.

838
00:30:45,577 --> 00:30:47,445
The criticism never ends.

839
00:30:47,512 --> 00:30:49,247
-I guess he doesn't want a star.
-Seriously.

840
00:30:49,314 --> 00:30:52,050
How is that criticism?
I'm just saying it was expected.

841
00:30:52,116 --> 00:30:54,419
Remember that he's here as a guest.

842
00:30:54,485 --> 00:30:56,454
You were just like him back in the day!

843
00:30:56,521 --> 00:30:59,123
-You were like him. Be nice.
-No, he wasn't like him.

844
00:30:59,190 --> 00:31:00,725
-He was worse.
-He was.

845
00:31:00,792 --> 00:31:01,793
Yes, he was much worse.

846
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:03,828
-See? Right?
-Is it necessary…

847
00:31:03,895 --> 00:31:06,664
He also wasn't really sociable
when the show had just started.

848
00:31:06,731 --> 00:31:07,632
Wait a second.

849
00:31:07,699 --> 00:31:09,767
Chef Sam said something very harsh.

850
00:31:09,834 --> 00:31:11,269
-What did he say?
-Say it again.

851
00:31:11,336 --> 00:31:13,204
He was one of the original members, right?

852
00:31:13,271 --> 00:31:15,340
He wasn't very sociable at the beginning.

853
00:31:17,242 --> 00:31:18,877
ET TU, CANINE…

854
00:31:19,878 --> 00:31:21,579
SPITEFUL SAM'S PROUD

855
00:31:21,646 --> 00:31:23,348
You'll also become social after a while.

856
00:31:23,414 --> 00:31:24,682
Is he my future?

857
00:31:24,749 --> 00:31:27,752
Back in 2014, I also remember him

858
00:31:27,819 --> 00:31:29,320
spending lots of time alone.

859
00:31:29,387 --> 00:31:31,689
-He rarely spoke with others.
-Right?

860
00:31:31,756 --> 00:31:33,391
-He didn't have any friends,
-Really?

861
00:31:33,458 --> 00:31:34,792
…so he began to play the guitar.

862
00:31:35,059 --> 00:31:37,161
THE REASON WHY HE PICKED UP THE GUITAR…

863
00:31:37,228 --> 00:31:39,497
They have so much in common.

864
00:31:39,564 --> 00:31:42,767
He may not remember,
but back then, in the green room,

865
00:31:42,834 --> 00:31:46,137
he was feeling miserable
that he lost his followers.

866
00:31:46,204 --> 00:31:48,072
Yes! I was there too.

867
00:31:48,139 --> 00:31:51,576
-He was like that?
-He was always checking the numbers.

868
00:31:51,643 --> 00:31:53,511
-I did that? Stop lying.
-Yes.

869
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:54,512
I'm dead serious.

870
00:31:54,579 --> 00:31:56,147
-Come on.
-You were like that.

871
00:31:56,214 --> 00:31:57,348
I've heard it too.

872
00:31:57,415 --> 00:32:00,318
It was that he uploaded the wrong post
and lost his followers.

873
00:32:00,385 --> 00:32:02,921
He often complained about that.

874
00:32:02,987 --> 00:32:04,522
He's facing his past self.

875
00:32:04,589 --> 00:32:07,158
-That'd be awful.
-Yes, he doesn't like it.

876
00:32:07,225 --> 00:32:08,059
Wait.

877
00:32:08,126 --> 00:32:09,127
Chef Sung-jun.

878
00:32:09,727 --> 00:32:10,728
It must've been lonely.

879
00:32:11,763 --> 00:32:12,797
CHOKING UP(?)

880
00:32:13,131 --> 00:32:14,933
PUTS HIMSELF IN HIS SHOES

881
00:32:14,999 --> 00:32:17,402
Everyone is attacking me
with these false claims.

882
00:32:17,468 --> 00:32:19,470
Well, there were multiple witnesses.

883
00:32:19,537 --> 00:32:23,207
There's something Sung-jun
needs to tell Ho-young.

884
00:32:23,841 --> 00:32:25,977
I'm often heartbroken to see his feed,

885
00:32:26,044 --> 00:32:28,346
-Really?
-…because he's doing it the wrong way.

886
00:32:28,413 --> 00:32:30,281
-Why?
-He takes pictures

887
00:32:30,348 --> 00:32:33,985
with the celebrity guests we have
and uploads them.

888
00:32:34,052 --> 00:32:35,720
But instead of using filters,

889
00:32:35,787 --> 00:32:38,389
he uploads the raw photo on the Internet.

890
00:32:38,456 --> 00:32:40,291
-That's cruel.
-It's cruel.

891
00:32:40,358 --> 00:32:43,194
-So he should probably use filters.
-I see.

892
00:32:43,261 --> 00:32:45,363
Are you mentioning this to ask him

893
00:32:45,430 --> 00:32:47,098
-to put a filter on you today?
-Yes.

894
00:32:47,165 --> 00:32:48,232
We just took one earlier.

895
00:32:48,299 --> 00:32:50,768
-You did?
-He wants him to touch it up.

896
00:32:51,336 --> 00:32:52,270
Nam-no.

897
00:32:52,337 --> 00:32:53,204
BREAK

898
00:32:53,271 --> 00:32:54,505
We have to take pictures.

899
00:32:55,473 --> 00:32:57,208
I need a picture with the guests.

900
00:32:57,275 --> 00:32:58,776
RUNNING OVER

901
00:32:58,843 --> 00:33:00,979
You're taking one because they're guests?

902
00:33:01,045 --> 00:33:02,547
Let me join.

903
00:33:02,613 --> 00:33:04,048
And one more.

904
00:33:04,115 --> 00:33:05,550
PLAYFUL

905
00:33:05,616 --> 00:33:08,720
Someone hold it. My arms are too short.

906
00:33:10,788 --> 00:33:13,324
CHECK OUT THE PICTURES HERE

907
00:33:13,391 --> 00:33:15,159
GIGGLING

908
00:33:15,226 --> 00:33:16,861
Please touch it up a little.

909
00:33:16,928 --> 00:33:17,762
In that case,

910
00:33:18,563 --> 00:33:20,198
I'll cut you out.

911
00:33:20,431 --> 00:33:21,599
OH, NO

912
00:33:21,666 --> 00:33:25,003
-That's a good idea.
-This time, I'll just include Nam-no.

913
00:33:25,069 --> 00:33:26,170
Wait, you have to upload me.

914
00:33:26,237 --> 00:33:27,305
OH, NOT THAT…

915
00:33:27,372 --> 00:33:29,140
I have something to share about Hyun-suk.

916
00:33:29,207 --> 00:33:30,608
-What is it?
-You have something?

917
00:33:30,675 --> 00:33:32,777
Whenever I upload a Story,

918
00:33:32,844 --> 00:33:35,413
-someone here is the fastest to check it.
-I see.

919
00:33:35,480 --> 00:33:38,216
-Chef Hyun-suk. The first.
-Is he the first?

920
00:33:38,282 --> 00:33:40,151
-He's always the first to show up.
-What?

921
00:33:40,218 --> 00:33:42,053
You're really conscious of me.

922
00:33:44,088 --> 00:33:45,590
COME ON, MAN

923
00:33:46,424 --> 00:33:48,459
CHEF HO-YOUNG'S INGREDIENTS:
VENUS CLAM, LITTLENECK CLAM, CARABINERO

924
00:33:48,526 --> 00:33:50,595
SCAMPI, KELP SEASONING, SHINE MUSCAT,
GELATIN, PUMPKIN FLOWER, AND MORE

925
00:33:50,661 --> 00:33:53,297
Ho-young, tell us about your dish.

926
00:33:53,364 --> 00:33:56,768
Now, take a look at Chef Sung-jun.

927
00:33:59,203 --> 00:34:01,606
Doesn't he sparkle like a jewel?

928
00:34:01,672 --> 00:34:03,307
-No.
-Correct.

929
00:34:03,374 --> 00:34:06,911
He said he liked shellfish and clams,

930
00:34:06,978 --> 00:34:10,014
so I'll use the expensive
yet delicious Spanish shellfish.

931
00:34:10,081 --> 00:34:13,017
-I'm making tartar sauce.
-Tartar?

932
00:34:13,084 --> 00:34:15,453
I also saw gelatin, so I'll use that

933
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:17,121
<i>and mix it with clam broth</i>

934
00:34:17,188 --> 00:34:19,257
to make sauce that sparkles like a jewel.

935
00:34:19,323 --> 00:34:20,858
-Sounds good.
-With gelatin?

936
00:34:20,925 --> 00:34:22,527
-That's my plan.
-He can't do that in 15 minutes.

937
00:34:22,593 --> 00:34:25,329
So when you look at the end result,

938
00:34:25,396 --> 00:34:27,398
it'll look as sparkly

939
00:34:27,465 --> 00:34:30,401
as how Chef Sung-jun sparkles now.

940
00:34:30,468 --> 00:34:32,470
When you said he sparkled,

941
00:34:32,537 --> 00:34:33,671
it felt so fake.

942
00:34:35,339 --> 00:34:37,775
-It's all because of the star.
-He just wants the star.

943
00:34:38,709 --> 00:34:42,780
CHEF HYUN-SUK'S INGREDIENTS:
PASTA, VENUS CLAM, ARUGULA, GARLIC

944
00:34:42,847 --> 00:34:45,450
The name of my dish is

945
00:34:45,516 --> 00:34:46,851
Kwon Sung-jun.

946
00:34:48,286 --> 00:34:49,587
The dish is called Kwon Sung-jun?

947
00:34:49,654 --> 00:34:52,824
The dish itself is a depiction of him.

948
00:34:52,890 --> 00:34:53,891
Kwon Sung-jun.

949
00:34:53,958 --> 00:34:55,426
-That's new.
-It'll be an issue.

950
00:34:55,493 --> 00:34:56,828
I'm almost too excited.

951
00:34:56,894 --> 00:34:58,029
What he wants

952
00:34:58,096 --> 00:35:00,865
is only for him
to receive attention and shine.

953
00:35:01,732 --> 00:35:03,534
I'm going to depict

954
00:35:03,601 --> 00:35:05,603
who Chef Kwon Sung-jun is in my dish.

955
00:35:05,670 --> 00:35:06,771
Wait a second.

956
00:35:06,838 --> 00:35:07,738
Is he making <i>sujebi?</i>

957
00:35:07,805 --> 00:35:09,540
-Are you making <i>sujebi?</i>
-Is that it?

958
00:35:09,607 --> 00:35:11,275
Are you really making <i>sujebi?</i>

959
00:35:11,342 --> 00:35:13,044
Then I'm giving you zero stars.

960
00:35:13,377 --> 00:35:15,146
REFUSING THE DISH(?)

961
00:35:15,213 --> 00:35:16,814
-It's not that.
-Zero stars?

962
00:35:16,881 --> 00:35:18,216
Is he leaving a review?

963
00:35:18,282 --> 00:35:20,418
You're an Italian chef, right?

964
00:35:20,485 --> 00:35:21,819
I'm making my signature dish.

965
00:35:21,886 --> 00:35:22,920
-Could it be?
-Vongole pasta.

966
00:35:22,987 --> 00:35:25,223
-What? Vongole pasta?
-Suddenly?

967
00:35:25,289 --> 00:35:27,024
-Vongole <i>sujebi?</i>
-Is he making <i>sujebi?</i>

968
00:35:27,091 --> 00:35:28,893
-Do you see the big pile of garlic?
-What?

969
00:35:28,960 --> 00:35:30,761
This is enough to make kimchi.

970
00:35:30,828 --> 00:35:32,063
I don't really like garlic.

971
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:34,999
Three years ago,
if I hadn't forgotten garlic that day,

972
00:35:35,066 --> 00:35:36,701
would Sung-jun be here today?

973
00:35:36,901 --> 00:35:39,203
HE FORGOT GARLIC
AND LOST TO SUNG-JUN BY 1 POINT

974
00:35:39,270 --> 00:35:41,973
He couldn't have been here.
He wouldn't be on this show.

975
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:44,775
Why is that a dish for me?

976
00:35:44,842 --> 00:35:45,776
-Right?
-True.

977
00:35:46,811 --> 00:35:49,514
THAT'S TRUE…

978
00:35:49,580 --> 00:35:51,082
Listen up, Chef Sung-jun.

979
00:35:52,750 --> 00:35:55,319
I know very well what it is that you want.

980
00:35:55,386 --> 00:35:57,555
You don't care about looking cool.

981
00:35:57,622 --> 00:35:59,757
All you want is attention.

982
00:35:59,824 --> 00:36:01,225
I will get that for you.

983
00:36:01,626 --> 00:36:02,560
DISTRUSTFUL…

984
00:36:02,627 --> 00:36:04,228
After all, it's about him.

985
00:36:04,295 --> 00:36:06,497
-Should've named it "Choi Hyun-suk."
-Yes.

986
00:36:06,564 --> 00:36:08,733
-That's it.
-"Choi Hyun-suk."

987
00:36:08,799 --> 00:36:11,369
Well, Hyun-suk is also Sung-jun.

988
00:36:11,736 --> 00:36:13,104
WHAT AN ODD RELATIONSHIP…

989
00:36:13,171 --> 00:36:15,473
I'll give Sung-jun what he wants,

990
00:36:15,540 --> 00:36:19,744
so I hope he will not forget
his first master of the show.

991
00:36:20,411 --> 00:36:22,213
YES, SURE…

992
00:36:22,280 --> 00:36:27,051
And now, let us begin the cook-off
for Chef Sung-jun.

993
00:36:27,118 --> 00:36:28,152
Whoa.

994
00:36:29,086 --> 00:36:30,788
-We get to see this?
-Right?

995
00:36:30,855 --> 00:36:32,690
Isn't it different from that seat?

996
00:36:32,757 --> 00:36:33,991
-It is.
-Right?

997
00:36:34,058 --> 00:36:35,493
I feel like a celebrity.

998
00:36:35,560 --> 00:36:39,430
The man who thirsts after
the Internet buzz more than Sung-jun,

999
00:36:39,497 --> 00:36:42,200
the social media addict,
Chef Jung Ho-young.

1000
00:36:42,266 --> 00:36:45,136
The man who preceded Sung-jun,

1001
00:36:45,203 --> 00:36:49,040
the original Kwon Sung-jun,
Chef Choi Hyun-suk.

1002
00:36:49,106 --> 00:36:50,208
That killed my motivation.

1003
00:36:50,274 --> 00:36:53,377
Which one of them will make him go viral?

1004
00:36:53,444 --> 00:36:57,014
Let the 15-minute cook-off begin!

1005
00:36:57,081 --> 00:37:00,051
<i>It has begun! The cook-off has begun!</i>

1006
00:37:00,618 --> 00:37:02,920
HOW WILL THE ORIGINAL KWON SUNG-JUN BEGIN?

1007
00:37:02,987 --> 00:37:04,922
<i>He'll start with salt.</i>

1008
00:37:05,356 --> 00:37:06,490
SHOOTING SALT

1009
00:37:06,557 --> 00:37:07,725
Ah, salt.

1010
00:37:07,792 --> 00:37:09,327
Ah, salt.

1011
00:37:09,393 --> 00:37:11,495
There's salt here.

1012
00:37:11,696 --> 00:37:13,030
SALT WHAT?

1013
00:37:13,698 --> 00:37:15,800
SPLAT…

1014
00:37:16,667 --> 00:37:18,202
He's cooking pasta first.

1015
00:37:18,269 --> 00:37:19,804
What about salt?

1016
00:37:19,870 --> 00:37:21,005
I added some.

1017
00:37:21,072 --> 00:37:22,607
None of it made it in.

1018
00:37:23,174 --> 00:37:24,475
It's okay. I got it.

1019
00:37:24,675 --> 00:37:26,344
COOKING VENUS CLAMS TO MAKE VONGOLE PASTA

1020
00:37:26,744 --> 00:37:27,578
ALSO STARTS WITH CLAMS!

1021
00:37:27,645 --> 00:37:30,514
Ho-young is using venus clams.

1022
00:37:30,581 --> 00:37:31,449
KELP SEASONING

1023
00:37:32,483 --> 00:37:33,784
-Okay.
-The red shrimp?

1024
00:37:33,851 --> 00:37:35,253
-Yes.
-He's using the shrimps.

1025
00:37:35,319 --> 00:37:38,623
-Those are over 20,000 won each.
-Really?

1026
00:37:38,689 --> 00:37:40,057
Almost 30,000 won.

1027
00:37:40,124 --> 00:37:41,292
Really? For one?

1028
00:37:41,359 --> 00:37:43,261
-It's the world's most expensive shrimp.
-Really?

1029
00:37:43,327 --> 00:37:45,463
-I see. The red shrimps.
-Why is that?

1030
00:37:45,529 --> 00:37:47,398
It tastes completely different.

1031
00:37:47,465 --> 00:37:50,167
Compared to regular shrimps,
I personally think

1032
00:37:50,234 --> 00:37:52,403
-they're ten times more delicious.
-The umami?

1033
00:37:52,470 --> 00:37:55,606
So that's 40,000 won, and now, 60,000 won.

1034
00:37:55,673 --> 00:37:57,942
Add another, 80,000 won, and one more.

1035
00:37:58,009 --> 00:37:59,210
Whoa, that's a fortune.

1036
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:00,511
He's using one too many.

1037
00:38:00,745 --> 00:38:01,612
LOOKING UP

1038
00:38:01,812 --> 00:38:03,848
ADDING FLOUR

1039
00:38:04,148 --> 00:38:05,016
WATER

1040
00:38:05,082 --> 00:38:06,217
-Wait.
-What?

1041
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:07,718
He's making <i>sujebi</i> dough.

1042
00:38:07,785 --> 00:38:09,620
-That's Sung-jun.
-He's making <i>sujebi.</i>

1043
00:38:09,687 --> 00:38:11,222
Are you really making it?

1044
00:38:11,289 --> 00:38:13,157
-He's making fresh noodles.
-It doesn't feel right.

1045
00:38:13,224 --> 00:38:15,793
My dish isn't anything like <i>sujebi.</i>

1046
00:38:15,860 --> 00:38:17,728
My dish is Kwon Sung-jun.

1047
00:38:18,462 --> 00:38:19,330
He's making <i>sujebi.</i>

1048
00:38:19,397 --> 00:38:21,699
-He's trying to form Sung-jun.
-It's <i>sujebi.</i>

1049
00:38:21,766 --> 00:38:22,933
PUNCH

1050
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:24,735
Weren't you making vongole pasta?

1051
00:38:24,802 --> 00:38:27,838
Don't belittle yourself
and call yourself <i>sujebi.</i>

1052
00:38:27,905 --> 00:38:29,507
-You…
-You did that.

1053
00:38:29,573 --> 00:38:31,175
You're the show's crown jewel…

1054
00:38:31,242 --> 00:38:33,944
You nicknamed him <i>sujebi.</i>

1055
00:38:34,011 --> 00:38:35,713
Is he going to add that whole?

1056
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:37,682
He's letting it rest.

1057
00:38:37,748 --> 00:38:38,683
TINY…

1058
00:38:38,749 --> 00:38:40,384
When I think of Sung-jun,

1059
00:38:40,451 --> 00:38:43,287
he's not very complicated,
but a very simple man.

1060
00:38:43,354 --> 00:38:45,423
Simple yet rough…

1061
00:38:45,823 --> 00:38:46,657
CHUCKLE…

1062
00:38:46,724 --> 00:38:48,859
-Rough? Tough?
-He's a guest for today.

1063
00:38:48,926 --> 00:38:51,028
Yet tough, that's Sung-jun.

1064
00:38:51,329 --> 00:38:53,431
STAY TOUGH, GRANDPA…

1065
00:38:53,497 --> 00:38:55,733
Don't even dare
to agree with what I make later.

1066
00:38:55,800 --> 00:38:56,967
All right.

1067
00:38:57,034 --> 00:38:58,502
HOW WELL WILL HE DEPICT HIM?

1068
00:38:58,836 --> 00:39:00,738
OVER HERE, THINGS ARE RATHER SERIOUS!

1069
00:39:00,805 --> 00:39:02,873
2. CHOP AND SOAK THE ONION
TO MELLOW THE SHARPNESS

1070
00:39:02,940 --> 00:39:05,276
-He's using grapes.
-What's that?

1071
00:39:05,343 --> 00:39:08,579
-Shine Muscat.
-He's chopping them.

1072
00:39:08,646 --> 00:39:10,548
The sheer cost of the ingredients
is through the roof.

1073
00:39:10,614 --> 00:39:13,084
Red shrimps and grapes.

1074
00:39:13,150 --> 00:39:14,085
CHOP CARABINERO MEAT!

1075
00:39:14,151 --> 00:39:16,153
-It looks good.
-He's not sharing the ingredients.

1076
00:39:16,220 --> 00:39:19,123
Yes, Ho-young's using everything.

1077
00:39:19,557 --> 00:39:22,026
BOILING CLAMS, OUT

1078
00:39:22,093 --> 00:39:26,297
I guess he's using only the clam meat…
No, just the broth?

1079
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:28,232
-He's making <i>tosazu </i>jelly.
-What's that?

1080
00:39:28,299 --> 00:39:31,836
A mix of bonito broth,
soy sauce, vinegar, and sugar.

1081
00:39:31,902 --> 00:39:33,904
-It's a sweet and sour sauce.
-I see.

1082
00:39:33,971 --> 00:39:35,840
And it's often made into jelly.

1083
00:39:35,906 --> 00:39:37,842
Gelatin.

1084
00:39:38,442 --> 00:39:39,810
That's a lot.

1085
00:39:39,877 --> 00:39:41,245
That'll turn into jelly?

1086
00:39:41,312 --> 00:39:43,013
He'll cool it in ice.

1087
00:39:43,080 --> 00:39:44,815
That turns into jelly?

1088
00:39:44,882 --> 00:39:46,984
-I see.
-Ho-young's doing a lot today.

1089
00:39:47,051 --> 00:39:48,586
Will he finish that in time?

1090
00:39:48,652 --> 00:39:50,087
It has to go viral too.

1091
00:39:50,154 --> 00:39:52,156
-Can you stir this?
-Sure.

1092
00:39:52,223 --> 00:39:53,791
Why are you making her do that?

1093
00:39:53,858 --> 00:39:57,828
-It has to cool to harden.
-It has to harden.

1094
00:39:57,895 --> 00:39:59,530
-Chef Ho-young.
-Yes?

1095
00:39:59,597 --> 00:40:00,998
Do you really think

1096
00:40:01,065 --> 00:40:03,067
that kind of a fancy dish
is what Sung-jun wants?

1097
00:40:03,634 --> 00:40:05,136
OH, GOSH…

1098
00:40:05,202 --> 00:40:07,171
-He just wants attention.
-Stop picking a fight.

1099
00:40:07,238 --> 00:40:09,373
Just focus on your dish.

1100
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:12,076
He's using so much garlic.

1101
00:40:12,643 --> 00:40:13,644
Why did he prepare so much?

1102
00:40:13,711 --> 00:40:15,679
I am not forgetting it today.

1103
00:40:15,746 --> 00:40:17,314
It's to vent his spite.

1104
00:40:17,381 --> 00:40:18,816
Forgetting garlic for vongole pasta

1105
00:40:18,883 --> 00:40:20,718
is like playing soccer
without soccer shoes.

1106
00:40:22,686 --> 00:40:25,189
Garlic has made him spiteful.

1107
00:40:25,256 --> 00:40:27,291
That much garlic?

1108
00:40:27,358 --> 00:40:29,326
<i>Today, I did not forget garlic.</i>

1109
00:40:29,393 --> 00:40:30,828
Whoa, garlic.

1110
00:40:30,895 --> 00:40:31,962
That's too much.

1111
00:40:32,029 --> 00:40:35,433
Did you add that much garlic
to cleanse him and make him human?

1112
00:40:36,934 --> 00:40:39,003
BINGO

1113
00:40:39,069 --> 00:40:40,738
<i>Everyone, I've made it!</i>

1114
00:40:40,805 --> 00:40:42,973
<i>-I've been cleansed!</i>
-He'll be cleansed.

1115
00:40:43,040 --> 00:40:45,309
I want to cleanse him
and let him go more viral.

1116
00:40:45,643 --> 00:40:47,211
4. STRAIN OUT THE VENUS CLAM
AND KEEP THE BROTH

1117
00:40:47,278 --> 00:40:49,680
He's actually making vongole pasta.

1118
00:40:50,114 --> 00:40:52,216
ADD VENUS CLAM BROTH

1119
00:40:52,283 --> 00:40:54,452
Vongole pasta is my favorite.

1120
00:40:55,853 --> 00:40:56,954
SHAKING

1121
00:40:57,021 --> 00:41:01,592
4. MIX WHITE BALSAMIC, OLIVE OIL,
SALT, AND PEPPER TO MAKE TARTAR SAUCE

1122
00:41:01,659 --> 00:41:02,660
Vinaigrette?

1123
00:41:02,726 --> 00:41:04,261
Don't let water get in there.

1124
00:41:04,328 --> 00:41:06,664
-Okay.
-Hold the inner bowl.

1125
00:41:06,730 --> 00:41:08,165
It's slowly hardening.

1126
00:41:08,232 --> 00:41:10,901
What are Ho-young and Moon-jung up to?

1127
00:41:10,968 --> 00:41:13,237
-Hold it.
-It's like a regular old house.

1128
00:41:13,304 --> 00:41:14,672
It's hardening.

1129
00:41:14,738 --> 00:41:19,677
The jelly hardens faster
if you stir it to cool it evenly.

1130
00:41:19,743 --> 00:41:22,179
-It's almost done.
-Really?

1131
00:41:22,246 --> 00:41:23,747
STARTS TO THICKEN

1132
00:41:23,814 --> 00:41:26,550
Sam was usually sitting right there.

1133
00:41:26,617 --> 00:41:29,220
I guess they've drifted apart.

1134
00:41:29,286 --> 00:41:31,589
They couldn't even win as a team.

1135
00:41:31,655 --> 00:41:35,125
I mean, they didn't even get
an offer for a duo ad gig.

1136
00:41:35,192 --> 00:41:37,895
Sam knew that it was a sinking ship.

1137
00:41:38,629 --> 00:41:40,531
-That's good.
-Is this good?

1138
00:41:40,598 --> 00:41:41,432
Thank you.

1139
00:41:42,633 --> 00:41:45,569
-It's done. It looks good.
-It's done.

1140
00:41:46,504 --> 00:41:49,273
He finished making that in seven minutes.

1141
00:41:49,340 --> 00:41:51,909
You usually store it in the fridge
to use it the next day.

1142
00:41:51,976 --> 00:41:54,478
-It takes a day?
-It does.

1143
00:41:54,545 --> 00:41:56,714
The dough must be ready.

1144
00:41:56,780 --> 00:41:58,916
It finished resting.

1145
00:41:58,983 --> 00:42:01,051
-Wait, that's <i>sujebi</i> dough.
-<i>Sujebi?</i>

1146
00:42:01,118 --> 00:42:04,288
Give him a moment.
He'll cut it with a knife.

1147
00:42:04,355 --> 00:42:06,156
He won't pull it with his hands.

1148
00:42:07,091 --> 00:42:08,559
But that's how you make <i>sujebi.</i>

1149
00:42:08,626 --> 00:42:11,562
-Is he making Sung-jun's face?
-He's not picking up a knife!

1150
00:42:11,629 --> 00:42:13,330
-Show him your <i>sujebi.</i>
-He's pulling the dough!

1151
00:42:13,397 --> 00:42:16,400
-Show him your <i>sujebi.</i>
-He's pulling the dough!

1152
00:42:16,767 --> 00:42:18,135
HE PULLED IT OFF!

1153
00:42:19,436 --> 00:42:20,704
It looks wide.

1154
00:42:20,771 --> 00:42:22,239
-He's studying his face.
-Yes.

1155
00:42:22,306 --> 00:42:24,742
He's depicting him as much as possible.

1156
00:42:24,808 --> 00:42:26,343
FORMING HIS FACE

1157
00:42:26,410 --> 00:42:28,178
-It's Sung-jun.
-Yes.

1158
00:42:28,245 --> 00:42:29,647
May I cast my vote now?

1159
00:42:30,214 --> 00:42:31,148
I'M HERE AS A GUEST…

1160
00:42:31,215 --> 00:42:33,884
He continues to study his model.

1161
00:42:33,951 --> 00:42:35,586
The fridge owner feels offended.

1162
00:42:35,653 --> 00:42:36,987
I think I can choose one now.

1163
00:42:37,321 --> 00:42:38,756
WHATEVER

1164
00:42:38,822 --> 00:42:40,257
-He's looking at him.
-He's serious.

1165
00:42:40,724 --> 00:42:42,693
SURFACE AREA, SCANNED

1166
00:42:43,027 --> 00:42:44,929
WIDE AND THICK

1167
00:42:44,995 --> 00:42:46,530
That's his chin, and that was his ear.

1168
00:42:46,597 --> 00:42:49,400
-He's actually making <i>sujebi.</i>
-Is he making my face?

1169
00:42:49,466 --> 00:42:50,534
Don't be mistaken.

1170
00:42:50,601 --> 00:42:52,937
He doesn't have
too many <i>sujebi</i> pieces on his face.

1171
00:42:53,003 --> 00:42:55,072
-That's even worse.
-What are those?

1172
00:42:55,139 --> 00:42:57,207
The <i>sujebi</i> pieces are quite big.

1173
00:42:57,274 --> 00:42:59,577
-They seem a bit too…
-It's…

1174
00:42:59,643 --> 00:43:02,379
Chef Ho-young will probably win today.

1175
00:43:02,446 --> 00:43:05,316
Did you mix the shrimps and the sauce?

1176
00:43:05,382 --> 00:43:06,550
5. MIX SAUCE AND INGREDIENTS

1177
00:43:06,617 --> 00:43:08,319
FINISHED CARABINERO TARTAR!

1178
00:43:09,386 --> 00:43:10,654
SHRIMP INNARDS

1179
00:43:11,221 --> 00:43:16,260
He's grabbing venus clam meat
to blend them.

1180
00:43:16,327 --> 00:43:19,129
6. GET CLAM MEAT
AND BLEND WITH CARABINERO INNARDS

1181
00:43:19,663 --> 00:43:21,231
Did you season that?

1182
00:43:21,298 --> 00:43:23,801
-No, I added shrimp innards.
-I see.

1183
00:43:23,867 --> 00:43:25,069
Red shrimps?

1184
00:43:25,135 --> 00:43:26,437
The innards have so much flavor.

1185
00:43:26,503 --> 00:43:29,106
Even its innards are that red?

1186
00:43:29,173 --> 00:43:32,209
It tastes like <i>gejang </i>in soy sauce.

1187
00:43:32,276 --> 00:43:35,079
-It's that rich in flavor.
-That must be why it's so good.

1188
00:43:35,145 --> 00:43:37,181
Chef Ho-young looks busy.

1189
00:43:37,247 --> 00:43:38,916
7. MIX FRYING POWDER WITH WATER

1190
00:43:39,817 --> 00:43:41,018
NIP THE TIP!

1191
00:43:42,086 --> 00:43:44,421
PUMPKIN FLOWERS FROM THE FRIDGE

1192
00:43:44,488 --> 00:43:46,457
What's Ho-young doing right now?

1193
00:43:46,523 --> 00:43:50,060
I'm stuffing pumpkin flowers
with blended clam and shrimp.

1194
00:43:50,127 --> 00:43:52,463
-That looks so good.
-It does.

1195
00:43:52,529 --> 00:43:54,031
I'll deep-fry these later.

1196
00:43:54,098 --> 00:43:56,567
-Deep-fry those? Wait.
-There's no way that's bad.

1197
00:43:56,634 --> 00:43:59,269
-He's stuffing them.
-I love those kinds of dishes.

1198
00:43:59,336 --> 00:44:01,071
He's making two, so is one for me?

1199
00:44:01,138 --> 00:44:03,140
Come on. He's not going to make just two.

1200
00:44:03,207 --> 00:44:05,342
He's putting a lot of work into those.

1201
00:44:05,409 --> 00:44:08,045
We'll see why those are so expensive.

1202
00:44:08,112 --> 00:44:10,114
It may be the best bite of the year.

1203
00:44:10,180 --> 00:44:12,349
-It's that good?
-It'll make a huge impact.

1204
00:44:12,416 --> 00:44:14,118
Five and a half minutes.

1205
00:44:14,551 --> 00:44:16,987
GRABBING JUST THE VENUS CLAM MEAT

1206
00:44:17,054 --> 00:44:18,856
Those are meaty.

1207
00:44:20,290 --> 00:44:21,258
It's hot.

1208
00:44:21,325 --> 00:44:22,526
-Is it hot?
-It's hot?

1209
00:44:22,593 --> 00:44:24,962
Choi Hyun-suk is in pain!

1210
00:44:25,029 --> 00:44:28,065
He rarely shows that something's too hot.

1211
00:44:29,066 --> 00:44:30,267
Butter?

1212
00:44:30,334 --> 00:44:31,502
Garlic and butter.

1213
00:44:31,568 --> 00:44:32,770
5. ADD CHOPPED ARUGULA

1214
00:44:32,836 --> 00:44:35,806
Butter isn't used
in traditional vongole pasta.

1215
00:44:36,306 --> 00:44:37,174
TRUE

1216
00:44:37,241 --> 00:44:39,743
-I see.
-It can feel a bit too greasy.

1217
00:44:39,810 --> 00:44:42,413
-Sung-ju, can you report from there?
-Sure.

1218
00:44:42,479 --> 00:44:44,548
Let me go see how things are going.

1219
00:44:44,982 --> 00:44:46,016
INTO THE OIL

1220
00:44:46,083 --> 00:44:47,384
That looks so good.

1221
00:44:47,451 --> 00:44:49,620
