00:53:34,711 --> 00:53:36,613
It tasted too perfect.

1465
00:53:36,680 --> 00:53:38,381
CURIOUS

1466
00:53:38,448 --> 00:53:40,584
Ho-young is up next.

1467
00:53:41,051 --> 00:53:45,655
A DISH REPRESENTING
SUNG-JUN'S DAZZLING NATURE

1468
00:53:46,623 --> 00:53:48,725
FULL OF EXPENSIVE SEAFOOD

1469
00:53:48,792 --> 00:53:51,394
-What did you depict?
-It's a person.

1470
00:53:51,461 --> 00:53:54,264
It's Sung-jun and his short limbs.

1471
00:53:54,664 --> 00:53:56,866
WAS THIS AN INSULT ROUND?

1472
00:53:57,167 --> 00:53:58,702
PERFECT TO MAKE HIM GO VIRAL!

1473
00:53:58,768 --> 00:54:00,804
The flowers are the legs,

1474
00:54:00,870 --> 00:54:03,940
-and the claws are the short arms.
-The legs are way too short.

1475
00:54:05,542 --> 00:54:07,010
Short limbs? Dang it.

1476
00:54:07,077 --> 00:54:08,278
I have short limbs too.

1477
00:54:08,345 --> 00:54:10,614
It's just that
his limbs are stuck deep in his body!

1478
00:54:11,448 --> 00:54:12,282
"Deep in his body."

1479
00:54:12,782 --> 00:54:14,284
THROWING AMAZING INSULTS

1480
00:54:14,351 --> 00:54:16,319
He may have short limbs,

1481
00:54:16,386 --> 00:54:20,156
but his dishes sparkle brightly
like those gems in the middle.

1482
00:54:20,223 --> 00:54:21,658
That's why those are in the center.

1483
00:54:21,725 --> 00:54:23,360
I see.

1484
00:54:23,426 --> 00:54:25,695
-After hearing that, I can see something.
-What is it?

1485
00:54:26,363 --> 00:54:27,464
I've lived the wrong life.

1486
00:54:27,530 --> 00:54:29,366
What's up?

1487
00:54:29,432 --> 00:54:31,735
-It still has a message.
-You're sparkling.

1488
00:54:31,801 --> 00:54:33,536
It's the Chuseok special,

1489
00:54:33,603 --> 00:54:36,606
and both dishes were made
with incredible insults.

1490
00:54:36,673 --> 00:54:40,710
I'm glad it meant something to him.

1491
00:54:40,777 --> 00:54:44,447
But the dish itself
is something I truly love.

1492
00:54:44,514 --> 00:54:48,118
-The pumpkin flower.
-Pumpkin flower with clams and shrimps.

1493
00:54:48,184 --> 00:54:51,621
<i>I blended red shrimp innards</i>
<i>and clam meat,</i>

1494
00:54:51,688 --> 00:54:52,756
<i>then filled the flowers with it.</i>

1495
00:54:54,024 --> 00:54:56,660
SAVORING THE FLAVOR

1496
00:54:56,726 --> 00:54:57,961
He's in deep thought.

1497
00:55:00,096 --> 00:55:01,931
It's the kind of flavor I love the most.

1498
00:55:01,998 --> 00:55:04,701
The mix of richness in shrimp innards

1499
00:55:04,768 --> 00:55:06,136
and the crunchiness of the fries,

1500
00:55:06,202 --> 00:55:09,039
along with the soft pumpkin flower.

1501
00:55:09,105 --> 00:55:11,341
It's too perfect.

1502
00:55:11,675 --> 00:55:13,443
GULP

1503
00:55:13,510 --> 00:55:17,314
When you eat the body,
scoop everything up and top it with jelly.

1504
00:55:17,380 --> 00:55:19,516
-Whoa.
-He topped it with jelly.

1505
00:55:19,582 --> 00:55:21,651
It was a bit sour when I tried it.

1506
00:55:21,718 --> 00:55:25,588
<i>It goes well with the sauce underneath.</i>
<i>It'll mix nicely with shrimp's sweetness.</i>

1507
00:55:25,655 --> 00:55:27,657
I love all carabinero dishes,

1508
00:55:27,724 --> 00:55:30,627
but my favorite is eating it raw,
just like this tartar.

1509
00:55:31,961 --> 00:55:33,563
SMELLS IT FIRST

1510
00:55:33,630 --> 00:55:35,465
AND THEN A BIG BITE

1511
00:55:37,634 --> 00:55:39,336
HIS FOREHEAD WILL GET DIRTY FROM HIS HAND

1512
00:55:39,402 --> 00:55:41,705
-He's an eyesore.
-He's eating it in that pose.

1513
00:55:41,771 --> 00:55:43,640
This is driving me insane.

1514
00:55:43,707 --> 00:55:45,108
Tell us what it's like.

1515
00:55:45,175 --> 00:55:46,776
Carabineros already come

1516
00:55:46,843 --> 00:55:49,612
with this umami and sweetness.

1517
00:55:49,679 --> 00:55:52,916
So the soy sauce
and the sour note go well with that.

1518
00:55:52,982 --> 00:55:55,618
Also, he made the jelly
with clam broth, right?

1519
00:55:55,685 --> 00:55:57,420
<i>So the depth is insane.</i>

1520
00:55:57,487 --> 00:55:58,688
<i>But the key here</i>

1521
00:55:58,755 --> 00:56:00,657
is the Shine Muscat.

1522
00:56:00,724 --> 00:56:03,059
-That adds more sweetness.
-It must've been effective.

1523
00:56:03,126 --> 00:56:05,662
The sourness, sweetness,
saltiness, and umami

1524
00:56:05,729 --> 00:56:07,230
join forces and slap my <i>sujebi.</i>

1525
00:56:07,297 --> 00:56:08,598
It slaps your <i>sujebi?</i>

1526
00:56:08,665 --> 00:56:11,000
-It's slapping his cheeks.
-His cheeks.

1527
00:56:12,535 --> 00:56:13,770
Lastly, the shrimp head.

1528
00:56:13,837 --> 00:56:17,207
-Then it's game over.
-I tried that, remember?

1529
00:56:17,273 --> 00:56:19,576
It's salted, so just eat it as is.

1530
00:56:19,642 --> 00:56:21,211
Fried red shrimp head.

1531
00:56:21,277 --> 00:56:22,545
It's the shrimp head.

1532
00:56:22,612 --> 00:56:23,546
CRUNCH

1533
00:56:25,115 --> 00:56:27,484
I can hear how crispy it is.

1534
00:56:29,085 --> 00:56:30,286
HAGGARD

1535
00:56:31,254 --> 00:56:33,323
He's mixing it with the Shine Muscat.

1536
00:56:34,991 --> 00:56:36,126
Mmm.

1537
00:56:36,192 --> 00:56:37,894
SHAKING HEAD

1538
00:56:38,461 --> 00:56:39,796
-He mooed.
-He notices the camera.

1539
00:56:40,096 --> 00:56:41,865
AUTOMATICALLY AMAZED

1540
00:56:41,931 --> 00:56:43,199
-Are you a cow?
-Can I finish this?

1541
00:56:43,266 --> 00:56:44,367
Hey.

1542
00:56:44,701 --> 00:56:46,836
NAM-NO LOSES IT…

1543
00:56:46,903 --> 00:56:49,172
Let's share. Food is all about sharing.

1544
00:56:49,239 --> 00:56:50,440
Food is about sharing?

1545
00:56:51,775 --> 00:56:52,675
Man.

1546
00:56:53,777 --> 00:56:56,446
This is what I call "right up my alley."

1547
00:56:56,513 --> 00:56:57,747
HAPPY, SAD

1548
00:56:57,814 --> 00:57:00,283
He used expensive ingredients,
so it had to be good.

1549
00:57:00,350 --> 00:57:02,552
So I already had high expectations.

1550
00:57:02,619 --> 00:57:03,620
But he surpassed it all.

1551
00:57:05,422 --> 00:57:09,659
-It was surely a round between my masters.
-Right. They were both your masters.

1552
00:57:09,726 --> 00:57:11,261
-I'll have to think.
-Do you want to?

1553
00:57:11,327 --> 00:57:12,896
-Chef Nam-no has to try it too.
-All right.

1554
00:57:12,962 --> 00:57:16,499
-Wait there. Can you push those?
-Nam-no's turn.

1555
00:57:16,566 --> 00:57:19,068
-Something's coming. Hyun-suk's here.
-Something's here.

1556
00:57:19,135 --> 00:57:20,503
THE LONG-LIMBED GRANDPA WALKS OVER

1557
00:57:20,570 --> 00:57:22,705
I didn't want him to eat alone
because we had two guests.

1558
00:57:22,772 --> 00:57:24,808
-You made another plate?
-Just the pasta.

1559
00:57:24,874 --> 00:57:25,975
PASTA JUST FOR NAM-NO

1560
00:57:26,042 --> 00:57:27,410
HA-HA!

1561
00:57:27,477 --> 00:57:30,013
I'm the most pleased at the moment.

1562
00:57:30,079 --> 00:57:31,581
He made a huge portion.

1563
00:57:31,648 --> 00:57:33,783
-Try Chef Hyun-suk's dish first.
-The vongole pasta.

1564
00:57:34,350 --> 00:57:35,652
The <i>sujebi?</i>

1565
00:57:35,718 --> 00:57:38,221
A BITE OF KWON SUNG-JUN'S RIGHT CHEEK

1566
00:57:39,856 --> 00:57:40,957
Eat as much as you like.

1567
00:57:42,258 --> 00:57:43,092
Go ahead.

1568
00:57:44,427 --> 00:57:45,462
Gosh.

1569
00:57:45,995 --> 00:57:47,197
Yes.

1570
00:57:47,964 --> 00:57:50,333
NAM-NO IS HIGH MAINTENANCE

1571
00:57:50,400 --> 00:57:52,202
-Do I look gross?
-Gross?

1572
00:57:52,268 --> 00:57:54,037
-You got green onion.
-A piece of green onion.

1573
00:57:54,103 --> 00:57:55,071
The <i>sujebi</i> texture

1574
00:57:55,138 --> 00:57:57,474
continues to stay resilient in the mouth.

1575
00:57:57,540 --> 00:57:59,709
-It must be firm and chewy.
-Yes.

1576
00:58:00,944 --> 00:58:02,979
He made another plate just for you.

1577
00:58:03,046 --> 00:58:04,447
FINISHES SUNG-JUN'S LEFTOVERS FIRST

1578
00:58:04,514 --> 00:58:06,749
It's a waste. We shouldn't waste food.

1579
00:58:07,750 --> 00:58:09,352
HE'LL NEVER BE PUNISHED FOR WASTING FOOD

1580
00:58:09,419 --> 00:58:11,187
-Why not eat the plate too?
-Okay.

1581
00:58:12,422 --> 00:58:13,690
Eat the plate too.

1582
00:58:14,924 --> 00:58:16,259
Vongole pasta.

1583
00:58:17,627 --> 00:58:20,497
SUCKING IN THE NOODLES AT A HIGH SPEED

1584
00:58:21,164 --> 00:58:23,333
SLURPING WITHOUT CUTTING IT OFF

1585
00:58:23,399 --> 00:58:26,269
You're making my mouth water.

1586
00:58:26,769 --> 00:58:29,339
SUCH AN AMAZING TALENT

1587
00:58:29,772 --> 00:58:32,175
QUIETLY STARING OFF INTO SPACE

1588
00:58:33,076 --> 00:58:35,345
Tell us what it's like.

1589
00:58:35,411 --> 00:58:37,514
I thought he had used too much garlic,

1590
00:58:37,580 --> 00:58:40,550
<i>but it would've been ordinary without it.</i>

1591
00:58:40,617 --> 00:58:42,519
He did add a lot.

1592
00:58:42,585 --> 00:58:43,586
WIPING

1593
00:58:43,820 --> 00:58:44,921
IN A TRANCE

1594
00:58:44,988 --> 00:58:46,589
I thought you got your nails done.

1595
00:58:46,856 --> 00:58:48,525
NAM-NO'S GUARDIAN(?) CAN'T CATCH A BREAK

1596
00:58:48,591 --> 00:58:51,060
He's the best vongole pasta chef in Korea.

1597
00:58:52,729 --> 00:58:53,596
The highest compliment.

1598
00:58:54,063 --> 00:58:55,765
CLEARING THE PLATE

1599
00:58:55,832 --> 00:58:58,268
-You have to eat your dishes too.
-Sorry?

1600
00:58:58,334 --> 00:59:00,470
KWON SUNG-JUN IS GONE FROM THIS WORLD

1601
00:59:00,537 --> 00:59:03,206
Next, Chef Ho-young's dish.

1602
00:59:03,273 --> 00:59:05,074
The umami is saying peekaboo.

1603
00:59:06,009 --> 00:59:06,876
"Peekaboo."

1604
00:59:06,943 --> 00:59:09,045
CHEF JUNG HO-YOUNG'S VIRAL ONE MORE TIME

1605
00:59:09,112 --> 00:59:11,381
This isn't just peekaboo.
It's "peek-a-boop-dee-doo."

1606
00:59:12,315 --> 00:59:13,583
SHRIMP GOES PEEKABOO

1607
00:59:13,850 --> 00:59:15,018
CAN'T BELIEVE THEIR EYES

1608
00:59:15,251 --> 00:59:17,020
EVEN THE HONORARY GUARDIAN FLEES

1609
00:59:17,086 --> 00:59:18,888
IMMENSELY DISPLEASED

1610
00:59:19,355 --> 00:59:20,924
SPEECHLESS

1611
00:59:21,858 --> 00:59:22,825
You'll go viral.

1612
00:59:22,892 --> 00:59:24,894
-Did you do that intentionally?
-Not at all.

1613
00:59:24,961 --> 00:59:27,497
<i>-Did you do that to go viral?</i>
<i>-No, never.</i>

1614
00:59:27,564 --> 00:59:29,632
It's the kind of flavor
that makes you jittery.

1615
00:59:29,966 --> 00:59:31,267
CALM DOWN, NAM-NO…

1616
00:59:31,834 --> 00:59:32,936
I get it.

1617
00:59:33,002 --> 00:59:34,771
Kwon Sung-jun's head.

1618
00:59:34,837 --> 00:59:35,738
CALMING DOWN WITH THE HEAD

1619
00:59:36,372 --> 00:59:37,273
FINISHES IT IN ONE BITE

1620
00:59:37,340 --> 00:59:38,908
So cruel.

1621
00:59:38,975 --> 00:59:41,945
It's fun to watch his <i>mukbang.</i>

1622
00:59:42,011 --> 00:59:42,979
He eats well.

1623
00:59:43,046 --> 00:59:45,181
All eyes are on him. Hey.

1624
00:59:45,248 --> 00:59:47,016
THIS DESERVES AN APPLAUSE

1625
00:59:47,083 --> 00:59:49,185
-Nam-no.
-I get what you mean.

1626
00:59:49,252 --> 00:59:51,955
I thought Chef Sung-jun was exaggerating.

1627
00:59:52,021 --> 00:59:54,157
-Come on.
-About the shrimps.

1628
00:59:54,223 --> 00:59:56,459
These are the most expensive shrimps
in the world,

1629
00:59:56,526 --> 00:59:58,728
but it's gone way past that.

1630
01:00:01,331 --> 01:00:04,367
AGAIN, FINISHES WITHOUT LEAVING A DROP

1631
01:00:04,434 --> 01:00:06,502
It's time to make a decision.

1632
01:00:06,569 --> 01:00:08,404
Kwon Sung-jun's choice.

1633
01:00:08,471 --> 01:00:11,341
Which side will he pick?

1634
01:00:11,407 --> 01:00:14,143
Press one for Jung Ho-young

1635
01:00:14,210 --> 01:00:15,979
and two for Choi Hyun-suk.

1636
01:00:16,779 --> 01:00:18,948
Make your decision and press the button.

1637
01:00:19,515 --> 01:00:22,452
One for Ho-young, two for Hyun-suk.

1638
01:00:22,518 --> 01:00:24,020
Kwon Sung-jun's choice.

1639
01:00:24,087 --> 01:00:27,190
Who will rise as the winner?

1640
01:00:27,256 --> 01:00:30,159
Let's find out. Show us!

1641
01:00:30,693 --> 01:00:33,663
Everyone, I've Done It! I've Gone Viral!

1642
01:00:33,730 --> 01:00:36,032
Did Hyun-suk get more attention?

1643
01:00:36,099 --> 01:00:38,234
Or was it Ho-young?

1644
01:00:38,301 --> 01:00:42,639
Which dish does Sung-jun want more?

1645
01:00:43,172 --> 01:00:44,874
Is it Hyun-suk

1646
01:00:44,941 --> 01:00:46,309
or Ho-young?

1647
01:00:46,843 --> 01:00:47,877
Who's the winner?

1648
01:00:51,714 --> 01:00:53,483
JUNG HO-YOUNG WINS

1649
01:00:53,549 --> 01:00:54,617
Jung Ho-young wins!

1650
01:00:54,851 --> 01:00:56,219
VIRAL ONE MORE TIME WINS

1651
01:00:56,285 --> 01:00:57,420
Jung Ho-young wins!

1652
01:00:59,122 --> 01:01:00,056
WALKING ON EGGSHELLS

1653
01:01:00,123 --> 01:01:02,392
Sung-jun chose Ho-young's dish.

1654
01:01:02,458 --> 01:01:06,362
Both dishes were incredibly delicious.

1655
01:01:06,429 --> 01:01:09,298
But the best way to get more clicks

1656
01:01:09,365 --> 01:01:12,835
on video or social media platforms
is using expensive ingredients.

1657
01:01:13,970 --> 01:01:15,872
In that aspect,

1658
01:01:15,938 --> 01:01:19,275
I thought Chef Ho-young had
the advantage with the ingredients.

1659
01:01:19,342 --> 01:01:21,411
I thought I could bait people

1660
01:01:21,477 --> 01:01:24,514
<i>-with the expensive shrimps.</i>
<i>-The red shrimps.</i>

1661
01:01:24,580 --> 01:01:26,816
Why didn't you just ask
for an expensive dish?

1662
01:01:28,251 --> 01:01:29,452
Huh?

1663
01:01:29,519 --> 01:01:31,087
THE GRANDPA'S MAD!

1664
01:01:31,421 --> 01:01:33,222
WHAT YOU SAID IS RIGHT

1665
01:01:33,289 --> 01:01:34,924
The <i>sujebi</i> triggered you, right?

1666
01:01:35,491 --> 01:01:37,360
-Stop him.
-It's a good day.

1667
01:01:37,427 --> 01:01:40,229
-It's a great day. Calm down, Hyun-suk.
-He's right.

1668
01:01:40,296 --> 01:01:41,531
For the first time on the show,

1669
01:01:41,597 --> 01:01:44,801
you saw the chef
protesting against the guest.

1670
01:01:44,867 --> 01:01:46,803
"Why didn't you just ask
for an expensive dish?"

1671
01:01:46,869 --> 01:01:48,771
It's not easy to choose.

1672
01:01:48,838 --> 01:01:51,240
Chef Ho-young, you got the star.

1673
01:01:51,307 --> 01:01:53,242
I never want to lose whenever the order

1674
01:01:53,309 --> 01:01:54,777
is about social media.

1675
01:01:56,412 --> 01:01:57,714
That was my attitude.

1676
01:01:57,780 --> 01:01:59,849
Ho-young the social media addict.

1677
01:01:59,916 --> 01:02:02,251
-That's how I got that star.
-I see.

1678
01:02:02,318 --> 01:02:06,622
Ho-young wins the first round.
Congratulations!

1679
01:02:06,689 --> 01:02:09,992
<i>-Everyone, I've done it. I got the star!</i>
-The addict takes the star.

1680
01:02:10,059 --> 01:02:12,895
That's Ho-young's ninth star.

1681
01:02:12,962 --> 01:02:14,397
-Congratulations!
-Congrats!

1682
01:02:14,797 --> 01:02:15,832
CONGRATULATIONS

1683
01:02:15,898 --> 01:02:17,366
Ho-young's ninth star!

1684
01:02:17,967 --> 01:02:19,102
DURING THE BREAK

1685
01:02:19,635 --> 01:02:21,771
KWON SUNG-JUN'S FRIDGE

1686
01:02:23,172 --> 01:02:25,608
-Can I have a piece of cheese?
-Sure.

1687
01:02:26,309 --> 01:02:28,478
I want those corn puffs.

1688
01:02:28,845 --> 01:02:31,013
RUNNING

1689
01:02:31,481 --> 01:02:33,883
CORN PUFFS ACQUIRED

1690
01:02:33,950 --> 01:02:35,952
It's glazed with sugar.

1691
01:02:36,018 --> 01:02:37,019
LET'S EAT IT TOGETHER

1692
01:02:37,086 --> 01:02:37,987
Okay.

1693
01:02:38,621 --> 01:02:39,655
These are delicious.

1694
01:02:39,722 --> 01:02:41,824
It's fine, we're all cast members.

1695
01:02:41,891 --> 01:02:45,161
This is the fun of these special episodes.

1696
01:02:48,631 --> 01:02:51,100
POURING

1697
01:02:52,201 --> 01:02:54,203
HEHE♥

1698
01:02:54,904 --> 01:02:56,839
YUM

1699
01:02:56,906 --> 01:02:58,975
We're all comfortably stealing food
because we're friends.

1700
01:02:59,809 --> 01:03:00,977
SUDDENLY EATING CHEESE

1701
01:03:01,043 --> 01:03:05,815
<i>The second round of cook-off</i>
<i>is played with Nam-no's ingredients.</i>

1702
01:03:05,882 --> 01:03:06,949
-Huh?
-Our hottest two,

1703
01:03:07,016 --> 01:03:09,719
-He's shocked.
-…Son Jong-won and Park Eun-yeong,

1704
01:03:09,786 --> 01:03:12,155
-Wait, what? Why is she so tall?
-…versus the OuDi brothers

1705
01:03:12,221 --> 01:03:16,092
-of the show, Sam Kim and Kim Poong.
-What?

1706
01:03:16,159 --> 01:03:17,493
What does OuDi mean?

1707
01:03:17,560 --> 01:03:22,298
Our friendship will last until we die.

1708
01:03:22,365 --> 01:03:24,667
How did Eun-yeong suddenly grow to 174 cm?

1709
01:03:25,501 --> 01:03:27,270
-She is. She's taller.
-It doesn't suit her.

1710
01:03:27,336 --> 01:03:29,138
-She's in the 150 cm range.
-You aren't tall.

1711
01:03:29,205 --> 01:03:31,774
The counter for this set

1712
01:03:31,841 --> 01:03:33,743
is quite high, actually.

1713
01:03:33,810 --> 01:03:36,879
But I need to be a little taller
to cook easier,

1714
01:03:36,946 --> 01:03:39,916
-so I decided to stand up here.
-Is she making dough?

1715
01:03:39,982 --> 01:03:44,053
Poong and Sam have been
good friends for over a decade.

1716
01:03:44,120 --> 01:03:45,521
We got a tip from Ho-young.

1717
01:03:45,588 --> 01:03:47,990
There's already a conflict
between Sam and Poong?

1718
01:03:48,057 --> 01:03:50,126
-Really?
-What conflict?

1719
01:03:50,193 --> 01:03:52,161
Poong's trying to lead the round,

1720
01:03:52,228 --> 01:03:55,031
and Sam is reluctantly playing along.

1721
01:03:55,665 --> 01:03:58,734
But he might end up losing it
within those 15 minutes.

1722
01:03:59,468 --> 01:04:01,938
But he looks too kind.

1723
01:04:02,004 --> 01:04:04,540
It's my first time
teaming up with Poong in a decade.

1724
01:04:04,607 --> 01:04:07,643
It turns out that he also had
a philosophy about cooking.

1725
01:04:09,178 --> 01:04:11,447
-You didn't know?
-He does.

1726
01:04:11,514 --> 01:04:13,616
I thought he just did random things,

1727
01:04:13,683 --> 01:04:15,251
but after talking to him,

1728
01:04:15,318 --> 01:04:17,053
I noticed that he had a philosophy.

1729
01:04:17,119 --> 01:04:20,056
Sam always loses
when he plays a team round.

1730
01:04:20,122 --> 01:04:21,457
LOST EVERY SINGLE TIME

1731
01:04:21,524 --> 01:04:22,692
What a shame.

1732
01:04:22,758 --> 01:04:25,127
-I know exactly why.
-You do?

1733
01:04:25,194 --> 01:04:27,396
The only person
Sam has ever teamed up with

1734
01:04:27,463 --> 01:04:29,298
-is Chef Ho-young.
-Just me?

1735
01:04:29,365 --> 01:04:31,200
-That's true.
-It may be him.

1736
01:04:31,267 --> 01:04:32,101
That's right.

1737
01:04:32,168 --> 01:04:35,304
-I don't think they have good teamwork.
-They don't?

1738
01:04:35,371 --> 01:04:37,006
-No.
-He's right.

1739
01:04:37,073 --> 01:04:40,910
Sam and Ho-young
are after the Best Couple Award.

1740
01:04:40,977 --> 01:04:44,113
Honestly, I think it's just Chef Ho-young.

1741
01:04:44,180 --> 01:04:46,983
-He doesn't seem to care.
-It wasn't Sam's idea?

1742
01:04:47,049 --> 01:04:48,584
I'm not very interested.

1743
01:04:48,651 --> 01:04:50,553
I'm not very interested.

1744
01:04:51,821 --> 01:04:53,389
It was one-sided.

1745
01:04:53,456 --> 01:04:54,724
In this round,

1746
01:04:54,790 --> 01:04:57,460
you four will cook just for Nam-no.

1747
01:04:57,526 --> 01:04:59,095
Oh, right. It's my turn.

1748
01:04:59,161 --> 01:05:01,898
Chef Eun-yeong,
you know him well, don't you?

1749
01:05:01,964 --> 01:05:04,867
My dear Nam-no has a strong stomach
trained with rich Chinese flavors

1750
01:05:04,934 --> 01:05:06,702
-and greasiness.
-What's with her?

1751
01:05:06,769 --> 01:05:10,706
I can capture his appetite
with greasy Chinese cuisine.

1752
01:05:11,574 --> 01:05:13,342
-I'm shocked.
-"My dear Nam-no…"

1753
01:05:13,409 --> 01:05:15,011
She knows Nam-no.

1754
01:05:15,077 --> 01:05:17,680
-Poong, you also know him well.
-Actually,

1755
01:05:17,747 --> 01:05:19,582
even when people criticized

1756
01:05:19,649 --> 01:05:21,784
and denounced the dishes I made,

1757
01:05:21,851 --> 01:05:24,186
-he always said it was good.
-That's true.

1758
01:05:24,253 --> 01:05:25,588
<i>He always said that.</i>

1759
01:05:25,655 --> 01:05:27,690
-It's good. It's just for me.
<i>-I even began to think that…</i>

1760
01:05:27,757 --> 01:05:29,525
-It's good.
<i>-he might love me.</i>

1761
01:05:29,592 --> 01:05:32,461
He likes anything
and everything that I make.

1762
01:05:32,528 --> 01:05:35,598
So if I make something I want to,
it'll be something he likes.

1763
01:05:35,665 --> 01:05:37,667
-Is something burning? I can smell it.
-It smells burnt.

1764
01:05:38,234 --> 01:05:39,835
My dishcloth. But it's all right now.

1765
01:05:40,403 --> 01:05:41,237
Huh?

1766
01:05:41,304 --> 01:05:43,372
-Your dishcloth burned?
-I heard the sound.

1767
01:05:43,439 --> 01:05:45,641
-It's burnt.
-The dishcloth burned.

1768
01:05:45,708 --> 01:05:47,343
-Was it you?
-No.

1769
01:05:47,410 --> 01:05:49,545
It might have been Sam.

1770
01:05:49,812 --> 01:05:51,314
HIS SUSPICIOUS CANINE

1771
01:05:51,380 --> 01:05:54,216
Before, it was in this corner.

1772
01:05:54,283 --> 01:05:56,585
-It couldn't have burnt.
-No.

1773
01:05:56,652 --> 01:05:58,888
See if it has canine marks.

1774
01:05:58,955 --> 01:06:02,558
-I think I can see it.
-Everyone is suspicious of him.

1775
01:06:02,625 --> 01:06:05,261
-Look at him.
-I didn't even go near that.

1776
01:06:05,328 --> 01:06:07,463
-I didn't go there.
-He could've left it before.

1777
01:06:07,530 --> 01:06:08,564
WHAT'S THE TRUTH?

1778
01:06:09,398 --> 01:06:11,434
POONG & SAM'S INGREDIENTS:
JOKBAL, INSIDE SKIRT, THIN SKIRT

1779
01:06:11,500 --> 01:06:13,569
SWEET SHRIMP, SHRIMP RAMYEON,
NAPA CABBAGE, HAPJAJANG, AND MORE

1780
01:06:13,636 --> 01:06:16,839
Sam and Poong, what are you two making?

1781
01:06:16,906 --> 01:06:19,475
Here's the name of our dish.

1782
01:06:19,542 --> 01:06:21,143
-Lots of…
-Incentives…

1783
01:06:21,210 --> 01:06:22,778
-from Poong and Sam.
-from Poong and Sam.

1784
01:06:22,845 --> 01:06:25,581
I see. Poong and Sam.

1785
01:06:25,648 --> 01:06:29,452
We're going to make such a huge serving

1786
01:06:29,518 --> 01:06:32,822
to make him feel like
he's receiving a huge incentive.

1787
01:06:32,888 --> 01:06:34,323
Also, Chef Nam-no

1788
01:06:34,390 --> 01:06:36,258
-really loves veggies too.
-Yes.

1789
01:06:36,325 --> 01:06:37,159
I love it.

1790
01:06:37,226 --> 01:06:40,096
We'll use the napa cabbage

1791
01:06:40,162 --> 01:06:43,599
and turn it into a huge flower,

1792
01:06:43,666 --> 01:06:47,169
-then top it with <i>jokbal.</i>
-You're using that?

1793
01:06:47,236 --> 01:06:51,640
I'll stir-fry it, boil it, steam it,
then put it on top,

1794
01:06:51,707 --> 01:06:53,976
so it'll look like a steamed dish.

1795
01:06:54,043 --> 01:06:57,713
Also, Nam-no loves noodles.

1796
01:06:57,780 --> 01:06:59,015
I go crazy for it.

1797
01:06:59,081 --> 01:07:02,551
We're thinking of making
a new kind of noodles.

1798
01:07:02,618 --> 01:07:04,720
-Are you making everything?
-No.

1799
01:07:04,787 --> 01:07:07,390
I laid down these ideas,

1800
01:07:07,456 --> 01:07:09,091
-and he said it's not so bad.
-It's not.

1801
01:07:09,158 --> 01:07:12,028
After all, it's either go big or go home.

1802
01:07:12,395 --> 01:07:13,396
HE SEEMS TO HAVE GIVEN UP…

1803
01:07:13,462 --> 01:07:17,066
-It'll either be funny or good.
-All right.

1804
01:07:17,900 --> 01:07:19,935
JONG-WON & EUN-YEONG'S INGREDIENTS:
JOKBAL, INSIDE SKIRT, MEAT DUMPLING

1805
01:07:20,002 --> 01:07:22,071
KIMCHI DUMPLING, SWEET SHRIMP,
SHRIMP RAMYEON, NOODLES, AND MORE

1806
01:07:22,872 --> 01:07:25,341
The name of our dish is…

1807
01:07:25,408 --> 01:07:26,342
Even Nam-no Will…

1808
01:07:26,409 --> 01:07:27,476
Feel Full When We Dump…

1809
01:07:27,543 --> 01:07:29,378
-…This Dumpling on Him.
-…This Dumpling on Him.

1810
01:07:30,379 --> 01:07:32,481
Are you making dumplings?

1811
01:07:32,548 --> 01:07:35,084
Yes, we prepared a dumpling.

1812
01:07:35,151 --> 01:07:38,788
Tiny dumplings
are never enough to satisfy him.

1813
01:07:38,854 --> 01:07:40,556
So we'll make one huge dumpling.

1814
01:07:40,623 --> 01:07:42,992
-I love it.
-And we'll fill it with three ingredients.

1815
01:07:43,059 --> 01:07:45,361
So we've prepared a new dumpling dish

1816
01:07:45,428 --> 01:07:46,962
with the ingredients he has.

1817
01:07:47,029 --> 01:07:48,898
We'll also prepare some sauce,

1818
01:07:48,964 --> 01:07:51,834
so he can eat it with the dumpling.

1819
01:07:51,901 --> 01:07:54,437
So this incentive will come
with a vacation to China.

1820
01:07:56,238 --> 01:07:57,073
Even a vacation?

1821
01:07:57,139 --> 01:07:58,507
-One dumpling?
-One.

1822
01:07:58,574 --> 01:07:59,675
-One?
-And one sauce.

1823
01:07:59,742 --> 01:08:00,943
A single dumpling?

1824
01:08:01,010 --> 01:08:03,646
What did Chef Nam-no say earlier?

1825
01:08:03,712 --> 01:08:04,980
-Finger food?
-Finger food.

1826
01:08:05,047 --> 01:08:07,483
I was quite triggered when he said that.

1827
01:08:07,550 --> 01:08:08,684
He got triggered.

1828
01:08:08,751 --> 01:08:12,354
I'll prove that I can also eat a lot
and make huge portions.

1829
01:08:12,788 --> 01:08:13,789
VERY PLEASED

1830
01:08:13,856 --> 01:08:15,591
-Very good.
-All right.

1831
01:08:15,658 --> 01:08:17,193
And now,

1832
01:08:17,259 --> 01:08:20,362
let us begin the cook-off for Chef Nam-no.

1833
01:08:20,429 --> 01:08:22,431
"Pay Stub? Nonsense.

1834
01:08:22,498 --> 01:08:24,767
We'll give you incentives too."

1835
01:08:24,834 --> 01:08:27,103
A word from Team Sam-Poong.

1836
01:08:27,169 --> 01:08:29,338
"Incentives? Nonsense.

1837
01:08:29,405 --> 01:08:31,240
We'll send you on a vacation too."

1838
01:08:31,307 --> 01:08:33,209
Another word from Team Son-Park.

1839
01:08:33,275 --> 01:08:38,114
Which one of the chefs
will fill up Nam-no's stomach?

1840
01:08:38,180 --> 01:08:42,251
Let the 15-minute cook-off begin!

1841
01:08:43,319 --> 01:08:44,553
LET'S GO!

1842
01:08:45,154 --> 01:08:46,088
HELPING OUT

1843
01:08:46,155 --> 01:08:48,824
I'm looking forward
to seeing these new teams.

1844
01:08:48,891 --> 01:08:50,259
Whoa. You're tall.

1845
01:08:50,326 --> 01:08:52,161
Eun-yeong continues to keep her height.

1846
01:08:52,228 --> 01:08:55,030
-Is she wearing special shoes?
-She's not keeping it.

1847
01:08:55,097 --> 01:08:57,133
She shrinks and rises again.

1848
01:08:57,867 --> 01:08:58,701
SHRINK

1849
01:08:59,468 --> 01:09:00,302
RISE

1850
01:09:00,369 --> 01:09:04,540
She's like those people who walk around
in platform shoes at amusement parks.

1851
01:09:05,140 --> 01:09:06,275
POONG'S CHILI OIL

1852
01:09:06,342 --> 01:09:07,510
Green onion oil.

1853
01:09:07,576 --> 01:09:09,378
He's starting with chili oil, as always.

1854
01:09:09,445 --> 01:09:11,313
-He always has to make it.
-Yes.

1855
01:09:11,380 --> 01:09:12,882
Nam-no loves my chili oil.

1856
01:09:12,948 --> 01:09:13,883
That's true.

1857
01:09:13,949 --> 01:09:16,285
It smells so fragrant.

1858
01:09:16,352 --> 01:09:18,554
They're playing different roles.

1859
01:09:18,621 --> 01:09:21,257
Poong and Sam are taking turns.

1860
01:09:21,323 --> 01:09:23,025
-Okay.
-Do we put the <i>jokbal</i> in now?

1861
01:09:23,092 --> 01:09:23,926
Yes.

1862
01:09:23,993 --> 01:09:26,695
-Eun-yeong seems to be kneading dough.
-I am.

1863
01:09:26,762 --> 01:09:28,397
-For the dumpling?
-You're right.

1864
01:09:28,464 --> 01:09:30,699
-The dumpling skin.
-Chinese kitchen knife.

1865
01:09:30,766 --> 01:09:32,301
Is that Jong-won?

1866
01:09:32,368 --> 01:09:34,303
I'm Eun-yeong's support today,

1867
01:09:34,370 --> 01:09:35,704
so I'm using the Chinese knife.

1868
01:09:35,771 --> 01:09:37,873
Chef Jong-won is using the Chinese knife.

1869
01:09:37,940 --> 01:09:39,041
He's Eun-yeong's support.

1870
01:09:39,341 --> 01:09:40,809
2. SALT CHOPPED CABBAGE

1871
01:09:41,043 --> 01:09:41,877
JOKBAL

1872
01:09:41,944 --> 01:09:43,879
<i>-Jokbal.</i>
-Are you boiling that?

1873
01:09:43,946 --> 01:09:45,114
-Yes.
-The bones too?

1874
01:09:45,181 --> 01:09:46,649
-Hasn't it been cooked?
-Yes.

1875
01:09:46,715 --> 01:09:48,450
He threw in the bones too.

1876
01:09:48,517 --> 01:09:50,119
He might be making broth.

1877
01:09:50,185 --> 01:09:51,687
By using the bones?

1878
01:09:51,754 --> 01:09:52,988
-Can you make broth with that?
-Wait.

1879
01:09:53,055 --> 01:09:54,723
-You can.
-I added the meat and the bones.

1880
01:09:54,790 --> 01:09:56,325
I'm using the actual meat.

1881
01:09:56,392 --> 01:09:57,359
I KNEW IT

1882
01:09:57,426 --> 01:09:59,828
-He's trying to make it tender.
-I'm cooking it again

1883
01:09:59,895 --> 01:10:01,330
to take advantage of the texture.

1884
01:10:01,397 --> 01:10:03,065
2. BOIL JOKBAL
IN ONION AND GREEN ONION BROTH

1885
01:10:03,132 --> 01:10:05,601
Eun-yeong must be
making the dumpling skin,

1886
01:10:05,668 --> 01:10:09,405
and Chef Jong-won seems to be
making the stuffing.

1887
01:10:09,471 --> 01:10:13,108
Don't you think one dumpling
is too little for Nam-no?

1888
01:10:13,175 --> 01:10:16,245
The skin will thin out and get bigger.

1889
01:10:16,812 --> 01:10:18,547
-Once she rolls it out…
-It'll be huge.

1890
01:10:18,614 --> 01:10:21,317
-Are you making one dumpling?
-Really?

1891
01:10:21,383 --> 01:10:23,652
-Just one.
-One big one.

1892
01:10:23,719 --> 01:10:25,254
But the dough is so thick.

1893
01:10:25,754 --> 01:10:27,523
GET BIGGER!

1894
01:10:27,590 --> 01:10:29,592
You're flattening it
like actual dumpling skin.

1895
01:10:29,658 --> 01:10:30,793
She's good.

1896
01:10:30,859 --> 01:10:33,929
I'm not sure if it'll get cooked fully.

1897
01:10:33,996 --> 01:10:38,100
Yes, there must be a reason
why the doughs come in smaller sizes.

1898
01:10:38,167 --> 01:10:40,769
-First, it may not cook thoroughly.
-Right.

1899
01:10:40,836 --> 01:10:41,971
Hurry up, Sam.

1900
01:10:42,037 --> 01:10:43,772
-Take a look at the amount.
-Good.

1901
01:10:43,839 --> 01:10:46,141
-Is this enough?
-Okay.

1902
01:10:46,342 --> 01:10:47,643
POONG, MINCED GARLIC

1903
01:10:47,910 --> 01:10:49,278
SAM, GREEN ONION

1904
01:10:49,345 --> 01:10:51,547
He's mixing the mussel sauce

1905
01:10:51,614 --> 01:10:53,782
with his chili oil

1906
01:10:53,849 --> 01:10:56,252
and making flavored chili oil.

1907
01:10:56,318 --> 01:10:57,152
It looks so good.

1908
01:10:57,219 --> 01:11:00,589
-It's ready.
-It looks like a fiery pit.

1909
01:11:01,056 --> 01:11:01,890
That's spicy.

1910
01:11:01,957 --> 01:11:02,925
TEARY-EYED

1911
01:11:03,592 --> 01:11:04,660
GREEN ONION, CHEONGYANG PEPPER

1912
01:11:05,060 --> 01:11:06,895
MAKING THE STIR-FRY SAUCE

1913
01:11:06,962 --> 01:11:08,697
Gosh.

1914
01:11:08,764 --> 01:11:12,434
I think I now understand
how the guests must feel.

1915
01:11:12,501 --> 01:11:15,337
They're all moving busily because of me.

1916
01:11:15,404 --> 01:11:17,306
-Yes, it's moving.
-Is it moving?

1917
01:11:17,373 --> 01:11:20,643
-They're cooking just for you, Nam-no.
-Just for me.

1918
01:11:20,709 --> 01:11:23,178
Yes, they're doing it for the company.

1919
01:11:23,245 --> 01:11:26,282
It's harder than usual
because they have to make a lot.

1920
01:11:26,348 --> 01:11:29,885
Chefs, always cook
with that mindset when you're here.

1921
01:11:29,952 --> 01:11:31,020
It's so moving.

1922
01:11:32,121 --> 01:11:33,522
So moving.

1923
01:11:33,589 --> 01:11:35,924
Can you grind this and some meat?

1924
01:11:35,991 --> 01:11:37,626
I'll do it.

1925
01:11:37,860 --> 01:11:41,096
4. GRIND JOKBAL SKIN AND THIN SKIRT

1926
01:11:41,797 --> 01:11:43,932
What's with this oyster sauce cap?

1927
01:11:43,999 --> 01:11:45,601
-Huh?
-It won't open.

1928
01:11:45,668 --> 01:11:47,202
-What won't open?
-The bottle cap.

1929
01:11:47,269 --> 01:11:48,103
-What?
-Wait.

1930
01:11:48,971 --> 01:11:51,340
-Was it Sam?
-No.

1931
01:11:51,407 --> 01:11:52,741
You're on the same team.

1932
01:11:52,808 --> 01:11:53,842
They're a team.

1933
01:11:53,909 --> 01:11:54,943
Attacking your own team?

1934
01:11:55,010 --> 01:11:57,179
He must've thought it was theirs.
Check for a canine mark.

1935
01:11:58,113 --> 01:11:59,281
-I got it.
-He opened it.

1936
01:11:59,348 --> 01:12:00,349
LIQUID OYSTER SAUCE

1937
01:12:00,916 --> 01:12:02,117
-Got it?
-Check the meat.

1938
01:12:02,184 --> 01:12:03,419
Okay. That's enough.

1939
01:12:03,485 --> 01:12:05,988
He's stir-frying ground <i>jokbal </i>skin

1940
01:12:06,055 --> 01:12:09,258
-and thin skirt.
-I see.

1941
01:12:09,325 --> 01:12:10,559
He's stir-frying?

1942
01:12:10,626 --> 01:12:12,594
-He can't eat spicy food, right?
-He can't.

1943
01:12:13,362 --> 01:12:15,831
They're using dumpling stuffings.

1944
01:12:15,898 --> 01:12:18,634
Eun-yeong and Jong-won
seem to be cooking two different things.

1945
01:12:18,701 --> 01:12:22,338
1. BEEF STUFFING: NAPA CABBAGE, XO SAUCE
KIMCHI DUMPLING STUFFING, INSIDE SKIRT

1946
01:12:23,205 --> 01:12:25,374
AND HE'S USING JOKBAL

1947
01:12:26,575 --> 01:12:29,311
Chef Moon-jung, what is he grinding?

1948
01:12:29,378 --> 01:12:32,247
He's making <i>jokbal</i> stuffing with <i>jokbal.</i>

1949
01:12:32,514 --> 01:12:33,916
WHAT?

1950
01:12:33,982 --> 01:12:38,354
They're making three different stuffings,
including <i>jokbal</i> stuffing.

1951
01:12:38,420 --> 01:12:40,656
-Are they using three different stuffings?
-Yes.

1952
01:12:40,989 --> 01:12:42,124
SOUNDS DELICIOUS

1953
01:12:42,191 --> 01:12:46,628
We're adding <i>jokbal</i> stuffing,
sweet shrimp stuffing, and beef stuffing.

1954
01:12:46,695 --> 01:12:47,529
MEAT DUMPLING STUFFING

1955
01:12:48,063 --> 01:12:49,631
Wait. We have to steam the napa cabbage.

1956
01:12:49,698 --> 01:12:51,400
-Hurry.
-The cabbage.

1957
01:12:51,467 --> 01:12:53,402
-Quickly.
-Wait, not like that. I got it.

1958
01:12:53,469 --> 01:12:56,004
-Poong's giving orders to Sam.
-He is.

1959
01:12:56,071 --> 01:12:57,840
-He told him to step aside.
-"Not like that."

1960
01:12:57,906 --> 01:12:59,842
-He pushed me.
-He pushed you?

1961
01:12:59,908 --> 01:13:02,878
Why are you tattling on me?

1962
01:13:02,945 --> 01:13:04,780
"You got eight stars and I got ten!"

1963
01:13:04,980 --> 01:13:06,281
DO YOU NEED A STAR?

1964
01:13:07,049 --> 01:13:10,219
He's going to cook the napa cabbage.

1965
01:13:10,285 --> 01:13:12,054
-You're steaming it?
-Yes.

1966
01:13:12,121 --> 01:13:14,223
Ten minutes left.
Five minutes have passed.

1967
01:13:14,289 --> 01:13:16,158
-Time's passing.
-It's too quick.

1968
01:13:16,225 --> 01:13:17,526
Has it always been this quick?

1969
01:13:17,593 --> 01:13:19,228
-It's so quick.
-Isn't it?

1970
01:13:19,294 --> 01:13:21,697
Eun-yeong's dumpling skin has become huge.

1971
01:13:21,764 --> 01:13:22,998
She's making one that big?

1972
01:13:23,065 --> 01:13:27,035
-Put some flour on it.
-That bowl usually fits many dumplings.

1973
01:13:27,102 --> 01:13:29,471
-Just like that?
-Whoa.

1974
01:13:29,538 --> 01:13:30,973
-Like that?
-I'm so happy.

1975
01:13:31,039 --> 01:13:32,541
The dough.

1976
01:13:32,608 --> 01:13:34,176
Add them and mix.

1977
01:13:34,243 --> 01:13:35,477
That should be enough.

1978
01:13:35,544 --> 01:13:37,946
7. MIX FLOUR AND STARCH
TO MAKE THE NOODLE DOUGH

1979
01:13:38,013 --> 01:13:38,847
Did it turn out all right?

1980
01:13:38,914 --> 01:13:39,915
-Look.
-Okay.

1981
01:13:39,982 --> 01:13:42,418
That's good. We got this.
Add lots of dusting flour.

1982
01:13:42,484 --> 01:13:43,318
Add a whole lot.

1983
01:13:43,385 --> 01:13:45,888
Poong's giving out orders now.

1984
01:13:45,954 --> 01:13:49,758
-Sam's doing the bulk of the work.
-"Add a whole lot."

1985
01:13:49,825 --> 01:13:51,727
You can make it spicy for me today.

1986
01:13:51,794 --> 01:13:52,661
Okay.

1987
01:13:52,728 --> 01:13:55,497
-You can make it spicy.
-Really? Okay.

1988
01:13:55,731 --> 01:13:56,565
ANCHOVY AEKJEOT

1989
01:13:58,000 --> 01:13:59,835
Sam's also rolling the dough.

1990
01:13:59,902 --> 01:14:03,172
Eun-yeong made it round,
but why is that a triangle?

1991
01:14:03,238 --> 01:14:05,073
We're pulling noodles from them.

1992
01:14:05,140 --> 01:14:06,141
-Like<i> sujebi?</i>
-You have to pull them?

1993
01:14:06,208 --> 01:14:07,810
-You're making <i>sujebi</i> too?
<i>-</i>Are you?

1994
01:14:07,876 --> 01:14:09,778
-Are you making <i>sujebi?</i>
-Wide noodles.

1995
01:14:09,845 --> 01:14:11,580
In a width you had never seen before.

1996
01:14:11,647 --> 01:14:13,148
What if that's the whole noodle?

1997
01:14:13,215 --> 01:14:15,684
Yes, right. I forgot to add that, Sam.

1998
01:14:15,751 --> 01:14:17,119
-What?
-The sauce.

1999
01:14:17,186 --> 01:14:18,387
-Darn it.
-The sauce.

2000
01:14:18,454 --> 01:14:20,456
Open it again. You can do that.

2001
01:14:21,056 --> 01:14:21,890
-Whoa.
-Got it.

2002
01:14:21,957 --> 01:14:24,092
-It's okay.
-Put it in there.

2003
01:14:24,159 --> 01:14:25,828
-That's <i>jokbal.</i>
-Where is it?

2004
01:14:25,894 --> 01:14:27,362
-Are you using <i>ramyeon </i>soup base?
-Yes.

2005
01:14:27,429 --> 01:14:29,331
<i>Ramyeon</i> soup base?

2006
01:14:29,398 --> 01:14:31,467
-The sauce.
-Did Sam agree to do this?

2007
01:14:31,533 --> 01:14:33,802
-Yes.
-Yes.

2008
01:14:33,869 --> 01:14:35,404
Sam agreed too.

2009
01:14:35,471 --> 01:14:37,372
It's in a T-shirt shape.

2010
01:14:37,439 --> 01:14:39,107
-A T-shirt?
-No.

2011
01:14:39,408 --> 01:14:41,543
NOODLE T-SHIRT

2012
01:14:42,478 --> 01:14:43,712
I'll add the entire soup base.

2013
01:14:43,779 --> 01:14:44,780
SHRIMP STUFFING

2014
01:14:44,847 --> 01:14:47,316
They're going to make
an amazingly huge dumpling.

2015
01:14:47,382 --> 01:14:48,484
JOKBAL STUFFING

2016
01:14:49,251 --> 01:14:51,019
Chef Eun-yeong made the mold

2017
01:14:51,086 --> 01:14:53,355
where they'll fill the stuffing.

2018
01:14:53,422 --> 01:14:56,124
Just the sheer size is overwhelming.

2019
01:14:56,191 --> 01:14:57,459
She'll have to cook it for a while.

2020
01:14:57,526 --> 01:14:59,061
She's cutting it with scissors.

2021
01:14:59,127 --> 01:15:00,162
Seven minutes now.

2022
01:15:00,229 --> 01:15:02,364
-Seven? We have to start stuffing now.
-Is there a reason?

2023
01:15:02,431 --> 01:15:05,400
The top portion can't be too thick,

2024
01:15:05,467 --> 01:15:07,903
-So it's to balance it out.
-In case it doesn't cook?

2025
01:15:07,970 --> 01:15:09,705
I guess she'll stuff it
and wrap it like this.

2026
01:15:09,771 --> 01:15:12,140
-I guess so.
-Like this?

2027
01:15:12,207 --> 01:15:13,809
-Like a bundle?
-Yes.

2028
01:15:13,876 --> 01:15:14,710
HAPJAJANG SAUCE

2029
01:15:14,776 --> 01:15:17,446
5. COOL HAPJAJANG SAUCE
AND ADD PRICKLY ASH OIL

2030
01:15:17,513 --> 01:15:18,347
PRICKLY ASH OIL

2031
01:15:18,847 --> 01:15:20,082
SWEET SHRIMPS IN A ZIPPER BAG

2032
01:15:20,549 --> 01:15:23,652
6. SOAK SWEET SHRIMPS
IN HAPJAJANG SAUCE AND SEAL

2033
01:15:25,087 --> 01:15:26,855
TA-DA

2034
01:15:28,190 --> 01:15:30,626
I made this sweet shrimp in soy sauce
for the seasoning.

2035
01:15:30,692 --> 01:15:33,428
-Sweet shrimp in soy sauce?
-I used Nam-no's <i>hapjajang.</i>

2036
01:15:33,495 --> 01:15:35,964
-Man.
-He's using <i>hapjajang.</i>

2037
01:15:36,031 --> 01:15:36,865
Gosh.

2038
01:15:36,932 --> 01:15:40,269
Jong-won has been
explaining his process before we ask.

2039
01:15:40,335 --> 01:15:42,938
Their <i>jokbal</i> was also seasoned
with <i>ramyeon</i> soup base and <i>hapjajang.</i>

2040
01:15:43,272 --> 01:15:45,541
A FIGHT-OFF WITH THE SAME INGREDIENTS

2041
01:15:45,607 --> 01:15:47,342
They'd both make great bar snacks.

2042
01:15:47,910 --> 01:15:49,344
-Can I add this now?
-Sure.

2043
01:15:50,012 --> 01:15:51,547
FINALLY, THE DUMPLING STUFFINGS

2044
01:15:52,014 --> 01:15:55,484
BEEF STUFFING,
SHRIMP STUFFING, JOKBAL STUFFING

2045
01:15:55,551 --> 01:15:56,785
Did you add this?

2046
01:15:56,852 --> 01:15:58,620
-I have to, on top of this.
-On top.

2047
01:15:58,687 --> 01:16:01,557
-Are you adding rice too?
-Is that rice?

2048
01:16:01,623 --> 01:16:03,959
-Frozen broth, I think.
-Frozen broth.

2049
01:16:04,026 --> 01:16:05,928
-She's making <i>tangbao</i>, I think.
-What's that?

2050
01:16:05,994 --> 01:16:10,165
-You can suck on its soup.
-With a straw.

2051
01:16:10,232 --> 01:16:12,301
It's full of broth,
and it's <i>gom-tang,</i> beef broth?

2052
01:16:12,367 --> 01:16:15,337
-That's a great idea.
-They used three different stuffings.

2053
01:16:15,404 --> 01:16:16,972
I'm adding the meat now.

2054
01:16:17,172 --> 01:16:18,006
INSIDE SKIRT

2055
01:16:18,073 --> 01:16:20,208
9. ADD BEEF AND SHRIMPS,
MAKE SHRIMP AND BEEF SOUP

2056
01:16:20,576 --> 01:16:22,177
SHRIMP AND BEEF SOUP

2057
01:16:22,244 --> 01:16:24,513
Cut the noodles now.

2058
01:16:25,080 --> 01:16:26,815
-Can you check?
-What?

2059
01:16:26,882 --> 01:16:28,717
Okay. Excellent. Perfect.

2060
01:16:28,784 --> 01:16:29,851
Great job.

2061
01:16:29,918 --> 01:16:33,989
Sam's mostly doing the simple jobs,

2062
01:16:34,056 --> 01:16:36,992
whereas Poong is doing
most of the cooking.

2063
01:16:37,059 --> 01:16:40,462
Also, Sam's been asking
for Poong's confirmation as he works.

2064
01:16:40,529 --> 01:16:42,998
-Yes, Sam got approval too.
-Throw in one at a time and stir.

2065
01:16:43,065 --> 01:16:45,000
Stir it immediately.

2066
01:16:45,067 --> 01:16:47,636
Sam's in charge of simple jobs.

2067
01:16:47,703 --> 01:16:50,606
I'm going to cook the noodles Nam-no had.

2068
01:16:50,672 --> 01:16:51,506
No.

2069
01:16:51,573 --> 01:16:52,774
One whole bundle?

2070
01:16:53,108 --> 01:16:54,376
HEART RACING

2071
01:16:54,443 --> 01:16:56,178
-The entire thing?
-What's he doing?

2072
01:16:56,244 --> 01:16:57,879
WELL, EVEN IF HE ADDED IT ALL,

2073
01:16:58,447 --> 01:16:59,748
IT'D BE 2 SERVINGS FOR NAM-NO.

2074
01:16:59,815 --> 01:17:01,550
THIS IS 1 SERVING

2075
01:17:01,617 --> 01:17:04,753
IF YOU CAN EAT IT WITH YOUR FINGERS,
IT'S FINGER FOOD

2076
01:17:06,388 --> 01:17:08,624
DROPPING 2(?) SERVINGS!

2077
01:17:08,690 --> 01:17:10,325
Is that pot big enough?

2078
01:17:10,392 --> 01:17:12,594
-It'll overflow.
-It's too much.

2079
01:17:12,661 --> 01:17:14,262
Yes, it'll overflow.

2080
01:17:14,329 --> 01:17:15,998
Five minutes and fifty seconds.

2081
01:17:16,064 --> 01:17:18,967
Eun-yeong is making the huge dumpling.

2082
01:17:19,568 --> 01:17:20,769
You should start steaming it.

2083
01:17:21,203 --> 01:17:22,838
THEY'LL BE AT 5 MINUTES SOON…

2084
01:17:22,904 --> 01:17:24,940
You should start steaming
before you hit five minutes.

2085
01:17:25,007 --> 01:17:28,510
Her hands are shaking.
She must be nervous.

2086
01:17:28,577 --> 01:17:30,412
She was that fond of Nam-no?

2087
01:17:30,479 --> 01:17:33,181
That dumpling is huge.

2088
01:17:33,248 --> 01:17:34,449
Five minutes.

2089
01:17:34,516 --> 01:17:36,818
Five minutes! Please leave, Jung-hwan.

2090
01:17:36,885 --> 01:17:38,987
Yes, which new team is going to win?

2091
01:17:39,588 --> 01:17:42,391
-That looks huge.
-This dumpling is big.

2092
01:17:42,457 --> 01:17:45,594
Is that really a thing?

2093
01:17:45,661 --> 01:17:48,563
She's calmly assembling the dumpling.

2094
01:17:48,630 --> 01:17:52,467
The noodles didn't get separated.
It was too much.

2095
01:17:52,534 --> 01:17:54,569
-Cut it with scissors.
-They're stuck together.

2096
01:17:54,636 --> 01:17:57,973
-You've added too much.
-You have.

2097
01:17:58,040 --> 01:18:00,509
That must be about 20 servings.

2098
01:18:00,575 --> 01:18:04,413
Once the noodles clump together,
it begins to taste like <i>sujebi.</i>

2099
01:18:04,479 --> 01:18:05,781
It changes the flavor.

2100
01:18:05,847 --> 01:18:07,115
Steam it now. 3 minutes, 50 seconds.

2101
01:18:07,182 --> 01:18:08,183
It has to go in now.

2102
01:18:08,250 --> 01:18:10,552
-It has to.
-You have to start steaming it now.

2103
01:18:10,619 --> 01:18:11,620
Steam it.

2104
01:18:11,687 --> 01:18:13,689
Three and a half minutes.

2105
01:18:13,755 --> 01:18:16,558
-Time to grab those.
-Three and a half minutes.

2106
01:18:16,625 --> 01:18:17,693
THE THIN NOODLES COOKED QUICKLY

2107
01:18:17,759 --> 01:18:18,894
This is perfect.

2108
01:18:19,161 --> 01:18:20,062
THE HELPER

2109
01:18:20,128 --> 01:18:22,230
Okay. All right.

2110
01:18:22,297 --> 01:18:24,533
Poong's making the main dish.

2111
01:18:24,599 --> 01:18:27,736
You're doing the same thing
as you would with Ho-young.

2112
01:18:28,103 --> 01:18:29,771
HMPH

2113
01:18:29,838 --> 01:18:34,109
-Lime juice.
-Give him some lime juice.

2114
01:18:34,176 --> 01:18:36,945
-Add them. Start stirring.
-I did. And what?

2115
01:18:37,012 --> 01:18:40,615
Can you grab the cabbage
and spread it out?

2116
01:18:40,682 --> 01:18:42,818
-Put it on here.
-Where? Okay.

2117
01:18:42,884 --> 01:18:44,753
The cabbage. It looks steaming hot.

2118
01:18:44,820 --> 01:18:47,789
-Is it cooked? Cook it some more.
-Spread them out evenly, okay?

2119
01:18:47,856 --> 01:18:50,058
Spread them out.

2120
01:18:50,125 --> 01:18:51,827
How? Like this?

2121
01:18:51,893 --> 01:18:56,298
Turn it to the center. Yes.
And then spread it out as much as you can.

2122
01:18:56,364 --> 01:18:57,432
Cut it in the center.

2123
01:18:57,499 --> 01:18:58,700
-"Cut it."
-Cut it.

2124
01:18:58,767 --> 01:19:01,903
Poong's treating Sam like a junior staff.

2125
01:19:01,970 --> 01:19:03,572
-I see.
-He's giving out orders.

2126
01:19:03,638 --> 01:19:06,441
-It's hot.
-I can see why that's a flower.

2127
01:19:06,508 --> 01:19:08,744
That dumpling looks so nice.

2128
01:19:08,810 --> 01:19:11,546
-It turned out well.
-The creases look so nice.

2129
01:19:11,613 --> 01:19:13,215
-It looks nice.
-Start steaming now.

2130
01:19:13,281 --> 01:19:14,983
It's like a dumpling out of a comic book.

2131
01:19:15,050 --> 01:19:17,919
-She has to steam it now.
-It's hot.

2132
01:19:17,986 --> 01:19:19,187
8. MAKE A HUGE DUMPLING AND STEAM

2133
01:19:19,254 --> 01:19:21,256
There's a huge gap over here.

2134
01:19:21,323 --> 01:19:23,258
You have to push it down firmly.

2135
01:19:23,325 --> 01:19:24,259
It won't work.

2136
01:19:24,326 --> 01:19:25,927
Pressure's escaping through that gap.

2137
01:19:25,994 --> 01:19:27,863
-Can you hold this? I got it.
-Wait, look.

2138
01:19:27,929 --> 01:19:30,298
Will it get cooked in three minutes?

2139
01:19:30,665 --> 01:19:33,001
HE CAN'T EVEN POUR THIS MUCH ALONE

2140
01:19:33,235 --> 01:19:34,803
DECIDED TO USE ONLY 1(?) SERVING

2141
01:19:34,870 --> 01:19:37,339
-Did you make a hole?
-I did.

2142
01:19:37,405 --> 01:19:40,675
No, you had to cut it off all the way.

2143
01:19:40,742 --> 01:19:44,246
-Okay. I got it.
-Poong's getting mad at Sam.

2144
01:19:44,312 --> 01:19:47,382
How many times did I tell you
to cut off the tip?

2145
01:19:47,449 --> 01:19:49,050
I could've used scissors.

2146
01:19:49,117 --> 01:19:52,487
-You should've.
-Scissors are kitchen tools too.

2147
01:19:52,554 --> 01:19:54,422
Wait. I have to work on the <i>jokbal.</i>

2148
01:19:54,489 --> 01:19:58,059
-<i>Jokbal.</i> Open it.
-<i>Jokbal.</i> Is it ready?

2149
01:19:58,126 --> 01:20:00,395
It must be hot. <i>Jokbal.</i>

2150
01:20:00,462 --> 01:20:02,898
-I got it.
-A minute and 40 seconds.

2151
01:20:02,964 --> 01:20:05,400
TORTURED BY NOODLES

2152
01:20:05,467 --> 01:20:09,304
He's made too many noodles.
He's unable to cool them.

2153
01:20:09,371 --> 01:20:11,573
Jong-won washes the noodles.

2154
01:20:11,907 --> 01:20:14,342
A SELF-INFLICTED ORDEAL

2155
01:20:14,409 --> 01:20:16,545
I doubt he's ever washed
that many noodles before.

2156
01:20:16,611 --> 01:20:20,782
I have, back when I was in the military.
I served at the GOP checkpoint,

2157
01:20:20,849 --> 01:20:23,485
and there were 23 of them,
so I used 1 bundle of noodles.

2158
01:20:23,552 --> 01:20:26,087
-One minute.
-It's literally like laundry.

2159
01:20:26,655 --> 01:20:29,324
-Get the <i>jokbal </i>out.
-One minute left.

2160
01:20:29,891 --> 01:20:31,593
-Okay. Get ready to mash them.
-Good.

2161
01:20:31,660 --> 01:20:33,094
-Okay.
-Get ready.

2162
01:20:33,161 --> 01:20:34,396
-A minute?
-A minute.

2163
01:20:35,330 --> 01:20:38,033
DROP SHRIMP AND BEEF NOODLES!

2164
01:20:38,099 --> 01:20:40,268
-All right.
-That looks great.

2165
01:20:40,335 --> 01:20:41,870
All right. It looks great.

2166
01:20:41,937 --> 01:20:44,472
Poong's team seems to lead the round.

2167
01:20:44,539 --> 01:20:47,409
SHRIMP & THIN SKIRT AND SEASONED JOKBAL

2168
01:20:47,475 --> 01:20:49,678
-More.
-More meat.

2169
01:20:49,744 --> 01:20:51,513
POONG'S FLAVORED CHILI OIL

2170
01:20:51,580 --> 01:20:53,748
-More meat.
-Okay.

2171
01:20:53,815 --> 01:20:55,750
Chili oil.

2172
01:20:55,817 --> 01:20:58,386
-That sauce looks so good.
-It looks nice.

2173
01:20:58,453 --> 01:21:00,622
Nam-no's going to love that.

2174
01:21:00,689 --> 01:21:03,491
-There's the sauce. The shrimp bag.
-There's the sauce bag.

2175
01:21:06,161 --> 01:21:07,195
FREED FROM NOODLES

2176
01:21:07,462 --> 01:21:09,197
JONG-WON FINISHES THE HAPJAJANG NOODLES

2177
01:21:09,598 --> 01:21:11,867
EUN-YEONG POURS THE SHRIMP MARINADE

2178
01:21:11,933 --> 01:21:13,235
I'll chop the green onion now.

2179
01:21:13,301 --> 01:21:15,070
Thirty seconds left.

2180
01:21:15,136 --> 01:21:17,973
This is a huge serving of noodles<i>.</i>

2181
01:21:18,039 --> 01:21:21,243
-It's all for him?
-It's the sauce, not noodles.

2182
01:21:21,309 --> 01:21:23,578
You can top the sauce on the dumpling.

2183
01:21:23,645 --> 01:21:24,946
The noodles?

2184
01:21:25,013 --> 01:21:26,514
-That's the sauce?
-On the dumpling?

2185
01:21:26,581 --> 01:21:28,149
Twenty seconds.

2186
01:21:28,850 --> 01:21:30,819
-Twenty seconds.
-Oh, no.

2187
01:21:31,386 --> 01:21:32,220
Right here?

2188
01:21:32,287 --> 01:21:33,955
PLATING THE DUMPLING SAUCE(?)

2189
01:21:35,023 --> 01:21:36,258
Dang.

2190
01:21:36,324 --> 01:21:37,993
-What is that?
-It's overflowing.

2191
01:21:38,059 --> 01:21:38,894
It's too much.

2192
01:21:38,960 --> 01:21:42,831
Leave out some noodles.

2193
01:21:42,898 --> 01:21:44,666
Sprinkle lots of oil on it.

2194
01:21:44,733 --> 01:21:47,302
A BIG DASH OF POONG'S CHILI OIL!

2195
01:21:47,369 --> 01:21:48,203
One more time.

2196
01:21:48,270 --> 01:21:50,272
-Twenty seconds.
-Right here.

2197
01:21:50,338 --> 01:21:52,307
-There's no time.
-Come on.

2198
01:21:52,374 --> 01:21:54,943
-What about the dumpling?
-I hope it's cooked.

2199
01:21:55,010 --> 01:21:55,977
Ten.

2200
01:21:56,044 --> 01:21:56,878
-Nine.
-Nine.

2201
01:21:56,945 --> 01:21:58,013
-Eight.
-We don't need that.

2202
01:21:58,079 --> 01:21:58,914
-Seven.
-No? Okay.

2203
01:21:58,980 --> 01:22:00,048
Six.

2204
01:22:00,682 --> 01:22:01,917
Poong and Sam finished.

2205
01:22:01,983 --> 01:22:03,852
It's ready.

2206
01:22:03,919 --> 01:22:05,887
-That's huge.
-It is huge.

2207
01:22:05,954 --> 01:22:07,555
-Ten. Nine.
-Nine.

2208
01:22:07,622 --> 01:22:11,092
10. TOP DUMPLING SAUCE(?)
WITH HAPJAJANG SHRIMP SAUCE, GREEN ONION

2209
01:22:11,159 --> 01:22:12,961
-Poong ended first.
-Poong and Sam finished.

2210
01:22:13,028 --> 01:22:15,964
-All done.
-That's a big serving.

2211
01:22:16,031 --> 01:22:17,866
-One, two, three.
-The steamer.

2212
01:22:17,933 --> 01:22:20,936
Jong-won and Eun-yeong finish too.

2213
01:22:21,002 --> 01:22:23,104
That dumpling.
They should open it and check it.

2214
01:22:23,171 --> 01:22:25,273
-Just serve that.
-Serve the whole thing.

2215
01:22:25,340 --> 01:22:26,975
It's served on the stove.

2216
01:22:27,042 --> 01:22:28,710
Nam-no, chew very carefully.

2217
01:22:28,777 --> 01:22:30,745
I'll chew very carefully.

2218
01:22:30,812 --> 01:22:33,114
-"Chew carefully."
-That'll take a while.

2219
01:22:33,949 --> 01:22:35,283
Great job, Sam.

2220
01:22:36,551 --> 01:22:38,486
-Great job.
-Great job.

2221
01:22:38,553 --> 01:22:41,957
All dishes were prepared for Chef Nam-no.

2222
01:22:42,023 --> 01:22:44,826
The servings are huge.

2223
01:22:44,893 --> 01:22:46,161
-It's insane.
-It is.

2224
01:22:46,227 --> 01:22:47,595
That's a lot.

2225
01:22:47,662 --> 01:22:50,131
-You look quite happy.
-I am.

2226
01:22:50,198 --> 01:22:51,633
First, Poong and Sam's dish,

2227
01:22:52,500 --> 01:22:54,302
<i>Lots of Incentives from Poong and Sam.</i>

2228
01:22:54,369 --> 01:22:57,539
A NOODLE DISH WITH STEAMED NAPA CABBAGE
AND BEEF, SHRIMP, JOKBAL SAUCE

2229
01:22:57,973 --> 01:23:02,077
SAM KIM & KIM POONG'S
LOTS OF INCENTIVES FROM POONG AND SAM

2230
01:23:02,911 --> 01:23:04,045
-Whoa.
-First, Poong's dish.

2231
01:23:04,112 --> 01:23:07,048
It's so heavy. And it looks like

2232
01:23:07,115 --> 01:23:08,550
it's from a classy Sichuan restaurant.

2233
01:23:08,616 --> 01:23:10,418
-Whoa!
-It's amazing.

2234
01:23:10,485 --> 01:23:15,256
It's a flower.
He cooked napa cabbage and made a flower.

2235
01:23:15,323 --> 01:23:17,559
He scolded Sam a lot in the process.

2236
01:23:17,625 --> 01:23:19,127
Did I?

2237
01:23:19,194 --> 01:23:20,795
"Cut the core, stupid."

2238
01:23:20,862 --> 01:23:22,697
-"Use your hands, stupid."
-Really? I'm sorry.

2239
01:23:23,264 --> 01:23:25,667
-I didn't realize it.
-Come on.

2240
01:23:25,734 --> 01:23:28,303
But it turned out like that.
He deserved to be mad at Sam.

2241
01:23:28,370 --> 01:23:30,839
Poong led the whole process.

2242
01:23:30,905 --> 01:23:33,274
-How should he eat it?
-You'll see

2243
01:23:33,341 --> 01:23:35,643
that the cabbage pieces are spread out.

2244
01:23:35,710 --> 01:23:38,246
-Eat them with the topping.
-Like a cabbage wrap?

2245
01:23:38,313 --> 01:23:40,482
The noodles will act like a wrap.

2246
01:23:40,548 --> 01:23:42,817
-Like that?
-It's been cooked well.

2247
01:23:42,884 --> 01:23:44,753
You'll find very wide noodles.

2248
01:23:44,819 --> 01:23:46,454
Yes, right here.

2249
01:23:46,521 --> 01:23:48,857
-This one?
-Correct.

2250
01:23:48,923 --> 01:23:50,859
-Lots of sauce.
-And add lots of sauce.

2251
01:23:51,426 --> 01:23:53,795
-It's a lot already.
-just like that.

2252
01:23:53,862 --> 01:23:54,796
LOTS OF SAUCE

2253
01:23:54,863 --> 01:23:56,865
-The chili oil seems strong.
-It looks good.

2254
01:23:56,931 --> 01:23:58,066
It's probably still hot.

2255
01:24:03,004 --> 01:24:04,906
A BITE WITH THE LADLE

2256
01:24:05,840 --> 01:24:07,075
INCREDI-BITE…

2257
01:24:07,142 --> 01:24:10,078
The collagen from <i>jokbal</i>
bounces around my mouth,

2258
01:24:10,145 --> 01:24:13,681
while the noodles gently
make their way inside.

2259
01:24:13,748 --> 01:24:16,351
I didn't add starch water on purpose.

2260
01:24:16,418 --> 01:24:20,388
<i>The collagen from</i> jokbal <i>made it thicker,</i>

2261
01:24:20,455 --> 01:24:23,191
so you can enjoy it that way.

2262
01:24:23,258 --> 01:24:26,127
-I'm sure it's much tenderer.
-Must be.

2263
01:24:26,194 --> 01:24:27,629
I need to try the cabbage.

2264
01:24:27,695 --> 01:24:31,399
It's still hot, so scoop out a few pieces.

2265
01:24:31,466 --> 01:24:32,767
You have one there.

2266
01:24:32,834 --> 01:24:34,436
A BIG BITE OF THE NAPA CABBAGE!

2267
01:24:34,502 --> 01:24:35,904
-Whoa.
-That's a lot.

2268
01:24:35,970 --> 01:24:38,373
That's it.

2269
01:24:38,440 --> 01:24:41,443
-It contains some moisture, right?
-It does.

2270
01:24:41,509 --> 01:24:43,478
-My gosh. Wait.
-Whoa.

2271
01:24:44,012 --> 01:24:45,713
REACHING

2272
01:24:45,780 --> 01:24:46,948
See? You want to wipe his face.

2273
01:24:47,015 --> 01:24:48,683
-What's it like?
-What's it like?

2274
01:24:49,951 --> 01:24:51,419
CHOKING UP…

2275
01:24:51,486 --> 01:24:52,754
-What's wrong?
-A headache?

2276
01:24:52,821 --> 01:24:55,256
-Are you crying?
-Why?

2277
01:24:55,323 --> 01:24:57,525
Gosh…

2278
01:24:57,592 --> 01:25:00,929
They're all moving busily because of me.

2279
01:25:00,995 --> 01:25:02,897
-It's touching.
-Isn't it?

2280
01:25:02,964 --> 01:25:05,033
What's wrong? A headache?

2281
01:25:05,100 --> 01:25:07,001
-It's hot.
-It's hot?

2282
01:25:07,068 --> 01:25:08,269
Have some water.

2283
01:25:08,336 --> 01:25:11,439
-He didn't cool it down. Cool it.
-He should've cooled it down.

2284
01:25:11,506 --> 01:25:12,974
-One second.
-Otherwise, you can't taste it.

2285
01:25:13,041 --> 01:25:14,909
He takes off his belt.

2286
01:25:15,477 --> 01:25:16,511
What?

2287
01:25:16,578 --> 01:25:18,980
You aren't taking off your pants, right?

2288
01:25:19,047 --> 01:25:21,816
STRUGGLING…

2289
01:25:22,450 --> 01:25:25,520
JONG-WON TAKES OFF HIS TIE
WHEN SOMETHING TASTES GOOD

2290
01:25:26,321 --> 01:25:29,390
BUT NAM-NO TAKES OFF HIS BELT

2291
01:25:29,457 --> 01:25:31,493
Do you even need the belt?

2292
01:25:31,559 --> 01:25:35,396
-It looks overly spicy, right?
-Yes.

2293
01:25:35,463 --> 01:25:38,099
But it's just spicy enough.

2294
01:25:38,166 --> 01:25:41,102
-It's not too spicy?
-It looked like it.

2295
01:25:41,169 --> 01:25:43,671
<i>These are my favorites,</i>
<i>like sweet shrimp and </i>jokbal<i>.</i>

2296
01:25:43,738 --> 01:25:44,772
<i>It's a huge party.</i>

2297
01:25:44,839 --> 01:25:47,909
It tastes fantastic
with the sweetness of the cabbage.

2298
01:25:47,976 --> 01:25:49,444
-Sounds good.
-It looks good.

2299
01:25:49,511 --> 01:25:51,613
-Can you taste the <i>jokbal?</i>
-Yes.

2300
01:25:52,147 --> 01:25:54,582
BUSY EATING

2301
01:25:55,383 --> 01:25:56,484
Look at that.

2302
01:25:56,551 --> 01:25:59,254
The noodles remind me
of knife-cut noodles.

2303
01:25:59,320 --> 01:26:02,490
It's similar, but it's thinner
so that it can shoot inside

2304
01:26:02,557 --> 01:26:04,626
when you slurp it in.

2305
01:26:06,427 --> 01:26:08,730
-He makes it look good.
-He eats well.

2306
01:26:08,796 --> 01:26:11,466
-He might finish that.
-A thumbs-up.

2307
01:26:11,533 --> 01:26:13,468
The noodles must have a nice texture.

2308
01:26:13,535 --> 01:26:15,270
-It's really good.
-The ingredients…

2309
01:26:15,336 --> 01:26:16,671
Try the next dish.

2310
01:26:16,738 --> 01:26:17,639
Give us some too.

2311
01:26:17,705 --> 01:26:19,674
Move it aside.

2312
01:26:19,741 --> 01:26:22,577
You're always dying to eat
other people's leftovers.

2313
01:26:22,644 --> 01:26:23,912
What's with you?

2314
01:26:23,978 --> 01:26:26,781
The next one, Team Jong-won and Eun-yeong.

2315
01:26:27,382 --> 01:26:30,118
A HUGE DUMPLING FOR NAM-NO

2316
01:26:30,919 --> 01:26:36,024
AND A SIDE
OF SWEET SHRIMP HAPJAJANG NOODLES

2317
01:26:36,991 --> 01:26:40,929
EVEN NAM-NO WILL FEEL FULL
WHEN WE DUMP THIS DUMPLING ON HIM

2318
01:26:40,995 --> 01:26:42,830
They're laying it out?

2319
01:26:42,897 --> 01:26:43,898
FLAP

2320
01:26:43,965 --> 01:26:46,968
You need to wear this to eat our dumpling.

2321
01:26:47,035 --> 01:26:48,703
Will she choke him?

2322
01:26:48,770 --> 01:26:50,305
What is this? A barbershop?

2323
01:26:51,873 --> 01:26:53,508
-Enjoy.
-Okay.

2324
01:26:53,575 --> 01:26:55,376
-I'm curious.
-Don't you want to know?

2325
01:26:55,443 --> 01:26:57,045
-How did it go?
-We haven't seen it either.

2326
01:26:57,111 --> 01:26:58,846
The dumpling is everything.

2327
01:26:58,913 --> 01:27:00,815
I wonder if it's cooked well.

2328
01:27:00,882 --> 01:27:02,417
The huge dumpling!

2329
01:27:02,483 --> 01:27:03,484
Two, three.

2330
01:27:04,452 --> 01:27:06,287
-Whoa!
-Whoa.

2331
01:27:06,621 --> 01:27:08,456
AMAZED

2332
01:27:08,523 --> 01:27:09,624
Two, three.

2333
01:27:10,158 --> 01:27:12,794
-Whoa!
-Whoa.

2334
01:27:13,027 --> 01:27:14,829
THE DUMPED DUMPLING LOOK NICELY STEAMED

2335
01:27:14,896 --> 01:27:16,698
-Is this it?
-It's nicely cooked.

2336
01:27:16,764 --> 01:27:18,333
-It looks cooked.
-I can't see it.

2337
01:27:18,399 --> 01:27:19,901
-Me neither.
-I can't see it.

2338
01:27:19,968 --> 01:27:21,769
Why did you give him a straw?

2339
01:27:21,836 --> 01:27:24,272
-For the soup.
-To drink the soup first.

2340
01:27:24,339 --> 01:27:26,274
Just like soup dumplings.

2341
01:27:26,341 --> 01:27:29,777
-She had stuffed frozen soup inside.
-She did.

2342
01:27:29,844 --> 01:27:31,846
Use the straw and try the soup first.

2343
01:27:31,913 --> 01:27:33,915
It'll be too hot. Can he do that?

2344
01:27:33,982 --> 01:27:36,985
-It smells like shrimp.
-He'll burn his throat.

2345
01:27:37,051 --> 01:27:38,419
Can you not handle hot soup?

2346
01:27:39,287 --> 01:27:40,388
He'll die.

2347
01:27:40,455 --> 01:27:43,858
-Check and see if you can do that.
-Check first.

2348
01:27:43,925 --> 01:27:46,728
-Just get some soup from the top.
-The outside.

2349
01:27:46,794 --> 01:27:49,330
-See if you can use a straw.
-He can't taste things anymore.

2350
01:27:49,397 --> 01:27:50,465
I don't think so.

2351
01:27:50,798 --> 01:27:53,368
GIVES UP QUICKLY

2352
01:27:53,434 --> 01:27:55,136
Try the cold dish first.

2353
01:27:55,203 --> 01:27:57,739
Top the dumpling with the sauce.

2354
01:27:57,805 --> 01:28:00,208
-This one?
-That's the sauce?

2355
01:28:00,275 --> 01:28:01,643
-Those are noodles.
-No, the sauce.

2356
01:28:01,709 --> 01:28:05,346
Most sauces include
green onion and garlic, right?

2357
01:28:05,413 --> 01:28:07,348
So I added a bit of noodles to that.

2358
01:28:07,415 --> 01:28:09,817
Those aren't "a bit." How is that a bit?

2359
01:28:09,884 --> 01:28:12,920
-"A bit"?
-It's overwhelming to look at.

2360
01:28:12,987 --> 01:28:15,423
I don't eat this much.

2361
01:28:15,490 --> 01:28:17,358
No, I think you can.

2362
01:28:17,992 --> 01:28:18,826
No.

2363
01:28:18,893 --> 01:28:20,128
You can make it happen.

2364
01:28:20,194 --> 01:28:22,463
A SWOOP OF THE SAUCE

2365
01:28:23,765 --> 01:28:25,333
HAPPY

2366
01:28:25,400 --> 01:28:26,934
That's most people's single serving.

2367
01:28:27,001 --> 01:28:28,936
-Top it with sweet shrimp.
-Sweet shrimp?

2368
01:28:30,071 --> 01:28:31,806
-Can you help me?
-Sure.

2369
01:28:32,373 --> 01:28:35,043
They asked him
to have that sauce with the dumpling.

2370
01:28:35,109 --> 01:28:36,411
-He's like an emperor.
-Is she his mom?

2371
01:28:36,477 --> 01:28:37,512
Man, look at that.

2372
01:28:37,578 --> 01:28:39,947
-He can fit that in his mouth?
-In one bite?

2373
01:28:40,014 --> 01:28:41,582
-This will go viral.
-Can you do that?

2374
01:28:41,649 --> 01:28:43,751
What? He's stealing my thunder again.

2375
01:28:43,818 --> 01:28:45,820
My favorite food combination

2376
01:28:45,887 --> 01:28:48,856
is cold noodles with hot dumplings.

2377
01:28:48,923 --> 01:28:49,791
I go crazy for it.

2378
01:28:49,857 --> 01:28:51,426
First, cold noodles.

2379
01:28:52,660 --> 01:28:53,995
WHOA

2380
01:28:54,662 --> 01:28:56,297
-Hey.
-Whoa.

2381
01:28:56,364 --> 01:28:58,933
If it's bad, you don't have to finish it.

2382
01:28:59,000 --> 01:28:59,834
It's still going in.

2383
01:29:00,168 --> 01:29:02,437
SLURPING IN

2384
01:29:02,904 --> 01:29:05,273
AND THE SHRIMP HE DROPPED

2385
01:29:05,340 --> 01:29:06,941
INTO HIS MOUTH

2386
01:29:07,608 --> 01:29:10,311
I feel like
I'm watching a superpower show.

2387
01:29:10,378 --> 01:29:12,046
It's so good.

2388
01:29:12,113 --> 01:29:13,014
Is it?

2389
01:29:15,249 --> 01:29:17,952
THE MOM COULDN'T STAND IT ANYMORE

2390
01:29:18,686 --> 01:29:20,288
-This is delicious, Mom.
-A mom?

2391
01:29:20,355 --> 01:29:22,557
I told you to slow down, kid.

2392
01:29:22,924 --> 01:29:24,792
HE HAS MOMS HERE AND THERE

2393
01:29:24,859 --> 01:29:26,561
You look like a European bourgeois.

2394
01:29:26,928 --> 01:29:30,198
LOOKS SO RICH

2395
01:29:30,264 --> 01:29:31,599
Like Louis XIV.

2396
01:29:31,933 --> 01:29:34,035
HE GREW UP WITHOUT ANY LACK

2397
01:29:34,102 --> 01:29:37,071
What did you use to make the sauce?
Soy sauce and…

2398
01:29:37,138 --> 01:29:39,574
-Hapjajang.
-Hapjajang. <i>I see.</i>

2399
01:29:39,640 --> 01:29:42,276
-Prickly ash.
-Prickly ash oil too.

2400
01:29:43,544 --> 01:29:44,379
SLURP

2401
01:29:46,013 --> 01:29:47,081
SLUUURP

2402
01:29:47,148 --> 01:29:50,084
-He makes it look so good.
-He's devouring it.

2403
01:29:50,151 --> 01:29:51,886
I'd watch him when I have no appetite.

2404
01:29:51,953 --> 01:29:54,655
-What's it like? Tell us.
-How is it different?

2405
01:29:55,089 --> 01:29:57,058
TAKING THE SODA

2406
01:29:57,125 --> 01:29:58,426
He just swallowed the noodles.

2407
01:29:58,493 --> 01:29:59,727
Gosh.

2408
01:29:59,794 --> 01:30:00,762
What's wrong?

2409
01:30:00,828 --> 01:30:01,763
Are you in pain?

2410
01:30:02,330 --> 01:30:03,598
Was it too cold?

2411
01:30:03,664 --> 01:30:05,500
What's it like?

2412
01:30:06,100 --> 01:30:07,068
DRINKING

2413
01:30:07,135 --> 01:30:09,270
How many times do I have to ask, punk?

2414
01:30:13,574 --> 01:30:18,846
WE APOLOGIZE FOR AN UNSIGHTLY MOMENT
IN THIS CHUSEOK HOLIDAY

2415
01:30:18,913 --> 01:30:21,816
We asked you a question,
so we expected an answer.

2416
01:30:21,883 --> 01:30:23,985
I kept asking what it was like!

2417
01:30:24,051 --> 01:30:25,653
Who'll eat that after you spit on it?

2418
01:30:25,720 --> 01:30:27,889
It was your plan
to finish everything alone!

2419
01:30:27,955 --> 01:30:31,125
We won't take it from you,
so take your time and eat it.

2420
01:30:31,192 --> 01:30:34,629
-Is it salty, sweet, or spicy?
-Well, first off,

2421
01:30:34,695 --> 01:30:36,798
-…it's too delicious.
-Was that why?

2422
01:30:36,864 --> 01:30:39,867
It's similar to cold Chinese noodles.

2423
01:30:39,934 --> 01:30:41,769
-Cold Chinese noodles?
-Cold Chinese noodles.

2424
01:30:41,836 --> 01:30:44,772
<i>It's made with prickly ash,</i>
<i>sweet shrimp, which is my favorite,</i>

2425
01:30:44,839 --> 01:30:49,477
<i>and the sauce on the plate</i>
<i>is made with </i>hapjajang<i> with strong umami</i>.

2426
01:30:49,544 --> 01:30:51,779
You've only had the sauce so far.

2427
01:30:52,146 --> 01:30:53,881
THE MAIN DISH, THE DUMPLING TO STUFF YOU

2428
01:30:53,948 --> 01:30:56,417
-Dumpling.
-He can probably suck on it now.

2429
01:30:56,484 --> 01:30:58,386
-Suck on it with the straw.
-Use the straw.

2430
01:31:00,054 --> 01:31:01,155
-The straw?
-It looks hot.

2431
01:31:01,222 --> 01:31:02,423
-"Suck on it."
-Try sucking on it.

2432
01:31:03,591 --> 01:31:05,092
STEAMING

2433
01:31:05,159 --> 01:31:07,962
It's still steaming hot
like a blast furnace.

2434
01:31:08,029 --> 01:31:10,164
Just suck it in for the show.

2435
01:31:10,698 --> 01:31:12,867
YOU'RE OUR VERY SPECIAL GUEST

2436
01:31:12,934 --> 01:31:13,801
Yes, sir!

2437
01:31:13,868 --> 01:31:16,037
Not all the way in.
Just a little off the top.

2438
01:31:16,103 --> 01:31:18,139
-Slowly.
-It's rising up.

2439
01:31:18,206 --> 01:31:22,477
-There's the broth.
-Can you see it?

2440
01:31:22,543 --> 01:31:23,778
Are you okay?

2441
01:31:24,011 --> 01:31:25,847
SO HOT

2442
01:31:25,913 --> 01:31:28,316
Do I have to eat it like this?

2443
01:31:28,382 --> 01:31:30,184
-Just use a spoon.
-Eat it as is.

2444
01:31:30,251 --> 01:31:31,953
-Open it.
-Scoop it up.

2445
01:31:32,019 --> 01:31:34,956
It's still piping hot.
Suck on this soup with a straw?

2446
01:31:36,824 --> 01:31:39,727
-Eat the skin too.
-You shouldn't burn your tongue.

2447
01:31:39,794 --> 01:31:42,096
There are three different zones.

2448
01:31:42,163 --> 01:31:44,365
-You're all cold.
-That looks good.

2449
01:31:44,432 --> 01:31:46,667
-With the noodles.
-Some people are like that.

2450
01:31:46,734 --> 01:31:49,036
-Eat it with the sauce.
-The sauce.

2451
01:31:49,103 --> 01:31:50,838
There are three flavors.

2452
01:31:50,905 --> 01:31:52,440
Is it hot or is it good?

2453
01:31:52,507 --> 01:31:54,075
There are different zones.

2454
01:31:54,141 --> 01:31:55,676
-Your face…
-It's hot, but he's eating it.

2455
01:31:55,743 --> 01:31:57,912
This is good, Mom.

2456
01:31:57,979 --> 01:32:00,281
She's like, "Don't eat too much."

2457
01:32:00,648 --> 01:32:03,084
LIKE SHE'S WIPING SOME STATUE…

2458
01:32:03,150 --> 01:32:06,187
-What's in the three zones?
-In here,

2459
01:32:06,254 --> 01:32:09,657
there's beef here,
and there's shrimp over here.

2460
01:32:09,724 --> 01:32:10,791
-Shrimps?
-Shrimp.

2461
01:32:10,858 --> 01:32:16,130
The frozen <i>gom-tang</i>
melts in the mouth like gelatin.

2462
01:32:18,366 --> 01:32:19,700
A BIG PIECE

2463
01:32:19,767 --> 01:32:21,269
Mom, can you help?

2464
01:32:23,371 --> 01:32:24,705
Mom, this place is delicious.

2465
01:32:25,606 --> 01:32:27,608
"Eat up, my son."

2466
01:32:27,675 --> 01:32:29,076
SLURP

2467
01:32:29,143 --> 01:32:30,211
It's still hot, right?

2468
01:32:30,278 --> 01:32:31,112
INTO THE MOUTH

2469
01:32:31,178 --> 01:32:34,048
Tell us what it's like now.

2470
01:32:36,384 --> 01:32:37,585
I've figured it out now.

2471
01:32:37,652 --> 01:32:39,520
-You have?
-I knew it.

2472
01:32:39,587 --> 01:32:41,155
Did you use XO dumplings?

2473
01:32:41,222 --> 01:32:43,791
We did use the filling.

2474
01:32:43,858 --> 01:32:46,494
It had all the dumpling products I love.

2475
01:32:46,561 --> 01:32:48,729
<i>The umami flavor</i>

2476
01:32:48,796 --> 01:32:52,867
<i>became three, four times stronger</i>
<i>because it's a mix of everything.</i>

2477
01:32:52,934 --> 01:32:55,036
I feel like I've had
the biggest dumpling in the world.

2478
01:32:55,102 --> 01:32:56,871
I've never seen one so big either.

2479
01:32:56,938 --> 01:32:59,840
Well, that also does resemble Nam-no.

2480
01:33:00,207 --> 01:33:02,376
JONG-WON & EUN-YEONG'S YOON NAM-NO

2481
01:33:02,443 --> 01:33:04,245
-I'm dumpling, he's <i>sujebi?</i>
-Sure.

2482
01:33:04,312 --> 01:33:05,313
Pick one.

2483
01:33:05,546 --> 01:33:06,781
COOLING HIS STOMACH WITH SODA

2484
01:33:06,847 --> 01:33:08,282
-We'll eat it now.
-We'll try this.

2485
01:33:08,349 --> 01:33:09,850
-Why don't we try it too?
-Sure.

2486
01:33:09,917 --> 01:33:12,587
Just eat whatever you can get for now.

2487
01:33:12,653 --> 01:33:15,890
The portion is huge,
so eat whatever you can take.

2488
01:33:15,957 --> 01:33:16,991
THE WIDE NOODLES FIRST

2489
01:33:19,293 --> 01:33:20,595
This is really good.

2490
01:33:20,661 --> 01:33:23,798
-It's good.
-Come over and have some.

2491
01:33:23,864 --> 01:33:26,100
Yes, have some before we go on.

2492
01:33:26,167 --> 01:33:29,537
GATHERING TOGETHER

2493
01:33:30,104 --> 01:33:31,339
It feels like the holidays.

2494
01:33:31,405 --> 01:33:33,174
It's the Chuseok vibe.

2495
01:33:33,240 --> 01:33:34,308
Have some more.

2496
01:33:35,476 --> 01:33:37,178
Mmm.

2497
01:33:37,244 --> 01:33:40,214
I thought it'd be really spicy,
but it's not.

2498
01:33:40,281 --> 01:33:42,483
So you can make fancy dishes too.

2499
01:33:42,550 --> 01:33:43,751
Give me some here.

2500
01:33:43,818 --> 01:33:46,721
The wide noodles
that Sam made are really good.

2501
01:33:47,088 --> 01:33:48,389
PROUD

2502
01:33:49,290 --> 01:33:51,959
It still carries
that distinct <i>jokbal</i> smell.

2503
01:33:53,361 --> 01:33:55,363
-Wait, Poong made this?
-Right?

2504
01:33:55,429 --> 01:33:57,832
-It's so fancy.
-It doesn't make sense.

2505
01:33:58,199 --> 01:34:00,034
SLURP

2506
01:34:00,401 --> 01:34:01,235
SLUUURP

2507
01:34:03,270 --> 01:34:05,539
SLURP

2508
01:34:05,606 --> 01:34:07,842
They're all slurping over there.

2509
01:34:08,242 --> 01:34:09,477
SLUUURP

2510
01:34:11,312 --> 01:34:13,014
It has a unique smell.

2511
01:34:13,080 --> 01:34:14,982
I like the smell of prickly ash.

2512
01:34:15,049 --> 01:34:17,385
-This is so good too.
-I love how it smells.

2513
01:34:18,052 --> 01:34:19,020
YUM

2514
01:34:19,086 --> 01:34:21,522
With so much food,
it's turning into a feast.

2515
01:34:21,589 --> 01:34:22,923
The dumpling's good too.

2516
01:34:24,425 --> 01:34:25,960
Mmm.

2517
01:34:26,027 --> 01:34:27,294
The dumpling is delicious.

2518
01:34:27,361 --> 01:34:29,964
-Who cares about stars?
-Right.

2519
01:34:30,031 --> 01:34:30,931
It's more important to be happy.

2520
01:34:32,199 --> 01:34:33,768
Things are so friendly right now.

2521
01:34:33,834 --> 01:34:34,769
It is.

2522
01:34:34,835 --> 01:34:37,038
-Don't be feisty over the result.
-Okay.

2523
01:34:37,104 --> 01:34:38,806
-Yes, let's go on a trip too.
-Let's just eat and chat.

2524
01:34:38,873 --> 01:34:40,341
BIG BITE

2525
01:34:40,408 --> 01:34:42,443
It's fun to walk around and eat.

2526
01:34:42,510 --> 01:34:43,344
Like a buffet.

2527
01:34:43,411 --> 01:34:44,645
-Sung-ju.
-Yes?

2528
01:34:44,712 --> 01:34:47,448
-Grab lots of noodles, okay?
-The noodles?

2529
01:34:47,515 --> 01:34:49,216
I want to try the noodles too.

2530
01:34:49,283 --> 01:34:52,887
-Nam-no, do you have kimchi in the fridge?
-That'd be so nice.

2531
01:34:53,220 --> 01:34:55,222
A BITE OF THE NOODLES

2532
01:34:58,826 --> 01:35:00,661
You're like a <i>CCW</i> judge.

2533
01:35:02,196 --> 01:35:04,865
THE BEST SUJEBI IN KOREA
KWON SUNG-JUN

2534
01:35:05,433 --> 01:35:07,535
It's our first time
eating while walking around.

2535
01:35:07,601 --> 01:35:09,270
What do you think, Sung-jun?

2536
01:35:09,336 --> 01:35:12,506
Both dumplings and noodles were great,

2537
01:35:12,573 --> 01:35:16,077
but Poong and Sam's dish today

2538
01:35:16,143 --> 01:35:18,279
was the best one I've had so far
since I joined.

2539
01:35:18,345 --> 01:35:19,980
-Really?
-Really.

2540
01:35:20,047 --> 01:35:22,216
It's so good. It's insane.

2541
01:35:22,283 --> 01:35:24,652
-Let me see.
-This is just crazy.

2542
01:35:25,853 --> 01:35:29,256
-Ho-young took the bowl.
-It's almost finished.

2543
01:35:29,323 --> 01:35:30,424
If they sold this at a restaurant,

2544
01:35:30,958 --> 01:35:32,693
-I'd go and eat it.
-Me too.

2545
01:35:32,760 --> 01:35:37,164
If he goes somewhere outside of Seoul
and opens a restaurant with this dish,

2546
01:35:37,698 --> 01:35:38,933
THE LAST SPURT

2547
01:35:38,999 --> 01:35:40,401
…I'd go and eat it there.

2548
01:35:40,468 --> 01:35:42,503
-You'd even travel?
-Yes.

2549
01:35:42,570 --> 01:35:44,939
If he gave orders
while making something like this, do it.

2550
01:35:45,005 --> 01:35:46,307
Stop showing your canine.

2551
01:35:48,242 --> 01:35:51,245
Both the dumpling
and the noodles were great too.

2552
01:35:51,312 --> 01:35:54,448
-The noodles were seasoned perfectly.
-Yes.

2553
01:35:54,515 --> 01:35:56,817
It wasn't too strong,
and it remained cold.

2554
01:35:56,884 --> 01:35:58,919
<i>The prickly ash kept popping in my mouth,</i>

2555
01:35:58,986 --> 01:36:01,088
<i>giving off its fragrance.</i>

2556
01:36:01,155 --> 01:36:03,891
It wasn't just simple cold noodles.

2557
01:36:03,958 --> 01:36:06,026
Something about it was fancy.

2558
01:36:06,093 --> 01:36:08,629
That's why I could keep eating it.

2559
01:36:08,929 --> 01:36:12,633
DAZED

2560
01:36:12,700 --> 01:36:13,768
The guest is asleep.

2561
01:36:14,168 --> 01:36:16,303
HIT WITH A BLOOD SUGAR SPIKE

2562
01:36:16,370 --> 01:36:17,638
Make your decision now.

2563
01:36:17,705 --> 01:36:19,406
-Oh, right.
-He's hit with a blood sugar spike.

2564
01:36:19,473 --> 01:36:21,275
-Yes, right. I have to choose.
-Pick one.

2565
01:36:21,342 --> 01:36:23,711
<i>Press one for Team Jong-won and Eun-yeong,</i>

2566
01:36:23,778 --> 01:36:26,213
<i>and two for Team Sam and Poong.</i>

2567
01:36:26,280 --> 01:36:29,216
You've all had it,
so you probably know how I feel.

2568
01:36:29,283 --> 01:36:30,851
-Yes.
-It's hard to pick.

2569
01:36:30,918 --> 01:36:33,854
"Pay Stub? Nonsense.
I'm Taking My Pay in Food."

2570
01:36:33,921 --> 01:36:35,356
It really could be
a substitute for the pay.

2571
01:36:35,422 --> 01:36:38,259
So Nam-no, you got paid in full today.

2572
01:36:38,325 --> 01:36:40,728
-He was overpaid.
-Right.

2573
01:36:40,795 --> 01:36:43,097
-Have you decided? Ten seconds.
-Ten seconds, please.

2574
01:36:44,398 --> 01:36:45,633
Five.

2575
01:36:45,699 --> 01:36:46,600
Four.

2576
01:36:46,667 --> 01:36:47,868
Three.

2577
01:36:47,935 --> 01:36:48,936
Two.

2578
01:36:49,003 --> 01:36:50,771
-One.
-It must be hard.

2579
01:36:51,672 --> 01:36:53,874
He chose one.

2580
01:36:53,941 --> 01:36:57,211
-It must've been hard.
-I'm so sorry.

2581
01:36:57,278 --> 01:37:00,781
Which team will win this round?

2582
01:37:00,848 --> 01:37:03,684
Let's find out who he chose. Show us!

2583
01:37:04,285 --> 01:37:06,787
Pay Stub? Nonsense.

2584
01:37:06,854 --> 01:37:08,489
-I'm Taking My Pay in Food.
-I'm Taking My Pay in Food.

2585
01:37:08,556 --> 01:37:09,790
Two new team combinations.

2586
01:37:09,857 --> 01:37:13,294
Sam and Poong
versus Jong-won and Eun-yeong.

2587
01:37:13,360 --> 01:37:15,996
Will Jong-won take another victory

2588
01:37:16,063 --> 01:37:18,165
after teaming up with Eun-yeong?

2589
01:37:18,232 --> 01:37:23,070
Or will Sam's fate change,
thanks to Poong's presence?

2590
01:37:23,137 --> 01:37:26,607
Which team did Nam-no choose?

2591
01:37:26,674 --> 01:37:27,741
Who won?

2592
01:37:28,742 --> 01:37:30,644
SON JONG-WON, PARK EUN-YEONG WINS

2593
01:37:30,878 --> 01:37:32,246
DUMPLING AND NOODLES WIN

2594
01:37:32,313 --> 01:37:35,583
Jong-won and Eun-yeong.

2595
01:37:36,183 --> 01:37:39,720
The huge dumpling and noodles.

2596
01:37:39,787 --> 01:37:41,288
Was there a special reason?

2597
01:37:41,355 --> 01:37:43,524
It was for a very personal reason.

2598
01:37:43,591 --> 01:37:47,127
<i>I love the mix</i>
<i>of cold noodles and hot dumplings.</i>

2599
01:37:47,194 --> 01:37:48,696
Yes, hot and cold.

2600
01:37:48,762 --> 01:37:51,732
-That mix.
-Also, it wasn't just cold.

2601
01:37:51,799 --> 01:37:55,669
<i>It had a prickly ash flavor</i>
<i>as well as the depth of </i>hapjajang<i>,</i>

2602
01:37:55,736 --> 01:37:57,438
<i>and it was perfectly cooked.</i>

2603
01:37:57,504 --> 01:38:00,808
So the moment I had a bite of the dumpling
after the cold noodles,

2604
01:38:01,475 --> 01:38:02,710
it tasted eightfold better.

2605
01:38:03,978 --> 01:38:09,350
Of course, the napa cabbage wrap with meat
was also delicious,

2606
01:38:09,416 --> 01:38:12,219
but I loved the dishes
with the temperature difference more.

2607
01:38:12,286 --> 01:38:14,054
This means

2608
01:38:14,121 --> 01:38:15,823
Ho-young wasn't at fault.

2609
01:38:16,056 --> 01:38:17,658
CAUGHT RED-HANDED(?)

2610
01:38:17,725 --> 01:38:19,460
So it seems the jinx is that

2611
01:38:19,526 --> 01:38:22,263
anyone who teams up with Sam loses.

2612
01:38:22,329 --> 01:38:23,931
-It looks like it.
-This is bad.

2613
01:38:23,998 --> 01:38:28,636
What a shame.
Poong, your dish was fantastic.

2614
01:38:28,702 --> 01:38:31,839
I had always disregarded him,
but I realized after working together

2615
01:38:31,906 --> 01:38:34,041
that he really has a profound philosophy.

2616
01:38:34,108 --> 01:38:36,243
-He has his own philosophy.
-I see.

2617
01:38:36,310 --> 01:38:38,545
So was this your fault?

2618
01:38:38,612 --> 01:38:40,681
-No, it wasn't.
-That's not it?

2619
01:38:41,916 --> 01:38:46,387
Anyhow, regardless of the result,
it was great to be here with everyone,

2620
01:38:46,453 --> 01:38:49,924
<i>sharing a hearty amount of food</i>
<i>among the cast.</i>

2621
01:38:49,990 --> 01:38:53,027
Viewers, I hope you also enjoy
lots of great food

2622
01:38:53,093 --> 01:38:55,930
as you enjoy your Chuseok holidays.

2623
01:38:55,996 --> 01:38:58,666
The winners are Jong-won and Eun-yeong!

2624
01:38:58,732 --> 01:39:00,034
Please put the stars on them.

2625
01:39:01,268 --> 01:39:02,569
That was Nam-no's choice.

2626
01:39:03,837 --> 01:39:06,140
Jong-won gets his 13th star,

2627
01:39:06,206 --> 01:39:08,776
-and Eun-yeong, the seventh.
-All right!

2628
01:39:08,842 --> 01:39:11,612
-Congratulations!
-Congratulations.

2629
01:39:11,679 --> 01:39:14,381
COMING UP: PREVIEW FOR
JOO SANG-UK & CHAE JUNG-AN'S EPISODE

2630
01:39:14,949 --> 01:39:16,951
-Take them outside.
<i>-He's a bit scary.</i>

2631
01:39:17,017 --> 01:39:18,819
-It's something he always had.
-Move quickly.

2632
01:39:18,886 --> 01:39:20,654
Do not rub Chairman Joo the wrong way.

2633
01:39:20,721 --> 01:39:21,622
That's scary.

2634
01:39:21,822 --> 01:39:23,457
CHEERS, EVERYONE!

2635
01:39:23,524 --> 01:39:24,992
He should've died back then.

2636
01:39:25,259 --> 01:39:26,560
ME?

2637
01:39:26,627 --> 01:39:28,729
Please welcome
actors Joo Sang-uk and Chae Jung-an!

2638
01:39:28,796 --> 01:39:32,132
He played the worst villain
on <i>Agent Kim Reactivated.</i>

2639
01:39:32,199 --> 01:39:33,701
You have that rich guy look.

2640
01:39:33,767 --> 01:39:34,935
DEFINITELY LOOKS RICH(?)

2641
01:39:35,202 --> 01:39:37,204
WHAT'S HIS HOBBY IN REAL LIFE?

2642
01:39:37,271 --> 01:39:40,107
That was 1 m and 10 cm. About 58 cm long.

2643
01:39:40,174 --> 01:39:41,709
-It was 1.5 kg.
-It's huge.

2644
01:39:41,942 --> 01:39:43,344
A PLEDGE FOR THE RATINGS?

2645
01:39:43,410 --> 01:39:45,946
I'll buy everyone a fridge
if it goes over 5%.

2646
01:39:46,013 --> 01:39:48,382
An overseas team vacation is on me
if it goes over 7%.

2647
01:39:50,150 --> 01:39:51,618
Be ready to lose an arm today.

2648
01:39:51,685 --> 01:39:52,553
A DESPERATE COOK-OFF

2649
01:39:52,753 --> 01:39:53,687
FOR AN OVERSEAS VACATION

2650
01:39:53,754 --> 01:39:55,022
This is how you do <i>mantecare.</i>

2651
01:39:55,089 --> 01:39:57,291
This is what you call
a perfect wine sauce.

2652
01:39:57,458 --> 01:39:58,592
READY FOR THE CHAIRMAN

2653
01:39:58,659 --> 01:40:00,260
Cooking is that easy.

2654
01:40:00,494 --> 01:40:01,762
THE CHAIRMAN LOOKS PLEASED

2655
01:40:01,962 --> 01:40:03,497
A PERSONALIZED DISH ROUND

2656
01:40:03,564 --> 01:40:05,299
JUST FOR CHAIRMAN JOO

2657
01:40:05,366 --> 01:40:07,301
It needs a bit more spiciness.

2658
01:40:07,368 --> 01:40:09,336
The chairman wants something spicy!

2659
01:40:09,403 --> 01:40:10,771
Humor his appetite!

2660
01:40:11,005 --> 01:40:11,872
Soju…

2661
01:40:11,939 --> 01:40:12,840
Mr. Jung, soju!

2662
01:40:12,906 --> 01:40:14,675
-Soju!
-Are you out of your mind?

2663
01:40:14,742 --> 01:40:17,578
Hurry up, Mr. Poong.
What do you think you're doing?

